536
00:21:27,420 --> 00:21:29,720
I'm telling you this only because
I believe we're on the same team.

537
00:21:29,720 --> 00:21:30,920
We have the final code.

538
00:21:30,920 --> 00:21:31,960
- You do?
- Yes.

539
00:21:31,960 --> 00:21:33,490
We're not certain,

540
00:21:33,490 --> 00:21:34,730
but we came up with an answer.

541
00:21:34,730 --> 00:21:36,600
We had one more theory.

542
00:21:36,600 --> 00:21:38,270
He keeps bringing up the war,

543
00:21:38,270 --> 00:21:41,470
- so we suspect he's related to the war.
- Exactly.

544
00:21:41,470 --> 00:21:42,970
That's so suspicious to me.

545
00:21:42,970 --> 00:21:44,440
- I think he takes the war expenses.
- I believe so.

546
00:21:44,440 --> 00:21:47,040
I feel like...

547
00:21:47,040 --> 00:21:48,110
he knows...

548
00:21:48,110 --> 00:21:51,210
that it's advantageous to him
while it's a loss for us.

549
00:21:51,210 --> 00:21:53,580
- I think this is his last resort.
- Yes.

550
00:21:53,580 --> 00:21:56,380
When things don't work out,
he tries to instigate wars.

551
00:21:56,380 --> 00:21:59,750
(The residents are convinced
about who Vector is.)

552
00:21:59,990 --> 00:22:02,860
First off, what's your conclusion?

553
00:22:02,860 --> 00:22:05,090
Team Blue has to check
the remaining life supply...

554
00:22:05,090 --> 00:22:06,490
- and has the best efficiency.
- Yes.

555
00:22:06,490 --> 00:22:09,200
She uses one, we use one, and they rest.

556
00:22:09,200 --> 00:22:10,300
Team White rests.

557
00:22:10,300 --> 00:22:11,430
- White?
- Their efficiency is low.

558
00:22:11,430 --> 00:22:12,870
- We...
- So, Team White rests.

559
00:22:12,870 --> 00:22:14,630
- Yes. Make your bids.
- Okay, then.

560
00:22:14,630 --> 00:22:16,440
- Team White, while you rest,
- Yes.

561
00:22:16,440 --> 00:22:17,970
- check on what Black is doing.
- Okay.

562
00:22:17,970 --> 00:22:21,370
We feel like he's a weapon dealer.

563
00:22:21,370 --> 00:22:23,510
One of our theories was...

564
00:22:23,510 --> 00:22:26,410
that he might be taking the prize
that was deducted due to the war.

565
00:22:26,410 --> 00:22:28,210
That could be why he keeps leading us
into it.

566
00:22:28,210 --> 00:22:29,780
I had been thinking that from the get-go.

567
00:22:31,080 --> 00:22:32,920
Okay, then. I should go and make a bid.

568
00:22:32,920 --> 00:22:34,150
- Right.
- I'll see you soon.

569
00:22:34,150 --> 00:22:36,290
- Careful.
- We'll go to Black.

570
00:22:36,290 --> 00:22:37,790
We'll go and talk to him.

571
00:22:37,790 --> 00:22:38,990
- Blue.
- Yes?

572
00:22:38,990 --> 00:22:40,890
- Don't be nervous. No pressure.
- Good luck.

573
00:22:40,890 --> 00:22:42,530
You're only checking the life supply.

574
00:22:42,530 --> 00:22:43,660
- Okay.
- Yes.

575
00:22:43,660 --> 00:22:46,370
If you would like to make a bid
for a production site,

576
00:22:46,370 --> 00:22:47,430
state your team name...

577
00:22:47,930 --> 00:22:51,140
and place a credit in the central box.

578
00:22:51,140 --> 00:22:52,640
This is Team Blue.

579
00:22:53,040 --> 00:22:54,570
(Team Blue bids 1 credit.)

580
00:22:54,570 --> 00:22:55,910
- Yes.
- It's Team Red.

581
00:22:55,910 --> 00:22:57,040
(Team Red bids 1 credit.)

582
00:22:57,180 --> 00:22:58,710
It's Team Gold.

583
00:23:00,710 --> 00:23:03,580
The production site bid has been closed.

584
00:23:03,850 --> 00:23:07,220
Team Blue, Team Red, and Team Gold...

585
00:23:07,490 --> 00:23:09,560
have been assigned a production site.

586
00:23:10,660 --> 00:23:13,490
Day six's production activity has begun.

587
00:23:14,860 --> 00:23:17,430
- Welcome to the production site.
- Let's do it.

588
00:23:17,800 --> 00:23:19,330
This is our first-ever production.

589
00:23:19,330 --> 00:23:22,040
If Team Gold chooses to produce credits,

590
00:23:22,040 --> 00:23:25,340
you get 1 credit for 1 correct answer.

591
00:23:25,340 --> 00:23:28,040
If Team Gold chooses to produce lives,

592
00:23:28,040 --> 00:23:30,980
you get 1 life for 3 correct answers.

593
00:23:30,980 --> 00:23:33,110
If you answer all ten questions correctly,

594
00:23:33,110 --> 00:23:35,480
you will get an extra five lives.

595
00:23:35,480 --> 00:23:38,050
One difference from Team White is...

596
00:23:38,050 --> 00:23:41,090
that they had the same efficiency
for both lives and credits.

597
00:23:41,090 --> 00:23:43,290
We have better credit production, though.

598
00:23:43,290 --> 00:23:45,690
But if we're going to team up
with Team Red,

599
00:23:45,690 --> 00:23:47,460
we have no reason to produce credits,

600
00:23:47,460 --> 00:23:49,260
- Right.
- so it's the same.

601
00:23:49,260 --> 00:23:51,060
- Lives.
- We'll produce lives.

602
00:23:51,500 --> 00:23:52,570
Credits.

603
00:23:52,800 --> 00:23:54,670
I'll produce lives.

604
00:23:54,670 --> 00:23:57,970
Please insert one credit
into the credit box.

605
00:23:58,200 --> 00:23:59,510
It's begun.

606
00:23:59,510 --> 00:24:01,140
Currently,

607
00:24:01,140 --> 00:24:04,240
there are 21 lives in the life supply.

608
00:24:04,240 --> 00:24:06,480
The keyword
for today's production activity is...

609
00:24:06,650 --> 00:24:09,050
"Every Order in the World."

610
00:24:09,050 --> 00:24:10,680
- It could be a historic order.
- Right.

611
00:24:10,680 --> 00:24:11,950
- Like a chronological table.
- Yes.

612
00:24:11,950 --> 00:24:13,290
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

613
00:24:13,290 --> 00:24:14,320
Let's get all of them.

614
00:24:14,320 --> 00:24:16,620
- I want to get more than Team Gold.
- Okay.

615
00:24:16,690 --> 00:24:19,160
- I'm nervous.
- Here's the first question.

616
00:24:19,160 --> 00:24:20,190
It's going to be so fun.

617
00:24:20,190 --> 00:24:22,100
Number one, "The Great Gatsby."

618
00:24:22,100 --> 00:24:23,560
- That's Machiavelli's.
- Two, Machiavelli.

619
00:24:23,560 --> 00:24:25,570
- Three, "Heartless," a Korean novel.
- "Heartless."

620
00:24:25,570 --> 00:24:27,400
- "Hamlet?"
- And George Orwell.

621
00:24:27,400 --> 00:24:28,770
- Is that "1984?"
- Yes.

622
00:24:28,770 --> 00:24:31,170
He couldn't have written that in 1984.

623
00:24:31,170 --> 00:24:32,710
What should we do with this?

624
00:24:32,710 --> 00:24:33,770
This one's tricky.

625
00:24:34,340 --> 00:24:35,980
- It's really tough today.
- Yes.

626
00:24:35,980 --> 00:24:38,810
It's probably
the first-ever modern Korean novel.

627
00:24:38,810 --> 00:24:40,110
Machiavelli was way before.

628
00:24:40,110 --> 00:24:41,350
- Right.
- Way before.

629
00:24:41,350 --> 00:24:43,680
- That is correct.
- Correct!

630
00:24:43,680 --> 00:24:46,320
("The Prince," "Hamlet," "Heartless,"
"The Great Gatsby," and "1984")

631
00:24:46,320 --> 00:24:47,950
- Well done.
- Yes!

632
00:24:48,460 --> 00:24:50,120
Let's surprise the world...

633
00:24:50,120 --> 00:24:51,390
- by guessing more correctly.
- Great.

634
00:24:51,390 --> 00:24:52,630
- We'll surprise them.
- Let's do it.

635
00:24:52,790 --> 00:24:54,490
- Here's the next question.
- What's this?

636
00:24:54,490 --> 00:24:56,230
- I'm good at this stuff.
- I might be able to do this.

637
00:24:56,230 --> 00:24:59,270
- This is our field.
- This is all I ever think about.

638
00:24:59,270 --> 00:25:01,200
- How to accumulate wealth.
- We might do it.

639
00:25:01,200 --> 00:25:04,470
The third one, Arnault, is struggling
these days, apparently.

640
00:25:04,470 --> 00:25:06,210
Isn't Amazon also struggling?

641
00:25:07,470 --> 00:25:09,980
You said, "Struggle."
Are we concerned for them?

642
00:25:09,980 --> 00:25:11,780
Musk is a big shot now.

643
00:25:11,780 --> 00:25:13,480
Oh, they're struggling. I feel so bad.

644
00:25:13,480 --> 00:25:15,880
That was hilarious.
We were like, "They're struggling."

645
00:25:16,120 --> 00:25:18,690
- Elon Musk has to be the richest.
- Absolutely.

646
00:25:18,690 --> 00:25:21,320
- Musk, Bezos, Zuckerberg, and Arnault.
- Okay.

647
00:25:21,720 --> 00:25:23,260
- We believe in you.
- This is irrefutable.

648
00:25:23,260 --> 00:25:24,460
That is correct.

649
00:25:24,490 --> 00:25:26,530
That was an easy one.

650
00:25:26,890 --> 00:25:29,230
Here's our answer. Three, one, five.

651
00:25:29,230 --> 00:25:30,430
- That is correct.
- Yes!

652
00:25:30,430 --> 00:25:31,530
(Correct)

653
00:25:31,870 --> 00:25:33,470
Eight, five, three.

654
00:25:33,700 --> 00:25:35,070
That is correct.

655
00:25:35,870 --> 00:25:37,000
We're pretty lucky.

656
00:25:37,000 --> 00:25:38,370
- How did you do that?
- Lucky guess.

657
00:25:38,370 --> 00:25:40,040
(Team Red gets 3 correct answers
in a row.)

658
00:25:41,410 --> 00:25:43,740
What are those? This looks interesting.

659
00:25:43,810 --> 00:25:46,080
Who's higher between the Minister of War
and the Left State Councilor?

660
00:25:46,080 --> 00:25:47,310
- Left State Councilor.
- Left State Councilor.

661
00:25:47,310 --> 00:25:49,120
It says, "Left State Councilor,"
in Chinese here.

662
00:25:49,120 --> 00:25:50,380
No way.

663
00:25:50,380 --> 00:25:51,380
Where is it?

664
00:25:51,380 --> 00:25:52,950
- That could have been bad.
- Chinese? Awesome.

665
00:25:54,920 --> 00:25:56,090
That is correct.

666
00:25:57,490 --> 00:25:58,930
What would be the last one?

667
00:25:59,530 --> 00:26:00,730
What's the difference?

668
00:26:01,130 --> 00:26:03,400
One, D, A, F, two.

669
00:26:03,400 --> 00:26:04,660
That is incorrect.

670
00:26:04,660 --> 00:26:05,670
(Incorrect)

671
00:26:05,670 --> 00:26:06,900
I'll use a credit...

672
00:26:06,900 --> 00:26:08,200
for a retry.

673
00:26:08,200 --> 00:26:09,240
That is incorrect.

674
00:26:09,240 --> 00:26:10,370
I'll retry.

675
00:26:10,370 --> 00:26:11,570
That is correct.

676
00:26:13,240 --> 00:26:15,480
They told me to win at least one,

677
00:26:15,480 --> 00:26:16,640
so I can use all the credits.

678
00:26:16,740 --> 00:26:18,180
We'll try again.

679
00:26:18,580 --> 00:26:19,850
That is correct.

680
00:26:19,850 --> 00:26:21,310
Good. We had no alternative.

681
00:26:21,550 --> 00:26:22,750
We'll try again.

682
00:26:23,950 --> 00:26:25,220
We'll try again.

683
00:26:25,220 --> 00:26:26,320
We wasted so many.

684
00:26:27,290 --> 00:26:29,890
- That is correct.
- It was a tank.

685
00:26:29,990 --> 00:26:33,290
Blue could get these answers
with some credits.

686
00:26:33,290 --> 00:26:34,290
Definitely.

687
00:26:34,290 --> 00:26:35,560
I used too many.

688
00:26:35,900 --> 00:26:37,200
I'll retry.

689
00:26:38,030 --> 00:26:39,030
(Laughing)

690
00:26:39,030 --> 00:26:40,270
I must use them.

691
00:26:40,430 --> 00:26:42,140
It's fun now that I'm alone.

692
00:26:42,640 --> 00:26:44,770
Two, four, three, one, five.

693
00:26:44,770 --> 00:26:45,970
That is correct.

694
00:26:47,010 --> 00:26:48,170
I won two.

695
00:26:48,410 --> 00:26:50,480
I can be a little smug now.

696
00:26:50,610 --> 00:26:53,110
The questions are so fun.

697
00:26:53,110 --> 00:26:54,810
I wish I could do this all day.

698
00:26:55,820 --> 00:26:57,020
It makes no sense.

699
00:26:57,020 --> 00:26:59,050
We let him trick us that way
so many times.

700
00:26:59,050 --> 00:27:01,120
I think there's a chance
that he's behind all of it.

701
00:27:01,120 --> 00:27:02,990
He has to be. I'm certain.

702
00:27:02,990 --> 00:27:04,920
- Right.
- But we need to find evidence.

703
00:27:06,730 --> 00:27:07,990
Hello?

704
00:27:09,100 --> 00:27:10,500
Anybody here?

705
00:27:14,130 --> 00:27:15,470
He went somewhere.

706
00:27:16,200 --> 00:27:17,370
Black, are you here?

707
00:27:18,740 --> 00:27:21,470
Are you producing or what? Production...

708
00:27:32,550 --> 00:27:33,590
No.

709
00:27:34,190 --> 00:27:35,460
I don't think he's here.

710
00:27:35,460 --> 00:27:36,720
What?

711
00:27:36,920 --> 00:27:38,630
Were you in a production activity?

712
00:27:38,630 --> 00:27:39,960
Were you producing?

713
00:27:39,960 --> 00:27:41,890
No, I was just resting.

714
00:27:41,890 --> 00:27:43,000
You're not producing today?

715
00:27:43,300 --> 00:27:45,470
I didn't get any instructions today.

716
00:27:45,470 --> 00:27:46,700
No instructions.

717
00:27:47,200 --> 00:27:48,840
There was a bid,

718
00:27:48,840 --> 00:27:50,540
so a team didn't have to produce.

719
00:27:50,540 --> 00:27:51,770
I had no idea.

720
00:27:51,770 --> 00:27:53,270
I couldn't get anything done...

721
00:27:53,270 --> 00:27:55,170
because I was busy organizing things,

722
00:27:55,170 --> 00:27:56,540
and Team White walked in.

723
00:27:56,780 --> 00:27:58,580
I physically opened it a bit.

724
00:27:58,580 --> 00:28:02,150
And he was hiding there.

725
00:28:02,150 --> 00:28:03,250
I thought,

726
00:28:03,250 --> 00:28:04,420
"What's this guy doing?"

727
00:28:04,950 --> 00:28:06,350
- What were you doing?
- What?

728
00:28:06,350 --> 00:28:09,260
- What were you doing?
- I was thinking about what to do.

729
00:28:09,260 --> 00:28:11,060
- I see.
- Listen.

730
00:28:11,060 --> 00:28:12,860
- We had two concerns.
- Okay.

731
00:28:12,890 --> 00:28:15,030
- It's WWE.
- What does that mean?

732
00:28:15,360 --> 00:28:17,300
I pretended to be worried.

733
00:28:17,300 --> 00:28:19,130
"We're afraid of Team Gold."

734
00:28:19,130 --> 00:28:21,770
"What if we made the war weird..."

735
00:28:21,770 --> 00:28:25,100
"to stop Team Gold
from even participating?"

736
00:28:25,100 --> 00:28:26,410
That's what I asked him.

737
00:28:26,710 --> 00:28:28,640
And his response...

738
00:28:28,640 --> 00:28:30,880
was very suspicious.

739
00:28:30,880 --> 00:28:32,710
He started pondering hard.

740
00:28:33,050 --> 00:28:34,280
That could be a solution.

741
00:28:35,050 --> 00:28:37,650
I think we can go that way.

742
00:28:37,650 --> 00:28:39,350
Team Blue came to us, right?

743
00:28:39,520 --> 00:28:40,920
So, I...

744
00:28:41,350 --> 00:28:43,660
The number of residents means
nothing to him.

745
00:28:43,660 --> 00:28:45,760
What's Black's clear goal?

746
00:28:45,760 --> 00:28:48,030
Maillard is very suspicious of you.

747
00:28:48,030 --> 00:28:51,400
We really need this for the community.

748
00:28:53,200 --> 00:28:55,300
And tell them to get it back through aid.

749
00:28:55,300 --> 00:28:56,770
If that happens,

750
00:28:56,770 --> 00:28:58,940
we'll be doomed
without even being able to start a war.

751
00:29:01,940 --> 00:29:03,540
There is a better solution.

752
00:29:05,310 --> 00:29:06,480
What is it?

753
00:29:09,580 --> 00:29:10,880
(Thinking)

754
00:29:10,880 --> 00:29:12,850
I was going to tell you today.

755
00:29:15,760 --> 00:29:16,890
- I'm actually...
- Yes.

756
00:29:20,360 --> 00:29:22,460
The weapon sales revenue is my prize.

757
00:29:23,960 --> 00:29:25,030
This is insane.

758
00:29:25,470 --> 00:29:27,370
I get to set the weapon prices.

759
00:29:28,330 --> 00:29:31,770
I was 90 percent sure.

760
00:29:31,770 --> 00:29:33,410
That wasn't that surprising.

761
00:29:33,410 --> 00:29:36,610
I thought he was creating confusion
by disclosing his secret.

762
00:29:36,740 --> 00:29:39,580
Vector was really smart.

763
00:29:39,580 --> 00:29:42,080
He realized that we had figured it out.

764
00:29:42,320 --> 00:29:45,050
So he revealed it to us.

765
00:29:45,620 --> 00:29:48,620
I have no reason to take any more now.

766
00:29:48,990 --> 00:29:52,690
- You already won 100,000 dollars.
- I already won that amount.

767
00:29:53,430 --> 00:29:54,660
Also,

768
00:29:54,660 --> 00:29:57,000
I don't care
whether diamonds or gold wins.

769
00:29:57,100 --> 00:29:59,230
But if I had to choose...

770
00:29:59,270 --> 00:30:01,030
- You'd rather see someone you know win.
- That's right.

771
00:30:01,030 --> 00:30:03,200
So, honestly, I wanted
to give you even a single vote...

772
00:30:03,240 --> 00:30:05,840
and build trust with White...

773
00:30:05,840 --> 00:30:08,110
by sharing information.

774
00:30:09,510 --> 00:30:10,910
I also felt sorry.

775
00:30:10,910 --> 00:30:12,680
It was my mission,

776
00:30:12,680 --> 00:30:14,750
- so I couldn't help it.
- Of course.

777
00:30:14,880 --> 00:30:16,580
I'll promise you this.

778
00:30:16,820 --> 00:30:18,850
I'll set the price of the weapons at zero.

779
00:30:18,950 --> 00:30:21,290
When the time comes
when you run out of lives,

780
00:30:21,320 --> 00:30:22,460
attack Team Gold.

781
00:30:22,890 --> 00:30:24,560
That's the only way.

782
00:30:25,220 --> 00:30:27,730
I revealed it because I thought...

783
00:30:27,730 --> 00:30:30,200
Team White and I had the same interests.

784
00:30:30,200 --> 00:30:31,730
I really trusted them.

785
00:30:31,730 --> 00:30:33,470
If they did that, they wouldn't lose.

786
00:30:33,500 --> 00:30:36,840
I thought I told them something
they could understand.

787
00:30:36,940 --> 00:30:38,740
I'm just telling you how to start a war...

788
00:30:39,010 --> 00:30:42,410
- without deducting the prize money.
- Right.

789
00:30:42,510 --> 00:30:45,680
What I did so far may have upset you,

790
00:30:45,850 --> 00:30:47,750
but I've come to you offering help.

791
00:30:47,750 --> 00:30:50,480
Honestly, I don't think
there's any reason not to trust me.

792
00:30:51,450 --> 00:30:53,990
All right. But I think
I'll have to share the updates.

793
00:30:53,990 --> 00:30:55,960
- With Leia.
- Sure, you can talk about it.

794
00:30:55,960 --> 00:30:58,290
You can head back first.

795
00:30:58,290 --> 00:31:00,730
- I'll talk with Black a bit more.
- You will? Let's go together.

796
00:31:00,730 --> 00:31:02,030
- You can head back first.
- Let's go together.

797
00:31:02,030 --> 00:31:03,230
Head back first.

798
00:31:04,060 --> 00:31:06,230
From my perspective,
I thought that, with Siseon around,

799
00:31:06,230 --> 00:31:09,300
we wouldn't be able to figure out
what his true intention was.

800
00:31:09,300 --> 00:31:11,270
Vector was the kind of person who,

801
00:31:11,270 --> 00:31:13,540
the more you try to reason
and empathize with him,

802
00:31:13,540 --> 00:31:15,440
the more he gets into your head.

803
00:31:15,440 --> 00:31:17,140
He was a snake.

804
00:31:17,140 --> 00:31:18,380
He talks too well.

805
00:31:18,380 --> 00:31:20,410
There were many times
when I almost fell for it,

806
00:31:20,410 --> 00:31:22,480
so I thought we shouldn't talk together.

807
00:31:22,750 --> 00:31:24,420
That's why I sent Siseon back.

808
00:31:25,380 --> 00:31:27,020
Personally, I think...

809
00:31:27,150 --> 00:31:29,620
when Team Red finds out about this...

810
00:31:29,960 --> 00:31:31,690
Team Red probably knows already.

811
00:31:31,790 --> 00:31:33,890
I saw them talking to Team Gold today,

812
00:31:34,160 --> 00:31:36,200
and I just told you this...

813
00:31:36,200 --> 00:31:37,900
- The justification...
- assuming they already know.

814
00:31:38,300 --> 00:31:40,870
They care about having a justification.

815
00:31:40,900 --> 00:31:43,140
I really want Team White,

816
00:31:43,140 --> 00:31:44,900
Team Blue, and Team Red to win.

817
00:31:45,710 --> 00:31:47,140
I feel sorry.

818
00:31:47,640 --> 00:31:50,180
I sat there like Maillard's kid.

819
00:31:50,180 --> 00:31:53,450
There's something intimidating
about Maillard...

820
00:31:53,450 --> 00:31:54,810
when he just stares blankly
and listens like that.

821
00:31:54,810 --> 00:31:56,420
"What is he thinking about?"

822
00:31:57,350 --> 00:31:59,950
"Is he normal?"
That was the impression I got.

823
00:32:00,090 --> 00:32:01,650
So I copied that.

824
00:32:05,630 --> 00:32:08,460
Why did you deposit lives to Team Blue...

825
00:32:08,460 --> 00:32:09,960
and not tell us?

826
00:32:10,260 --> 00:32:11,460
That's...

827
00:32:12,270 --> 00:32:14,330
because I had to start a war...

828
00:32:14,330 --> 00:32:15,570
at least once.

829
00:32:16,140 --> 00:32:18,070
Team Blue asked me.

830
00:32:18,300 --> 00:32:20,240
It worked.

831
00:32:20,270 --> 00:32:22,410
He kept falling into the empty trap I set,

832
00:32:22,410 --> 00:32:24,680
trying to fill the spaces,

833
00:32:24,680 --> 00:32:26,310
and ended up...

834
00:32:26,310 --> 00:32:27,610
letting things slip.

835
00:32:28,310 --> 00:32:30,220
I don't think saying sorry...

836
00:32:30,220 --> 00:32:32,590
will be enough to convince Team Red today.

837
00:32:32,590 --> 00:32:35,050
You should think of a plan for that.

838
00:32:35,150 --> 00:32:36,790
I have one way.

839
00:32:37,220 --> 00:32:38,290
What is that?

840
00:32:39,560 --> 00:32:41,560
I have an ally on Team Red.

841
00:32:46,270 --> 00:32:47,500
Who? Donkey?

842
00:32:47,500 --> 00:32:48,530
Yes.

843
00:32:48,570 --> 00:32:50,600
He will share the prize money with me.

844
00:32:51,540 --> 00:32:52,770
- A spy?
- Yes.

845
00:32:53,440 --> 00:32:54,640
Well...

846
00:32:55,470 --> 00:32:58,040
Donkey has built a strong level
of trust with them,

847
00:32:58,110 --> 00:33:01,580
so I tried to ask Donkey
to make Team Red...

848
00:33:01,580 --> 00:33:02,780
join this side.

849
00:33:02,950 --> 00:33:06,020
But since Donkey is at the bottom
of the hierarchy,

850
00:33:06,020 --> 00:33:09,360
I need to convince Maillard and Izaha.

851
00:33:11,290 --> 00:33:14,330
The production activity
for Day Six has ended.

852
00:33:14,330 --> 00:33:17,260
Out of 10 questions,
you got 5 questions right.

853
00:33:17,260 --> 00:33:18,260
We got five right.

854
00:33:18,260 --> 00:33:20,530
If we had answered 1 more,
we would have had 2 lives.

855
00:33:20,530 --> 00:33:22,500
If we had more credits,

856
00:33:22,500 --> 00:33:25,570
- we could have gotten six right.
- That's right.

857
00:33:25,870 --> 00:33:27,870
If I had more credits...

858
00:33:27,910 --> 00:33:29,810
If I had more credits,

859
00:33:30,110 --> 00:33:31,740
I could have answered more.

860
00:33:32,210 --> 00:33:33,410
- Okay.
- Okay.

861
00:33:33,410 --> 00:33:34,580
- Nine is good.
- I'm satisfied.

862
00:33:34,580 --> 00:33:36,650
We're pretty productive.

863
00:33:36,650 --> 00:33:38,720
We spent a lot of credits,
but we did well.

864
00:33:38,820 --> 00:33:40,750
They were questions
that made us realize...

865
00:33:40,750 --> 00:33:43,020
we really need credits.

866
00:33:43,720 --> 00:33:45,560
We'll get pollution-free credits.

867
00:33:46,060 --> 00:33:47,130
Yes!

868
00:33:47,130 --> 00:33:48,630
Four, yes!

869
00:33:48,860 --> 00:33:50,060
It's here.

870
00:33:50,060 --> 00:33:51,760
Thank you.

871
00:33:51,860 --> 00:33:53,070
(Resources After Day 6's Production
Lost the bid for the production site)

872
00:33:53,070 --> 00:33:54,930
(Team Red: 298 diamonds, 9 lives,
12 credits, 0 gold pieces)

873
00:33:54,930 --> 00:33:56,870
(Team Blue: 100 diamonds, 0 lives,
0 credits, 0 gold pieces)

874
00:33:56,870 --> 00:33:58,800
(Team Gold: 0 diamonds, 20 lives,
0 credits, 200 gold pieces)

875
00:33:59,010 --> 00:34:01,240
(Team Red: 298 diamonds, 9 lives,
30 pollution-free credits, 0 gold pieces)

876
00:34:05,280 --> 00:34:07,580
(Team White: 201 diamonds, 3 lives,
12 credits, 0 gold pieces)

877
00:34:07,650 --> 00:34:09,520
They're in front of our house.

878
00:34:09,550 --> 00:34:11,120
- It's Team White, right?
- Yes.

879
00:34:11,680 --> 00:34:13,690
Why are you occupying our place?

880
00:34:13,690 --> 00:34:15,190
Why are you here?

881
00:34:15,320 --> 00:34:17,520
- Black...
- Black...

882
00:34:17,520 --> 00:34:18,690
was a weapon dealer.

883
00:34:18,690 --> 00:34:20,490
- That's right.
- That's true.

884
00:34:21,290 --> 00:34:22,360
Why are you occupying this place?

885
00:34:22,360 --> 00:34:23,900
- Why are you guarding it?
- To have a talk.

886
00:34:23,900 --> 00:34:25,870
Did you produce
many pollution-free credits?

887
00:34:25,870 --> 00:34:27,130
We got nine answers right.

888
00:34:27,130 --> 00:34:28,200
They got a lot.

889
00:34:28,200 --> 00:34:29,670
- That's amazing.
- We might have...

890
00:34:29,670 --> 00:34:30,740
a little showdown with Team Gold.

891
00:34:30,740 --> 00:34:32,200
- Did you get any right?
- How many did you get right?

892
00:34:32,200 --> 00:34:33,270
Four.

893
00:34:33,270 --> 00:34:34,540
Great job.

894
00:34:34,540 --> 00:34:36,010
That's great.
How many credits did you use?

895
00:34:36,010 --> 00:34:37,510
- I used them all.
- Nice.

896
00:34:37,580 --> 00:34:39,650
I wanted to tell you to do that.

897
00:34:39,650 --> 00:34:40,980
To get as many as you can
even if you have to spend all the credits.

898
00:34:40,980 --> 00:34:42,150
I heard the questions were okay.

899
00:34:42,150 --> 00:34:44,680
They were doable today
if you had enough credits.

900
00:34:44,680 --> 00:34:45,920
- Nice.
- Well done.

901
00:34:45,920 --> 00:34:48,190
Then shall we talk...

902
00:34:48,190 --> 00:34:50,620
- based on the information we have now?
- Okay.

903
00:34:50,720 --> 00:34:52,060
Our predictions were right.

904
00:34:52,060 --> 00:34:53,930
He's a weapon dealer,
and he took 100,000 dollars.

905
00:34:53,930 --> 00:34:56,130
Also, the weapon dealer
can adjust the price.

906
00:34:56,200 --> 00:34:58,130
- He can adjust the weapon prices.
- He can adjust the weapon prices.

907
00:34:58,130 --> 00:34:59,800
So he made us spend 100,000 dollars.

908
00:34:59,800 --> 00:35:02,130
He was the one who set
those insanely high weapon prices.

909
00:35:02,500 --> 00:35:04,040
Black was ready to show his cards...

910
00:35:04,040 --> 00:35:05,670
to everyone.

911
00:35:05,910 --> 00:35:07,440
So you're saying Black...

912
00:35:07,440 --> 00:35:09,380
revealed that he took 100,000 dollars.

913
00:35:09,380 --> 00:35:10,780
He revealed that he took it.

914
00:35:10,780 --> 00:35:12,580
- But it's...
- How did he reveal it?

915
00:35:12,580 --> 00:35:14,950
- Since he was already under suspicion,
- He realized...

916
00:35:14,950 --> 00:35:17,450
he decided to reveal his identity...

917
00:35:17,450 --> 00:35:18,950
and try to win us over.

918
00:35:23,190 --> 00:35:24,860
He'll let us buy the weapons
at a lower price...

919
00:35:24,860 --> 00:35:27,630
and fight a more advantageous war?

920
00:35:27,630 --> 00:35:29,130
Yes. He says he'll do that.

921
00:35:29,130 --> 00:35:31,560
But I don't think the prize money
of 100,000 dollars he took...

922
00:35:31,560 --> 00:35:32,730
is a fixed amount.

923
00:35:32,730 --> 00:35:34,200
I don't think it's a fixed amount.

924
00:35:34,200 --> 00:35:35,530
- That's why...
- It wouldn't be fixed.

925
00:35:35,530 --> 00:35:36,940
- It's too advantageous for him.
- He would have too little risk.

926
00:35:36,940 --> 00:35:38,740
In that case, he could just
lock his door and sleep.

927
00:35:38,740 --> 00:35:39,740
That's right.

928
00:35:39,740 --> 00:35:41,670
So I asked him to show me the card.

929
00:35:41,670 --> 00:35:43,780
It would have the conditions written down.

930
00:35:43,780 --> 00:35:45,280
So I asked him to show me the rules.

931
00:35:45,280 --> 00:35:47,410
He said he couldn't show me.

932
00:35:47,410 --> 00:35:49,150
I think he was bluffing.

933
00:35:49,150 --> 00:35:51,150
That means there's a condition
for taking him down,

934
00:35:51,150 --> 00:35:52,550
but we don't know that yet.

935
00:35:52,650 --> 00:35:53,750
It's just...

936
00:35:53,750 --> 00:35:56,020
Let's gather all the information and see.

937
00:35:56,020 --> 00:35:57,190
- Yes.
- Let's do that.

938
00:35:57,190 --> 00:35:58,420
- Okay.
- Let's go.

939
00:35:58,420 --> 00:35:59,730
See you later.

940
00:35:59,730 --> 00:36:01,230
- See you.
- See you.

941
00:36:03,260 --> 00:36:05,030
Why is he showing us all his cards now?

942
00:36:05,030 --> 00:36:06,200
Exactly.

943
00:36:06,200 --> 00:36:07,430
We already knew it, though.

944
00:36:08,000 --> 00:36:10,870
Why is he acting like he's being chased?

945
00:36:10,870 --> 00:36:12,070
Is he being chased?

946
00:36:12,300 --> 00:36:13,810
(Exclaiming)

947
00:36:13,810 --> 00:36:15,070
This is annoying.

948
00:36:15,210 --> 00:36:17,580
There are more things to think about now.

949
00:36:17,580 --> 00:36:18,980
Why are things so complicated?

950
00:36:19,410 --> 00:36:20,710
He's a weapon dealer?

951
00:36:22,110 --> 00:36:23,650
This is exhausting.

952
00:36:27,750 --> 00:36:29,020
It was complicated.

953
00:36:29,020 --> 00:36:30,290
I felt dizzy.

954
00:36:30,820 --> 00:36:34,430
When I got to know that
he'd told Team White first,

955
00:36:34,590 --> 00:36:35,960
I wondered,

956
00:36:35,960 --> 00:36:37,400
"Why did he tell them that?"

957
00:36:37,400 --> 00:36:38,860
"How am I..."

958
00:36:39,170 --> 00:36:41,170
"going to survive?"

959
00:36:41,170 --> 00:36:43,640
That's what I thought.

960
00:36:46,170 --> 00:36:48,270
Do you think...

961
00:36:49,110 --> 00:36:50,380
you can trust what I say from now on?

962
00:36:52,910 --> 00:36:54,010
What is it?

963
00:36:55,380 --> 00:36:56,980
I want you to be the only one
who knows this.

964
00:36:57,480 --> 00:36:59,190
I don't want anyone else to know.

965
00:37:03,520 --> 00:37:04,820
I'm...

966
00:37:04,820 --> 00:37:06,460
Black's ally.

967
00:37:09,230 --> 00:37:10,500
What kind of ally?

968
00:37:11,400 --> 00:37:14,330
If I help Black sell lots of weapons,

969
00:37:14,330 --> 00:37:15,530
I can get a share...

970
00:37:15,530 --> 00:37:17,500
of the prize.

971
00:37:18,040 --> 00:37:20,210
Personally,

972
00:37:20,610 --> 00:37:23,080
I wanted to make
Team Red and Black win together.

973
00:37:28,450 --> 00:37:29,920
But why...

974
00:37:30,180 --> 00:37:31,920
are you telling me?

975
00:37:49,200 --> 00:37:50,400
Why all of a sudden?

976
00:37:50,640 --> 00:37:52,540
Are you worried I might join forces
with Team Gold?

977
00:37:52,540 --> 00:37:54,340
No. It's because...

978
00:37:55,210 --> 00:37:56,680
I didn't think...

979
00:37:56,680 --> 00:37:59,140
Black would tell others
that he's the weapon dealer.

980
00:37:59,880 --> 00:38:01,110
Why would he say that?

981
00:38:01,110 --> 00:38:02,920
Since he said it himself,

982
00:38:02,920 --> 00:38:05,480
I have nothing more to do as his ally.

983
00:38:05,480 --> 00:38:07,650
That's why I'm telling you now.

984
00:38:08,650 --> 00:38:11,320
The card I have...

985
00:38:11,560 --> 00:38:14,130
is the strong trust
I've built with Team Red.

986
00:38:14,190 --> 00:38:15,960
"Please believe me."

987
00:38:16,060 --> 00:38:19,000
That was the only thing I could say.

988
00:38:19,000 --> 00:38:20,800
Maillard was really confused...

989
00:38:20,800 --> 00:38:22,900
when he heard that.

990
00:38:23,070 --> 00:38:25,470
He looked like he had a lot on his mind.

991
00:38:26,070 --> 00:38:29,380
I was given that role when I got here.

992
00:38:29,440 --> 00:38:32,440
Things have gotten worse...

993
00:38:32,880 --> 00:38:35,050
because the code on the wall
that Team Gold is working on...

994
00:38:35,380 --> 00:38:38,750
is about resetting
the war prize we collected.

995
00:38:38,880 --> 00:38:40,420
It won't come back.

996
00:38:40,420 --> 00:38:41,820
It will just disappear.

997
00:38:41,950 --> 00:38:43,320
That's why I'm telling you.

998
00:38:43,460 --> 00:38:45,960
If possible, could you not solve it?

999
00:38:46,230 --> 00:38:49,830
From now on, I won't touch
the remaining money.

1000
00:38:49,960 --> 00:38:52,160
Since I'm useless now,

1001
00:38:52,160 --> 00:38:53,770
you can leave me out of the split.

1002
00:38:54,230 --> 00:38:56,570
I wanted to tell you that.

1003
00:38:57,440 --> 00:38:58,640
Secondly,

1004
00:38:59,140 --> 00:39:00,410
Vector...

1005
00:39:00,410 --> 00:39:02,510
- knows your code.
- Right.

1006
00:39:02,980 --> 00:39:05,440
I gave it to him.

1007
00:39:05,440 --> 00:39:07,380
I'm sorry about that.

1008
00:39:09,010 --> 00:39:11,320
He could target the code...

1009
00:39:11,380 --> 00:39:13,320
as a last resort,

1010
00:39:13,650 --> 00:39:17,760
so you shouldn't push Vector too hard.

1011
00:39:19,730 --> 00:39:21,760
He tried to get as much
out of us as possible.

1012
00:39:21,760 --> 00:39:24,960
I would be lying if I said
I didn't feel betrayed.

1013
00:39:24,960 --> 00:39:26,970
(Maillard, cooking YouTuber)

1014
00:39:26,970 --> 00:39:30,300
But he worked hard
as a member of our team.

1015
00:39:30,700 --> 00:39:34,640
He did a lot to help us with our survival.

1016
00:39:35,170 --> 00:39:38,510
(Maillard, cooking YouTuber)

1017
00:39:38,510 --> 00:39:41,010
That was why my mind
was filled with different thoughts.

1018
00:39:43,680 --> 00:39:44,980
This is so complicated.

1019
00:39:44,980 --> 00:39:46,420
Right. We don't have enough information.

1020
00:39:46,420 --> 00:39:48,290
We don't have enough information
to make a decision.

1021
00:39:50,290 --> 00:39:53,030
"Is he mad at me?"
That was what I thought.

1022
00:39:53,360 --> 00:39:55,890
He was disappointed in me...

1023
00:39:56,160 --> 00:39:57,730
and was fooled by me.

1024
00:39:58,260 --> 00:40:01,900
I think he felt something beyond
just those feelings.

1025
00:40:12,080 --> 00:40:14,680
This is an announcement
from the Community Center.

1026
00:40:14,880 --> 00:40:17,580
The new rule that applies from Day Six...

1027
00:40:17,580 --> 00:40:21,120
has been delivered. Please take a look.

1028
00:40:21,520 --> 00:40:22,820
- Something has been delivered.
- Right.

1029
00:40:22,820 --> 00:40:25,020
- There must be a new announcement.
- There's something new?

1030
00:40:25,720 --> 00:40:27,560
- Let's open it.
- Gather around.

1031
00:40:29,290 --> 00:40:31,460
- The Relocation Rule.
- Darn it.

1032
00:40:32,000 --> 00:40:34,730
- They've added something ridiculous.
- The Relocation Rule.

1033
00:40:34,730 --> 00:40:35,930
The Relocation Rule has begun.

1034
00:40:35,930 --> 00:40:37,740
- Gosh, I knew it.
- That's insane.

1035
00:40:38,270 --> 00:40:39,940
- That was it.
- Isn't this about switching teams?

1036
00:40:39,940 --> 00:40:41,670
- The Relocation Rule.
- The Relocation Rule.

1037
00:40:42,010 --> 00:40:43,640
"A resident who wishes to
relocate themself..."

1038
00:40:43,640 --> 00:40:46,650
"must visit the Community Center
within opening hours..."

1039
00:40:46,650 --> 00:40:49,110
"and tag the resident notebook."

1040
00:40:49,310 --> 00:40:52,420
That was why there was a QR code
in the resident notebook.

1041
00:40:52,420 --> 00:40:53,550
I wondered why there was a QR code...

1042
00:40:53,550 --> 00:40:55,820
when we weren't allowed to use our phones.

1043
00:40:56,090 --> 00:40:57,290
"The relocation request..."

1044
00:40:57,290 --> 00:40:59,320
- "gets sent to the selected group..."
- Right.

1045
00:40:59,320 --> 00:41:02,090
"through a private message
on the dormitory monitor."

1046
00:41:02,460 --> 00:41:04,830
"If the leader of the selected group
accepts the request,"

1047
00:41:04,830 --> 00:41:08,370
"the relocation gets announced
to all residents."

1048
00:41:08,370 --> 00:41:09,500
"When the request gets denied,"

1049
00:41:09,500 --> 00:41:12,000
"the relocation request
will not get announced."

1050
00:41:12,470 --> 00:41:13,770
Once the relocation happens,

1051
00:41:13,770 --> 00:41:15,340
- it will be announced.
- Right.

1052
00:41:15,340 --> 00:41:17,040
"As soon as the relocation request
gets accepted,"

1053
00:41:17,040 --> 00:41:19,880
"one hour will be given to move things
to the new dormitory."

1054
00:41:19,880 --> 00:41:22,250
"Access to the previous dorm
will be restricted."

1055
00:41:22,250 --> 00:41:24,150
"A resident who is the only member
in a team..."

1056
00:41:25,080 --> 00:41:26,080
Gosh!

1057
00:41:26,750 --> 00:41:29,220
- Pitou must be alone until the end!
- Right.

1058
00:41:30,090 --> 00:41:31,090
"There is no limit..."

1059
00:41:31,090 --> 00:41:33,130
- "on making relocation requests."
- No limit.

1060
00:41:33,660 --> 00:41:35,030
Would anyone want to move?

1061
00:41:35,030 --> 00:41:37,100
They would want to move to us.

1062
00:41:37,100 --> 00:41:40,200
This allows members of Team White
and Team Gold...

1063
00:41:40,200 --> 00:41:43,000
to move back and forth.

1064
00:41:43,000 --> 00:41:45,300
Team White and Team Gold will mix up.

1065
00:41:45,570 --> 00:41:48,770
If two members of Team White...

1066
00:41:48,770 --> 00:41:50,310
- run to Team Gold first,
- Right.

1067
00:41:50,310 --> 00:41:51,880
the slow one...

1068
00:41:53,010 --> 00:41:55,310
- will be left in Team White forever.
- Right.

1069
00:41:55,310 --> 00:41:57,720
That member will be
at a great disadvantage.

1070
00:41:58,750 --> 00:42:00,350
But they might not accept the new member.

1071
00:42:00,550 --> 00:42:02,620
The leader's approval is needed.

1072
00:42:02,620 --> 00:42:03,990
We won't let anyone in.

1073
00:42:03,990 --> 00:42:06,360
- Right.
- It does mean...

1074
00:42:06,530 --> 00:42:08,830
we need an extra life.

1075
00:42:08,830 --> 00:42:10,360
I think this might be possible.

1076
00:42:10,360 --> 00:42:12,800
Team White might leave one person...

1077
00:42:12,800 --> 00:42:14,000
while the others move to Team Blue.

1078
00:42:14,000 --> 00:42:15,870
It's because Team Blue
produces resources well.

1079
00:42:15,970 --> 00:42:17,800
That will be solely based on trust.

1080
00:42:17,800 --> 00:42:20,140
- The last one in Team White...
- Right.

1081
00:42:20,140 --> 00:42:21,740
might get abandoned.

1082
00:42:21,740 --> 00:42:23,310
But the members of Team White
wouldn't do that.

1083
00:42:23,310 --> 00:42:24,640
They wouldn't do that.

1084
00:42:24,640 --> 00:42:27,180
I believe Team White must have
the fewest members possible.

1085
00:42:27,180 --> 00:42:29,110
One person should stay here.

1086
00:42:29,110 --> 00:42:31,120
- Right.
- The others should move to Blue and Red.

1087
00:42:31,380 --> 00:42:33,420
That is possible if the leftover member
of Team White self-destructs.

1088
00:42:33,420 --> 00:42:35,650
The self-destructing one will
self-destruct without taking anything?

1089
00:42:35,650 --> 00:42:37,220
Right. Without taking anything.

1090
00:42:37,220 --> 00:42:41,760
That one will survive until the very end.

1091
00:42:41,760 --> 00:42:43,700
"Let's work together, Black."
This is what will happen next.

1092
00:42:43,700 --> 00:42:45,630
I was the one to come up with this idea.

1093
00:42:45,630 --> 00:42:47,730
I'm confident in becoming
the self-destructing one.

1094
00:42:47,800 --> 00:42:49,330
I'm sorry to say this,

1095
00:42:49,330 --> 00:42:50,840
but you won't be able to win anything.

1096
00:42:50,840 --> 00:42:51,840
It doesn't matter.

1097
00:42:52,070 --> 00:42:53,440
Let's say...

1098
00:42:53,440 --> 00:42:55,940
we will only use gold from now on.

1099
00:42:56,180 --> 00:42:58,780
We will conduct all trades with gold...

1100
00:42:58,780 --> 00:43:01,310
and secure deals with gold.

1101
00:43:01,310 --> 00:43:03,380
As Black doesn't have any gold right now,

1102
00:43:03,380 --> 00:43:05,220
we can make him win nothing.

1103
00:43:05,480 --> 00:43:09,620
The residents paid with diamonds
for war and weapon costs.

1104
00:43:09,620 --> 00:43:14,130
They believe the dealer's prize money
is based on diamonds as well.

1105
00:43:14,630 --> 00:43:17,660
The diamonds earned through
the Platform...

1106
00:43:17,660 --> 00:43:20,330
are believed to be the prize money
of the dealer.

1107
00:43:20,330 --> 00:43:24,570
If gold becomes the resource for
the final prize money instead of diamonds,

1108
00:43:24,970 --> 00:43:27,870
they believe the dealer's prize money
up until now...

1109
00:43:27,870 --> 00:43:30,640
can be turned into nothing.

1110
00:43:31,380 --> 00:43:33,580
However, the dealer's prize money...

1111
00:43:33,580 --> 00:43:36,920
can only be earned from war funds.

1112
00:43:36,920 --> 00:43:39,690
It will be cut down based on the value
of the current currency.

1113
00:43:39,690 --> 00:43:42,090
Based on the value of diamonds earned...

1114
00:43:42,090 --> 00:43:44,820
from war and weapons costs,

1115
00:43:44,820 --> 00:43:47,590
the prize money will be given based on
the current currency.

1116
00:43:47,590 --> 00:43:49,460
(Dealer's profit)

1117
00:43:49,460 --> 00:43:52,400
The prize money will not be affected.

1118
00:43:53,270 --> 00:43:56,000
It doesn't matter who takes the win,

1119
00:43:56,000 --> 00:43:57,640
but Team Gold upsets me.

1120
00:43:57,640 --> 00:43:59,070
I don't have any gold.

1121
00:43:59,070 --> 00:44:00,740
I have no way to earn gold.

1122
00:44:00,740 --> 00:44:02,910
If I suddenly move to Team Gold,

1123
00:44:03,210 --> 00:44:05,980
the others will find it strange.

1124
00:44:06,180 --> 00:44:08,180
This is the reason behind
coming up with this.

1125
00:44:08,180 --> 00:44:10,250
The goal is to give Black a sucker punch.

1126
00:44:10,250 --> 00:44:12,350
If that happens,

1127
00:44:12,350 --> 00:44:15,090
we will give Black
a big smack on the back of his head.

1128
00:44:16,820 --> 00:44:18,490
It's not about having bad feelings
toward him.

1129
00:44:18,490 --> 00:44:20,630
I thought we had to cut off the villain.

1130
00:44:20,630 --> 00:44:24,700
If we continue to side with Black,

1131
00:44:24,700 --> 00:44:26,770
I believe something unexpected
might happen.

1132
00:44:26,770 --> 00:44:28,300
As we wanted to get rid of
the roots of trouble,

1133
00:44:28,300 --> 00:44:29,800
we came up with that plan.

1134
00:44:30,340 --> 00:44:32,670
I'll go and meet Team Red.

1135
00:44:39,580 --> 00:44:41,050
- Let's talk together.
- First of all...

1136
00:44:41,480 --> 00:44:44,680
It has become much harder
to trade with Black.

1137
00:44:44,680 --> 00:44:46,650
There's no sense of trust.

1138
00:44:46,650 --> 00:44:48,490
If we are to give Black a sucker punch,

1139
00:44:48,490 --> 00:44:50,020
we must go with gold instead of diamonds.

1140
00:44:50,020 --> 00:44:53,360
He won't be able to trade with gold.

1141
00:44:53,360 --> 00:44:55,930
Paul will be left on the team
as the bomb man.

1142
00:44:55,930 --> 00:44:57,630
The two of us will go to Team Blue.

1143
00:44:58,230 --> 00:45:00,900
As we can produce lives there,

1144
00:45:00,900 --> 00:45:03,840
there's no need for us
to trade with Black.

1145
00:45:04,040 --> 00:45:06,540
We won't allow Black
to take the upper hand with diamonds.

1146
00:45:06,540 --> 00:45:08,240
We'll stop him from making a profit...

1147
00:45:08,240 --> 00:45:10,280
through deals with the Platform?

1148
00:45:10,280 --> 00:45:11,280
- Right.
- Right.

1149
00:45:11,280 --> 00:45:12,940
This is the reason behind
choosing to do this.

1150
00:45:12,940 --> 00:45:14,710
I'm sorry to say this,
but we couldn't handle him anymore.

1151
00:45:14,710 --> 00:45:16,210
But that's too...

1152
00:45:17,420 --> 00:45:18,420
Well,

1153
00:45:18,420 --> 00:45:19,950
this is my personal opinion.

1154
00:45:19,950 --> 00:45:21,490
- Feel free to speak.
- Feel free to speak.

1155
00:45:21,850 --> 00:45:24,660
I think we should trust Black.

1156
00:45:24,660 --> 00:45:25,960
We must trust Black?

1157
00:45:25,960 --> 00:45:27,060
Right. Just like how things are now.

1158
00:45:27,560 --> 00:45:30,200
This seems to be about
the things we can earn...

1159
00:45:30,200 --> 00:45:33,230
by going against Black.

1160
00:45:33,230 --> 00:45:35,730
But the prize money of 100,000 dollars
will never come back.

1161
00:45:35,870 --> 00:45:37,700
You trust that?

1162
00:45:37,700 --> 00:45:39,300
- That will make it too easy.
- You never know.

1163
00:45:39,300 --> 00:45:40,840
To be honest,

1164
00:45:40,840 --> 00:45:44,640
I believe we might be mistrusting him
for no good reason.

1165
00:45:45,510 --> 00:45:48,380
My eyes moving around can't be seen
when I put on my sunglasses.

1166
00:45:48,380 --> 00:45:50,020
Gosh.

1167
00:45:50,380 --> 00:45:51,720
I saw Donkey...

1168
00:45:51,720 --> 00:45:55,020
swallow his saliva 5 times in 1 second...

1169
00:45:55,020 --> 00:45:57,990
and move his Adam's apple back and forth.

1170
00:45:57,990 --> 00:45:59,730
I thought that I should
get some information from him...

1171
00:45:59,730 --> 00:46:02,160
or persuade him.

1172
00:46:07,930 --> 00:46:08,930
Spy?

1173
00:46:08,930 --> 00:46:09,940
What?

1174
00:46:10,270 --> 00:46:11,800
I'm asking if you're a spy.

1175
00:46:12,200 --> 00:46:13,310
What spy?

1176
00:46:14,270 --> 00:46:15,470
Are you Black's spy?

1177
00:46:16,440 --> 00:46:17,440
Who said that?

1178
00:46:17,540 --> 00:46:18,540
Black.

1179
00:46:18,540 --> 00:46:19,680
- Black said that?
- Yes.

1180
00:46:20,710 --> 00:46:22,050
"Why does he know?"

1181
00:46:22,050 --> 00:46:25,980
"Why does he know about this already?"

1182
00:46:26,380 --> 00:46:27,390
Well...

1183
00:46:27,390 --> 00:46:28,850
(Donkey, stand-up comedian,
Meaning, Ability, Consequence)

1184
00:46:28,850 --> 00:46:30,360
"Why did Black tell him?"

1185
00:46:31,090 --> 00:46:32,290
I felt flustered.

1186
00:46:32,720 --> 00:46:33,830
What did you two talk about?

1187
00:46:33,960 --> 00:46:35,560
Well, a few things.

1188
00:46:36,430 --> 00:46:38,260
- I am a spy.
- Right.

1189
00:46:38,930 --> 00:46:40,570
Who else knows about this?

1190
00:46:40,970 --> 00:46:43,640
To be honest,
all members of our team know about this.

1191
00:46:43,870 --> 00:46:45,970
I have no intention
of causing harm to the team.

1192
00:46:45,970 --> 00:46:48,010
It's the same with the other teams.

1193
00:46:48,010 --> 00:46:50,510
- Right.
- There's no reason for me to do that.

1194
00:46:50,510 --> 00:46:53,380
I'm not fooling others to cause harm.

1195
00:46:53,380 --> 00:46:55,180
- You don't need to worry about that.
- Do you know how...

1196
00:46:55,450 --> 00:46:57,150
Vector won't be able to earn resources...

1197
00:46:57,150 --> 00:46:58,380
and how to go against him from doing so?

1198
00:46:58,650 --> 00:47:00,650
- Oh, right.
- You must share that with us.

1199
00:47:00,820 --> 00:47:02,220
If you keep this hidden,

1200
00:47:02,220 --> 00:47:04,790
we will have to come up
with a different plan.

1201
00:47:04,960 --> 00:47:06,160
- Right.
- Right.

1202
00:47:07,230 --> 00:47:08,890
Could you give me some time
to think about this?

1203
00:47:08,890 --> 00:47:10,300
- Sure.
- We know about you.

1204
00:47:11,330 --> 00:47:12,900
I'll take some time to think.

1205
00:47:15,130 --> 00:47:18,300
I'm not sure what Vector
is thinking about.

1206
00:47:18,870 --> 00:47:20,740
"Is he doing this as part of his plan?"

1207
00:47:20,740 --> 00:47:23,380
"Is he causing problems?"

1208
00:47:23,710 --> 00:47:25,610
I'm not sure where he is right now.

1209
00:47:26,010 --> 00:47:27,450
"Does he want us to both die?"

1210
00:47:29,280 --> 00:47:30,280
Can I have a word?

1211
00:47:30,580 --> 00:47:31,580
Sure.

1212
00:47:32,150 --> 00:47:33,150
Vector...

1213
00:47:33,690 --> 00:47:36,590
told Team White about my identity as well.

1214
00:47:37,390 --> 00:47:38,590
What is he doing?

1215
00:47:40,060 --> 00:47:42,560
I think he's doing everything he can
before his end.

1216
00:47:47,630 --> 00:47:49,200
If you die,

1217
00:47:49,200 --> 00:47:51,300
will Vector's prize money
be cut in half as well?

1218
00:47:51,300 --> 00:47:52,300
Yes.

1219
00:47:56,810 --> 00:47:58,580
He just threw you under the bus.

1220
00:47:58,780 --> 00:48:00,280
That could be the case.

1221
00:48:00,580 --> 00:48:02,380
But that means it doesn't matter to him
if you die.

1222
00:48:02,380 --> 00:48:03,780
Half of the prize money
must be shared with you if you survive.

1223
00:48:04,250 --> 00:48:06,050
Half of the prize money will be lost
if you die.

1224
00:48:07,490 --> 00:48:09,320
He must be acting this way
after coming up with a plan.

1225
00:48:09,490 --> 00:48:12,190
I need to hear about what he wants to do.

1226
00:48:12,560 --> 00:48:16,760
It might be his method
of coming out of the corner.

1227
00:48:17,560 --> 00:48:19,700
But he shouldn't be talking about you.

1228
00:48:20,730 --> 00:48:23,400
That doesn't help with solving his issues.

1229
00:48:23,700 --> 00:48:25,400
I also didn't expect him
to talk about my identity.

1230
00:48:25,540 --> 00:48:27,310
I can't understand why he did that.

1231
00:48:28,270 --> 00:48:30,840
He's making reckless plays.

1232
00:48:32,240 --> 00:48:35,110
This is something
I still struggle to understand.

1233
00:48:35,350 --> 00:48:39,580
He gave his ally's information
to Team White's Paul.

1234
00:48:39,680 --> 00:48:44,490
That makes it really hard for me
to protect Donkey.

1235
00:48:44,560 --> 00:48:46,560
Even after knowing that he's a spy,

1236
00:48:46,560 --> 00:48:48,490
keeping him on the same team...

1237
00:48:48,490 --> 00:48:51,500
can spark a big problem for Team Red.

1238
00:48:51,500 --> 00:48:53,400
It felt like...

1239
00:48:53,400 --> 00:48:56,430
he threw his ally under the bus.

1240
00:48:57,000 --> 00:48:58,970
Donkey was in danger...

1241
00:48:58,970 --> 00:49:02,670
and it also shook up our team's bond.

1242
00:49:02,810 --> 00:49:04,740
I just couldn't understand it.

1243
00:49:07,280 --> 00:49:09,680
I think he played all of his cards...

1244
00:49:10,250 --> 00:49:12,680
and lay on the floor.

1245
00:49:16,220 --> 00:49:17,660
Should I just pollute the pot?

1246
00:49:17,720 --> 00:49:19,160
This is annoying as heck.

1247
00:49:20,730 --> 00:49:22,060
Darn jerks.

1248
00:49:22,260 --> 00:49:23,330
Let's see you die.

1249
00:49:24,760 --> 00:49:26,670
Can I take one of the chairs?

1250
00:49:26,670 --> 00:49:27,730
Sure.

1251
00:49:29,730 --> 00:49:30,870
Gosh, my back.

1252
00:49:31,270 --> 00:49:32,840
My back's killing me.

1253
00:49:40,580 --> 00:49:42,950
- What?
- Why is he sitting out there?

1254
00:49:43,250 --> 00:49:44,320
I'm resting.

1255
00:49:44,750 --> 00:49:45,820
The weather's too nice.

1256
00:49:45,950 --> 00:49:48,390
Maybe you can get a view
of everyone from there.

1257
00:49:49,650 --> 00:49:53,120
Donkey and Maillard
were talking at the Hub,

1258
00:49:53,290 --> 00:49:54,760
mentioning things like...

1259
00:49:54,760 --> 00:49:56,560
blowing everyone up.

1260
00:49:57,030 --> 00:49:58,700
(Paul, Dancer)

1261
00:49:58,700 --> 00:50:02,000
This is something only I can do,

1262
00:50:02,530 --> 00:50:04,040
but I got myself a chair...

1263
00:50:04,040 --> 00:50:05,870
and listened to what they had to say.

1264
00:50:06,570 --> 00:50:08,570
I'm like the sheriff of this community.

1265
00:50:09,540 --> 00:50:11,580
That's right. The sheriff.

1266
00:50:12,280 --> 00:50:13,450
(Dormitory for Gold)

1267
00:50:13,450 --> 00:50:14,480
- Here's where we are.
- Yes, we should do that.

1268
00:50:14,910 --> 00:50:17,580
Luna is saying...

1269
00:50:17,580 --> 00:50:20,790
that we need
to take a different approach here.

1270
00:50:20,990 --> 00:50:23,690
I'm just suggesting
we try saying this once.

1271
00:50:23,960 --> 00:50:26,220
"Secret room of center."

1272
00:50:26,220 --> 00:50:27,690
The facility over there is the center.

1273
00:50:28,090 --> 00:50:29,790
You think there's a secret room there?

1274
00:50:29,960 --> 00:50:32,960
I'm just saying there's no harm in trying.

1275
00:50:32,960 --> 00:50:34,600
- Let's go there.
- Is it open?

1276
00:50:34,600 --> 00:50:36,230
- I think it will be.
- Let's give it a try.

1277
00:50:36,230 --> 00:50:37,300
Let's go there.

1278
00:50:38,940 --> 00:50:41,070
We need to get this puzzle solved...

1279
00:50:41,170 --> 00:50:42,970
so we can move on.

1280
00:50:45,240 --> 00:50:48,450
(Occupied: Please wait.)

1281
00:50:55,350 --> 00:50:57,390
Let's take our time with this.

1282
00:50:58,390 --> 00:51:00,860
We're here to unlock the secret.

1283
00:51:00,860 --> 00:51:01,860
That's right.

1284
00:51:01,860 --> 00:51:04,030
- Tell these words within... This?
- Yes.

1285
00:51:08,900 --> 00:51:11,500
"Tell these words in the center."

1286
00:51:14,570 --> 00:51:16,940
"The truth of the weapon dealer..."

1287
00:51:20,480 --> 00:51:21,750
"placed within..."

1288
00:51:23,650 --> 00:51:24,880
"secret room..."

1289
00:51:25,850 --> 00:51:26,990
"of center."

1290
00:51:35,330 --> 00:51:38,800
The exact command has been stated.

1291
00:51:39,960 --> 00:51:40,970
What the...

1292
00:51:41,830 --> 00:51:42,900
What the...

1293
00:51:46,940 --> 00:51:47,970
My gosh!

1294
00:51:49,710 --> 00:51:52,310
- My gosh!
- The weapon dealer's secret safe...

1295
00:51:52,310 --> 00:51:53,480
has been opened.

1296
00:51:53,480 --> 00:51:55,910
(Vector's current total prize money)

1297
00:51:56,950 --> 00:51:58,550
My gosh!

1298
00:52:00,550 --> 00:52:02,120
My gosh!

1299
00:52:04,720 --> 00:52:07,060
Quiet, guys. They'll hear us from outside.

1300
00:52:10,060 --> 00:52:12,460
- That jerk.
- That jerk. We were right!

1301
00:52:12,560 --> 00:52:14,670
- Vector's current total prize money.
- What?

1302
00:52:14,670 --> 00:52:16,670
- Vector's current total prize money.
- What?

1303
00:52:16,670 --> 00:52:19,000
- I got goosebumps all over my legs.
- We were right!

1304
00:52:19,370 --> 00:52:20,840
So, from here...

1305
00:52:22,440 --> 00:52:24,080
- Guys...
- The dopamine rush!

1306
00:52:24,140 --> 00:52:26,380
Anyway, this is the secret room, right?

1307
00:52:26,380 --> 00:52:28,210
- Then, we...
- Team Gold...

1308
00:52:28,210 --> 00:52:30,480
has opened the weapon dealer's...

1309
00:52:30,480 --> 00:52:31,680
secret safe.

1310
00:52:32,080 --> 00:52:35,390
The weapon dealer's prize money
will be erased.

1311
00:52:38,660 --> 00:52:39,690
Nice!

1312
00:52:39,690 --> 00:52:43,160
(Vector's current total prize money)

1313
00:52:45,260 --> 00:52:46,400
We hit the jackpot.

1314
00:52:46,400 --> 00:52:48,930
The dopamine hit was real,
and I got goosebumps all over.

1315
00:52:49,030 --> 00:52:50,600
I really got goosebumps.

1316
00:52:50,740 --> 00:52:53,340
The rush of accomplishment...

1317
00:52:53,340 --> 00:52:55,110
sent a buzz through my whole body.

1318
00:52:55,310 --> 00:52:58,510
The weapon dealer's secret safe
has been opened.

1319
00:52:58,980 --> 00:53:01,950
The weapon dealer's prize money
has been erased.

1320
00:53:05,980 --> 00:53:07,820
Are you kidding me? Okay, fine.

1321
00:53:08,520 --> 00:53:10,220
Okay, back to making money, then.

1322
00:53:11,360 --> 00:53:12,420
We won.

1323
00:53:12,420 --> 00:53:14,830
- We took out the public enemy.
- I know.

1324
00:53:15,490 --> 00:53:16,560
I wanted to share the news badly...

1325
00:53:17,130 --> 00:53:18,130
with Team White.

1326
00:53:19,560 --> 00:53:21,800
Honestly, that's all I could think about.

1327
00:53:21,900 --> 00:53:23,800
So that they'd stop being played,

1328
00:53:23,840 --> 00:53:25,870
I wanted them to know the truth.

1329
00:53:25,940 --> 00:53:29,370
On top of that,
the initial idea was Leia's,

1330
00:53:29,540 --> 00:53:31,740
so I wanted to tell her
that she was right.

1331
00:53:32,740 --> 00:53:34,850
The safe was opened,
so the prize is now at zero.

1332
00:53:34,850 --> 00:53:35,980
I can't believe he had 100,000 dollars.

1333
00:53:35,980 --> 00:53:37,880
- Now, a war shouldn't happen.
- He's now at zero.

1334
00:53:37,880 --> 00:53:39,750
- We can't afford a war.
- Back at zero.

1335
00:53:39,750 --> 00:53:41,350
Let's go expose him.

1336
00:53:41,350 --> 00:53:42,920
- A war can't happen.
- This...

1337
00:53:42,920 --> 00:53:44,890
- Let's announce this first.
- Let's declare this.

1338
00:53:44,890 --> 00:53:45,960
- Exactly.
- Let's declare this.

1339
00:53:54,570 --> 00:53:56,230
It was tough to crack.

1340
00:53:57,500 --> 00:53:59,240
Should the supermarket guy be this late?

1341
00:53:59,570 --> 00:54:01,040
Sorry, everyone.

1342
00:54:01,370 --> 00:54:03,470
I had a lot on my mind, so I was late.

1343
00:54:04,280 --> 00:54:07,480
You know, we could've got this
in the morning.

1344
00:54:07,480 --> 00:54:09,210
- Exactly.
- I got goosebumps all over.

1345
00:54:09,210 --> 00:54:10,720
Can you guys come with me for a second?

1346
00:54:10,720 --> 00:54:11,750
It shouldn't get complicated.

1347
00:54:15,890 --> 00:54:17,760
Did you hear
that they answered it correctly?

1348
00:54:18,620 --> 00:54:19,860
No, I didn't see anything.

1349
00:54:20,290 --> 00:54:21,830
Aren't we having...

1350
00:54:21,830 --> 00:54:24,100
- the best time here since we arrived?
- We are.

1351
00:54:24,160 --> 00:54:27,030
I'm so happy because it feels like...

1352
00:54:27,030 --> 00:54:28,170
we've found the answer.

1353
00:54:28,530 --> 00:54:30,640
- Team Gold just solved it.
- Did they?

1354
00:54:30,900 --> 00:54:32,700
Our prize money is now gone.

1355
00:54:32,700 --> 00:54:33,910
- Is it over for us?
- Yes.

1356
00:54:34,070 --> 00:54:35,470
- Then...
- We need to slowly...

1357
00:54:35,470 --> 00:54:37,280
- earn some more.
- Why?

1358
00:54:37,740 --> 00:54:40,750
I'll help so that diamonds
become the currency.

1359
00:54:40,910 --> 00:54:43,380
So when things stabilize for you guys,

1360
00:54:43,580 --> 00:54:45,420
start an internal conflict...

1361
00:54:45,720 --> 00:54:46,750
and make sure...

1362
00:54:46,750 --> 00:54:48,190
- we don't leave with nothing.
- Got it.

1363
00:54:48,290 --> 00:54:49,920
If you promise that,
we'll stick with White all the way.

1364
00:54:49,920 --> 00:54:51,390
- That's an extreme example.
- Everyone.

1365
00:54:51,390 --> 00:54:52,490
Everyone.

1366
00:54:52,990 --> 00:54:55,230
Team Gold...

1367
00:54:55,230 --> 00:54:58,100
would like to make an announcement.

1368
00:54:58,200 --> 00:55:00,730
Can you gather around and listen?

1369
00:55:01,030 --> 00:55:03,430
Why don't I relay the news?

1370
00:55:03,430 --> 00:55:05,200
- No, we'd like to say it.
- We'll say it ourselves.

1371
00:55:05,200 --> 00:55:06,340
- We'll...
- Sure, go ahead.

1372
00:55:06,340 --> 00:55:07,570
- We'll say it.
- It really doesn't matter.

1373
00:55:07,570 --> 00:55:09,540
- We'll be the ones to say it.
- Sure.

1374
00:55:09,540 --> 00:55:12,080
- We...
- I'm the weapon dealer...

1375
00:55:12,080 --> 00:55:13,310
and my prize is now gone.

1376
00:55:14,110 --> 00:55:15,350
Right, well...

1377
00:55:15,550 --> 00:55:17,320
We'll say it ourselves.

1378
00:55:17,350 --> 00:55:18,380
Congratulations.

1379
00:55:19,520 --> 00:55:21,590
To be honest, it was annoying.

1380
00:55:21,820 --> 00:55:24,420
Black stole our thunder
by announcing it before we could.

1381
00:55:24,790 --> 00:55:26,320
Even in that moment,

1382
00:55:26,420 --> 00:55:29,590
he seemed obsessed with being
in the spotlight.

1383
00:55:29,760 --> 00:55:32,960
That's why I didn't hold back
and kept trying to say it in my own words.

1384
00:55:33,160 --> 00:55:34,830
- We'll say it ourselves.
- Sure.

1385
00:55:34,830 --> 00:55:37,000
We solved the code...

1386
00:55:37,100 --> 00:55:38,900
- You solved the Wall Code.
- on the wall.

1387
00:55:38,900 --> 00:55:40,540
This is what it said.

1388
00:55:40,640 --> 00:55:42,770
"Tell these words in the center."

1389
00:55:43,510 --> 00:55:45,740
"The truth of the weapon dealer..."

1390
00:55:46,010 --> 00:55:49,710
"placed within the secret room of center."

1391
00:55:49,810 --> 00:55:53,180
With that, we were able to unlock
the weapon dealer's identity.

1392
00:55:53,180 --> 00:55:54,320
It turns out...

1393
00:55:54,490 --> 00:55:56,190
Vector was holding 100,000 dollars
in prize money,

1394
00:55:56,190 --> 00:56:00,760
meaning all the war expenses
from this community were going directly...

1395
00:56:00,760 --> 00:56:02,760
into his pockets.

1396
00:56:02,760 --> 00:56:04,930
Once we uncovered the truth,

1397
00:56:05,530 --> 00:56:07,030
his money vanished.

1398
00:56:07,030 --> 00:56:08,070
Congratulations.

1399
00:56:13,570 --> 00:56:17,040
The other residents
didn't seem thrilled at all.

1400
00:56:17,410 --> 00:56:19,410
How should I put it?

1401
00:56:19,410 --> 00:56:22,150
It's not like we gained anything...

1402
00:56:22,450 --> 00:56:24,250
from it, but...

1403
00:56:24,580 --> 00:56:26,580
Still, I'm really grateful...

1404
00:56:26,880 --> 00:56:28,490
you figured it out so quickly.

1405
00:56:28,490 --> 00:56:30,590
I was worried you'd solve it
right before the game ended.

1406
00:56:30,990 --> 00:56:33,690
I couldn't have fixed it
if you'd solved it later,

1407
00:56:33,690 --> 00:56:35,360
but getting it today...

1408
00:56:35,890 --> 00:56:36,960
saved me.

1409
00:56:37,700 --> 00:56:39,560
Thanks to that...

1410
00:56:41,030 --> 00:56:43,470
That's why I approached you yesterday,

1411
00:56:43,700 --> 00:56:45,170
telling you not to solve the Wall Code...

1412
00:56:45,170 --> 00:56:46,770
because it would get you nowhere.

1413
00:56:46,770 --> 00:56:49,270
Now, I have no reason to help Team Gold.

1414
00:56:49,270 --> 00:56:50,710
We don't need your help.

1415
00:56:50,710 --> 00:56:51,710
Got it.

1416
00:56:51,710 --> 00:56:53,810
- We got it too.
- We'll talk among ourselves now.

1417
00:56:54,680 --> 00:56:57,250
I was offended.
He made it sound like we're nothing,

1418
00:56:57,380 --> 00:57:00,520
and that us solving the Wall Code was...

1419
00:57:00,520 --> 00:57:02,720
within his control all along.

1420
00:57:02,720 --> 00:57:06,460
It sounded like he was trying
to get that message across to us.

1421
00:57:06,690 --> 00:57:08,190
I was disgusted by it.

1422
00:57:09,160 --> 00:57:12,500
The Wall Code was my only risk,

1423
00:57:12,760 --> 00:57:14,430
and I think Team Gold freed me from it.

1424
00:57:14,970 --> 00:57:17,940
The weapon dealer is...

1425
00:57:18,200 --> 00:57:21,140
a saint on the outside,
but a devil behind the scenes.

1426
00:57:21,270 --> 00:57:22,740
He was born to be the villain.

1427
00:57:23,040 --> 00:57:24,780
The moment I got this role,

1428
00:57:24,780 --> 00:57:27,650
I knew being painted as the villain
was part of the deal.

1429
00:57:28,280 --> 00:57:30,550
But since I'd already laid
all the groundwork,

1430
00:57:30,550 --> 00:57:32,480
no one was surprised by the revelation.

1431
00:57:32,850 --> 00:57:34,720
That's why I volunteered
to share the news,

1432
00:57:34,720 --> 00:57:36,190
since everyone already
knew about it anyway.

1433
00:57:36,290 --> 00:57:39,190
I was trying to brush it off as nothing.

1434
00:57:39,660 --> 00:57:40,830
We're not that surprised...

1435
00:57:40,830 --> 00:57:42,260
- because we already knew.
- We already knew.

1436
00:57:42,260 --> 00:57:43,460
- You already knew?
- Yes.

1437
00:57:43,530 --> 00:57:45,800
- Still, we had to tell you.
- Right, and we appreciate it.

1438
00:57:45,800 --> 00:57:46,930
I was worried.

1439
00:57:47,330 --> 00:57:50,300
I couldn't have fixed it
if you'd solved it later,

1440
00:57:50,300 --> 00:57:52,470
- but getting it today...
- Darn it.

1441
00:57:53,270 --> 00:57:55,570
Luna, what's wrong?
Aren't you feeling well?

1442
00:57:56,070 --> 00:57:57,810
- I'm just so annoyed.
- Why?

1443
00:57:58,180 --> 00:57:59,540
What's with his attitude?

1444
00:57:59,540 --> 00:58:01,580
Vector's just really getting on my nerves.

1445
00:58:01,810 --> 00:58:02,910
Annoying, right?

1446
00:58:03,750 --> 00:58:05,350
Are you kidding me?

1447
00:58:05,750 --> 00:58:07,920
- Unbelievable.
- Did you find out just now?

1448
00:58:07,920 --> 00:58:09,090
Of course.

1449
00:58:09,550 --> 00:58:12,560
Black was just bluffing us this morning.

1450
00:58:12,690 --> 00:58:14,660
I don't mind playing the game like that.

1451
00:58:14,660 --> 00:58:17,160
It's understandable,
especially if you're backed into a corner.

1452
00:58:17,160 --> 00:58:18,800
We can't all be logical and reasonable
all the time.

1453
00:58:18,800 --> 00:58:21,800
But everything he's said and done
since yesterday...

1454
00:58:21,800 --> 00:58:24,500
has been getting on my nerves.

1455
00:58:24,700 --> 00:58:27,070
- Wait, forget the emotional part.
- Yes, of course.

1456
00:58:27,070 --> 00:58:28,340
Where do we go from here?

1457
00:58:28,440 --> 00:58:32,140
The way I see it,
Gold, White, Red, and Blue are all...

1458
00:58:32,210 --> 00:58:33,310
up against Black.

1459
00:58:33,310 --> 00:58:34,950
That's what I'm saying.

1460
00:58:35,150 --> 00:58:36,780
- But what can we do about it?
- Nothing.

1461
00:58:36,780 --> 00:58:37,980
- Exactly.
- There's nothing we can do.

1462
00:58:39,380 --> 00:58:41,120
Let's talk somewhere else.

1463
00:58:41,320 --> 00:58:43,720
Let's go to the Hub to talk for a bit.

1464
00:58:44,890 --> 00:58:45,990
Seriously.

1465
00:58:45,990 --> 00:58:49,130
Why did they take away
the 100,000 dollars we could've had?

1466
00:58:49,290 --> 00:58:50,360
They didn't know.

1467
00:58:51,530 --> 00:58:52,530
What a bummer.

1468
00:58:52,530 --> 00:58:54,900
I'll play an honest game from now on
and leave with a small earning.

1469
00:58:55,200 --> 00:58:56,800
Honestly? Serves him right.

1470
00:58:57,100 --> 00:58:59,340
He got what he deserved.

1471
00:58:59,870 --> 00:59:01,840
It's not like I could give him a beating,

1472
00:59:01,840 --> 00:59:03,670
and I hated the way he was playing sneaky.

1473
00:59:03,670 --> 00:59:05,340
Serves him right.

1474
00:59:06,010 --> 00:59:09,050
Based on his attitude,
I felt like he didn't see of us...

1475
00:59:09,050 --> 00:59:10,310
- as part of the game.
- You're right.

1476
00:59:10,310 --> 00:59:11,320
- Therefore...
- It only...

1477
00:59:11,320 --> 00:59:13,450
left a bad taste in my mouth.

1478
00:59:13,450 --> 00:59:15,020
Right. So... To be honest,

1479
00:59:15,320 --> 00:59:17,290
I'm not really happy about it.

1480
00:59:17,290 --> 00:59:19,190
- I don't like his attitude.
- Same here.

1481
00:59:19,320 --> 00:59:21,890
I honestly don't understand
why Team Black plays the game like this.

1482
00:59:23,330 --> 00:59:27,570
Up until that point,
no one else knew that I was a spy.

1483
00:59:27,570 --> 00:59:29,400
Even Team Gold didn't know that.

1484
00:59:29,830 --> 00:59:32,970
Had he not revealed it,
Team White wouldn't have known either.

1485
00:59:33,200 --> 00:59:36,070
Then, only Maillard, Black, and I
would've known,

1486
00:59:36,410 --> 00:59:38,810
which would've made it easy for us
to come up with a new plan.

1487
00:59:39,210 --> 00:59:41,380
The fact that he just gave up on it...

1488
00:59:41,380 --> 00:59:43,250
(Donkey, stand-up comedian,
Meaning, Ability, Consequence)

1489
00:59:43,250 --> 00:59:45,350
I think
it could be the reason for the failure.

1490
00:59:45,580 --> 00:59:48,190
Your special meal has arrived.0

1491
00:59:48,450 --> 00:59:49,450
Awesome.

1492
00:59:49,450 --> 00:59:50,760
- Did we order packed meals?
- Yes.

1493
00:59:51,620 --> 00:59:53,760
- Enjoy.
- Enjoy your meal.

1494
00:59:53,760 --> 00:59:55,090
(Team Gold couldn't purchase lunch.)

1495
00:59:55,730 --> 00:59:57,760
- They're having a chat, so...
- Sorry?

1496
00:59:58,830 --> 01:00:01,530
I mean, we might as well get acquainted
with them instead of staying by ourselves.

1497
01:00:01,530 --> 01:00:03,200
We have nothing to do in our room anyway.

1498
01:00:03,770 --> 01:00:04,800
- Hey.
- Hi.

1499
01:00:04,800 --> 01:00:06,740
- You were talking with your head down.
- Yes.

1500
01:00:06,740 --> 01:00:07,970
- With his head down?
- We should stay focused.

1501
01:00:07,970 --> 01:00:09,470
Yes. I was curious.

1502
01:00:09,910 --> 01:00:11,610
I find productive activities
most enjoyable.

1503
01:00:11,880 --> 01:00:13,080
Yes, it's fun.

1504
01:00:13,440 --> 01:00:15,150
It's stir-fried eggplant...
It's an eggplant dish.

1505
01:00:15,150 --> 01:00:16,210
It's deep-fried eggplant.

1506
01:00:16,750 --> 01:00:17,920
From now on, will you really...

1507
01:00:18,650 --> 01:00:19,820
Will you not give them food?

1508
01:00:19,820 --> 01:00:21,650
How can I do that when they attacked me?

1509
01:00:22,720 --> 01:00:23,990
- We have a lot to eat.
- They really...

1510
01:00:23,990 --> 01:00:26,090
They crushed my hopes and dreams.
I have no choice.

1511
01:00:26,090 --> 01:00:27,260
- You mean, the 100,000 dollars?
- Yes.

1512
01:00:27,260 --> 01:00:28,630
But that was because you...

1513
01:00:29,360 --> 01:00:32,060
I was going to give them some food today.

1514
01:00:32,060 --> 01:00:34,230
- But they stabbed me in the back.
- I see.

1515
01:00:35,230 --> 01:00:37,970
I think he, too,
is a bear trying hard to be a fox.

1516
01:00:38,540 --> 01:00:39,900
Even if we don't eat now...

1517
01:00:40,200 --> 01:00:42,540
We still have one packed meal left.

1518
01:00:42,540 --> 01:00:44,880
I think we can hold out for a day or two.

1519
01:00:45,210 --> 01:00:46,440
How about this? Let's take this with us.

1520
01:00:46,440 --> 01:00:47,780
(Team Gold kept the food
they received yesterday.)

1521
01:00:47,780 --> 01:00:50,110
I'll take the fried... Wait up for me.

1522
01:00:51,220 --> 01:00:52,380
I do understand him,

1523
01:00:52,380 --> 01:00:54,790
but it's not exactly cool
to pull a power trip using food.

1524
01:00:57,960 --> 01:00:59,020
Well, I...

1525
01:00:59,020 --> 01:01:00,860
I hope they'll give us a special meal
like samgyetang again.

1526
01:01:01,060 --> 01:01:02,130
Right.

1527
01:01:02,360 --> 01:01:04,400
- Why don't they eat first and then talk?
- I just...

1528
01:01:05,060 --> 01:01:07,000
- Exactly.
- It's bothering me.

1529
01:01:07,200 --> 01:01:08,400
We can't eat now...

1530
01:01:08,400 --> 01:01:10,070
because we don't have money for food.

1531
01:01:10,570 --> 01:01:12,070
I wasn't talking about Team Gold.

1532
01:01:12,870 --> 01:01:14,370
- Oh, them?
- That was scary.

1533
01:01:20,180 --> 01:01:23,180
I know. I wonder
how many battles have been prepared.

1534
01:01:23,850 --> 01:01:25,780
How do you fight a war?

1535
01:01:25,780 --> 01:01:27,790
- I'm sure it's not a physical fight.
- Of course not.

1536
01:01:27,790 --> 01:01:28,820
- We play a game.
- We solve a quiz.

1537
01:01:28,820 --> 01:01:30,620
- It's kind of a large-scale quiz.
- Is it like a battle of wits?

1538
01:01:30,820 --> 01:01:33,160
- What was the question?
- We can't tell you that.

1539
01:01:33,520 --> 01:01:34,860
- It could be repeated.
- Really?

1540
01:01:40,400 --> 01:01:43,400
I feel like we were dancing to his tune,
and it made me feel so disgusted.

1541
01:01:43,730 --> 01:01:45,600
That was so stressful for me.

1542
01:01:46,170 --> 01:01:48,870
But now, I think that
if even a single war breaks out...

1543
01:01:48,940 --> 01:01:49,940
Then, it'll all be over.

1544
01:01:49,940 --> 01:01:52,140
He'll make us bleed our resources
for the war cost again.

1545
01:01:52,210 --> 01:01:54,650
And the rest of the people will fight
against one another again.

1546
01:01:54,650 --> 01:01:56,010
- At that point, it's just game over.
- Exactly.

1547
01:01:56,010 --> 01:01:57,350
Team Blue needs
to pull themselves together...

1548
01:01:57,350 --> 01:01:59,250
and cut Team Black out
as soon as possible,

1549
01:01:59,250 --> 01:02:01,150
so we can just focus on producing lives...

1550
01:02:01,150 --> 01:02:02,690
- and surviving together.
- Right.

1551
01:02:02,890 --> 01:02:04,360
- Can all of you make it to the final day?
- Yes.

1552
01:02:04,360 --> 01:02:07,220
- Exactly how many do you have?
- We had exactly 25.

1553
01:02:07,220 --> 01:02:08,530
- Twenty-five?
- Yes.

1554
01:02:08,530 --> 01:02:09,930
So we have enough lives for four days...

1555
01:02:09,930 --> 01:02:11,330
- and extra five lives.
- I see.

1556
01:02:11,330 --> 01:02:12,630
- And we produced more lives today.
- Okay.

1557
01:02:12,630 --> 01:02:14,070
- We can save Team Red.
- You guys can even...

1558
01:02:14,070 --> 01:02:16,000
- save us.
- My point exactly.

1559
01:02:16,000 --> 01:02:18,140
If we all just agree
to turn on Team Black...

1560
01:02:18,140 --> 01:02:19,200
- Right.
- Yes.

1561
01:02:19,200 --> 01:02:21,110
We thought your team had only a few.

1562
01:02:21,440 --> 01:02:22,970
- Also...
- You need to tell them it's not true.

1563
01:02:22,970 --> 01:02:24,780
- Here's the bottom line.
- Okay.

1564
01:02:24,780 --> 01:02:26,980
At this point,
it's completely pointless...

1565
01:02:26,980 --> 01:02:29,010
to debate which team to ally with.

1566
01:02:29,150 --> 01:02:30,250
It's simple.

1567
01:02:30,450 --> 01:02:33,050
Think about the lives
your team and mine have secured...

1568
01:02:33,050 --> 01:02:34,350
and the number of days remaining.

1569
01:02:34,350 --> 01:02:35,950
And calculate the total life supply.

1570
01:02:35,950 --> 01:02:38,220
- It's enough for all of us to survive.
- Yes.

1571
01:02:38,360 --> 01:02:39,820
- No one has to die.
- Exactly.

1572
01:02:39,920 --> 01:02:41,760
Then why have we been fighting wars?

1573
01:02:42,160 --> 01:02:43,460
We did that not to get eliminated.

1574
01:02:43,560 --> 01:02:45,060
But we won't get eliminated,

1575
01:02:45,130 --> 01:02:46,930
and there's no reason to start a war.

1576
01:02:46,930 --> 01:02:49,630
- But we couldn't share our information.
- That's right.

1577
01:02:49,630 --> 01:02:51,670
- "We might die. Should we kill them?"
- Right.

1578
01:02:51,670 --> 01:02:53,300
"They'll probably attack us
as they're on the verge of elimination."

1579
01:02:53,300 --> 01:02:54,510
- Right.
- That's what we've been doing.

1580
01:02:54,510 --> 01:02:57,980
That fear of elimination is what made us
turn against each other.

1581
01:02:57,980 --> 01:03:00,480
With this information out there,
Team Black will be isolated.

1582
01:03:00,480 --> 01:03:01,910
- Exactly.
- Team Black being isolated means...

1583
01:03:01,910 --> 01:03:04,480
- there will be no more wars here.
- Right.

1584
01:03:04,480 --> 01:03:05,550
- That's what it symbolizes.
- Yes.

1585
01:03:05,550 --> 01:03:07,890
- Here's my question. After that...
- Okay.

1586
01:03:07,890 --> 01:03:10,990
After survival, we still have to deal
with the prize money.

1587
01:03:10,990 --> 01:03:13,060
- It's the currency of Gold or White.
- Yes.

1588
01:03:13,060 --> 01:03:14,390
Once our survival is guaranteed,

1589
01:03:14,390 --> 01:03:16,390
- we'll naturally want some prize money.
- Yes.

1590
01:03:16,390 --> 01:03:18,800
If things keep going
the way they are going now,

1591
01:03:18,800 --> 01:03:20,500
- gold will be selected.
- Right.

1592
01:03:20,500 --> 01:03:21,930
Then what will Team White get?

1593
01:03:21,930 --> 01:03:24,440
So Team Gold needs
to take in everyone from Team White.

1594
01:03:24,440 --> 01:03:26,670
- But one person must stay on the team.
- That person will make a sacrifice.

1595
01:03:32,340 --> 01:03:33,640
We even considered that possibility.

1596
01:03:34,180 --> 01:03:35,310
My team considered it.

1597
01:03:43,220 --> 01:03:44,390
But who would make that sacrifice?

1598
01:03:44,490 --> 01:03:45,590
I don't mind being the one.

1599
01:03:52,530 --> 01:03:54,570
Defeating the great evil requires
a sacrifice.

1600
01:03:54,570 --> 01:03:55,670
Right.

1601
01:03:56,130 --> 01:03:57,170
Well...

1602
01:03:57,300 --> 01:03:59,170
- I don't want any more wars.
- Me neither.

1603
01:03:59,370 --> 01:04:01,410
I'll try to convince my team members...

1604
01:04:01,410 --> 01:04:04,070
because you need the leader's consent
when you move to another team.

1605
01:04:04,440 --> 01:04:06,640
I'll make sure
at least two of you can move to our team.

1606
01:04:08,410 --> 01:04:09,480
Okay.

1607
01:04:10,310 --> 01:04:11,880
Let's just live in peace now.

1608
01:04:11,880 --> 01:04:13,450
Who would be happy about having a war?

1609
01:04:14,050 --> 01:04:15,390
- I would be happy if a war breaks out.
- A war...

1610
01:04:15,520 --> 01:04:18,090
War wears no merciful face.

1611
01:04:18,090 --> 01:04:20,420
But wars are inevitable in this game.

1612
01:04:21,130 --> 01:04:24,060
- Well... Isn't it a matter of choice?
- I think it's a matter of choice.

1613
01:04:24,960 --> 01:04:26,730
I believe it's inevitable.

1614
01:04:28,330 --> 01:04:29,700
At least for protection.

1615
01:04:30,530 --> 01:04:32,400
- We should keep him from talking.
- Protecting who?

1616
01:04:32,900 --> 01:04:33,940
Myself.

1617
01:04:33,940 --> 01:04:36,070
If I were to join Team Gold,

1618
01:04:36,670 --> 01:04:39,440
would you give me 100 gold pieces?

1619
01:04:40,110 --> 01:04:43,350
But the total number of gold pieces
we've issued is...

1620
01:04:43,350 --> 01:04:45,080
- Yes.
- only 200.

1621
01:04:45,550 --> 01:04:48,050
- I already know that.
- I see. But that can't be done.

1622
01:04:48,050 --> 01:04:49,290
- I see.
- Yes.

1623
01:04:49,490 --> 01:04:52,690
Be it someone from Team Red,
Team White, or any other team.

1624
01:04:52,860 --> 01:04:55,360
If you want to win over the casting vote,

1625
01:04:55,990 --> 01:04:57,390
I think you should consider...

1626
01:04:57,390 --> 01:05:01,000
making an exceptional offer,
like the one I suggested.

1627
01:05:01,200 --> 01:05:03,330
- You see, actually,
- Yes?

1628
01:05:03,870 --> 01:05:05,900
we can guarantee Team Red...

1629
01:05:05,900 --> 01:05:07,540
enough lives for two days.

1630
01:05:07,540 --> 01:05:09,110
Wouldn't that be...

1631
01:05:09,410 --> 01:05:11,280
the most exceptional offer?

1632
01:05:11,480 --> 01:05:12,540
- But...
- Yes?

1633
01:05:13,040 --> 01:05:14,910
- to me,
- Yes.

1634
01:05:14,910 --> 01:05:16,810
survival is not a very sweet offer.

1635
01:05:17,250 --> 01:05:19,950
We've been doing everything we can,

1636
01:05:20,150 --> 01:05:22,850
taking every single risk.

1637
01:05:22,850 --> 01:05:23,850
Right.

1638
01:05:23,850 --> 01:05:26,090
- So I want you to trust us.
- I understand.

1639
01:05:31,360 --> 01:05:32,930
- Can those members of Team Gold join us?
- Sure.

1640
01:05:33,300 --> 01:05:34,630
- Can we sit here?
- Please have a seat.

1641
01:05:34,630 --> 01:05:37,130
- I know it's just a game.
- Yes.

1642
01:05:37,130 --> 01:05:39,740
- But your attitude still matters.
- Yes.

1643
01:05:39,870 --> 01:05:42,470
- Team Black is our common enemy anyway.
- True.

1644
01:05:42,610 --> 01:05:45,080
We have to wrestle the control
away from Team Black.

1645
01:05:45,340 --> 01:05:46,740
I'll be honest with you.

1646
01:05:46,840 --> 01:05:48,310
Our role is
to keep the Community prosperous.

1647
01:05:48,380 --> 01:05:49,850
Meanwhile, Team Black plays a role...

1648
01:05:49,850 --> 01:05:51,750
that is destined
to draw criticisms from all residents.

1649
01:05:51,750 --> 01:05:53,150
And he's been deceiving us
this whole time.

1650
01:05:53,150 --> 01:05:56,190
But there has been
an information asymmetry.

1651
01:05:56,290 --> 01:05:58,560
- We thought Team Gold would attack us.
- Listen.

1652
01:05:58,560 --> 01:05:59,760
It was the exact opposite.

1653
01:05:59,760 --> 01:06:00,890
- Right. It was the exact opposite.
- Team Black...

1654
01:06:00,890 --> 01:06:02,360
- So...
- Black planted that seed in our minds.

1655
01:06:02,360 --> 01:06:05,260
We thought your team would start a war
this afternoon...

1656
01:06:05,260 --> 01:06:06,460
to attack us.

1657
01:06:06,630 --> 01:06:07,830
Through an alliance with Team Blue...

1658
01:06:07,830 --> 01:06:08,930
- Through an alliance.
- We thought there was a possibility...

1659
01:06:08,930 --> 01:06:10,070
you'd ally with Team Blue and attack us.

1660
01:06:10,070 --> 01:06:12,700
We did come up with such an idea
before we knew for sure.

1661
01:06:12,700 --> 01:06:15,940
Such thoughts like that were meaningless,

1662
01:06:15,940 --> 01:06:17,680
and that annoys me so much.

1663
01:06:18,840 --> 01:06:20,810
- We let him play us.
- Right.

1664
01:06:21,650 --> 01:06:23,050
Here's the root of the conflict.

1665
01:06:23,280 --> 01:06:25,850
It's very hard
for Team White and Team Gold...

1666
01:06:25,850 --> 01:06:28,120
- to coexist in a symbiotic relationship.
- In the end...

1667
01:06:28,120 --> 01:06:30,820
- Yes.
- But there's a way to minimize our risks.

1668
01:06:30,990 --> 01:06:32,890
- What is it?
- We leave one person on Team White.

1669
01:06:32,890 --> 01:06:34,690
- That person won't need to use lives.
- Yes.

1670
01:06:34,760 --> 01:06:36,960
- Then we move to Team Blue.
- Yes.

1671
01:06:36,960 --> 01:06:39,360
We just have to produce a few more lives.

1672
01:06:39,360 --> 01:06:40,530
After that,

1673
01:06:40,530 --> 01:06:42,230
- we only spend gold.
- Right.

1674
01:06:42,230 --> 01:06:43,400
We only divide the gold pieces.

1675
01:06:43,670 --> 01:06:45,970
- And we all vote for gold.
- Our votes...

1676
01:06:46,140 --> 01:06:47,500
Team Black has no gold.

1677
01:06:47,500 --> 01:06:48,970
- Then...
- Right. He has no gold.

1678
01:06:49,140 --> 01:06:50,140
And that's game over.

1679
01:06:50,140 --> 01:06:51,210
We can divide the gold pieces evenly...

1680
01:06:51,210 --> 01:06:53,110
- or find another way to divide them.
- We can decide later.

1681
01:06:53,110 --> 01:06:55,210
But let's put the split aside
for a moment.

1682
01:06:55,210 --> 01:06:58,120
The more people
that get a share of the prize, the better.

1683
01:06:58,120 --> 01:06:59,350
The bigger the prize money, the better.

1684
01:06:59,350 --> 01:07:01,250
It's possible
through the sacrifice of just one person.

1685
01:07:01,750 --> 01:07:04,020
I guess that's up to Team White.

1686
01:07:04,020 --> 01:07:05,720
- That's right.
- We've already discussed it.

1687
01:07:05,720 --> 01:07:07,660
And we need Team Gold
to give us a guarantee.

1688
01:07:07,660 --> 01:07:08,830
A guarantee about what?

1689
01:07:09,030 --> 01:07:10,560
- You could just issue more gold...
- I see.

1690
01:07:10,560 --> 01:07:12,130
- after the trade...
- Oh, I get it.

1691
01:07:12,130 --> 01:07:14,030
- to dilute the value of what we have.
- If we...

1692
01:07:14,030 --> 01:07:15,030
- Right.
- Earn our trust on that matter.

1693
01:07:15,030 --> 01:07:18,000
We haven't even thought
of doing something like that.

1694
01:07:18,000 --> 01:07:20,540
Of course, we'll guarantee you that
before moving forward.

1695
01:07:20,570 --> 01:07:21,870
However we're going
to split the prize money...

1696
01:07:21,870 --> 01:07:24,270
We can decide that later
while enjoying playing this game.

1697
01:07:24,270 --> 01:07:26,340
- I just don't want to waste it on wars.
- Me neither.

1698
01:07:26,340 --> 01:07:28,010
- We're all on the same page about that.
- Right.

1699
01:07:28,010 --> 01:07:29,310
Since we've all agreed...

1700
01:07:29,310 --> 01:07:30,580
- to end the wars,
- We've all agreed on that.

1701
01:07:30,580 --> 01:07:31,950
there's no need to discuss it any further.

1702
01:07:32,150 --> 01:07:33,350
- We're all on the same page about that.
- I understand.

1703
01:07:33,350 --> 01:07:34,350
I understand for now.

1704
01:07:34,350 --> 01:07:36,020
- We'll have to discuss...
- We'll discuss it among ourselves.

1705
01:07:36,020 --> 01:07:37,990
Go ahead.
I'll talk to the two ladies on our team.

1706
01:07:37,990 --> 01:07:39,060
You should...

1707
01:07:39,060 --> 01:07:40,490
Now that we have a common enemy,

1708
01:07:40,490 --> 01:07:43,130
Team Black's defeat is a done deal.

1709
01:07:43,490 --> 01:07:45,960
From that moment on, I focused...

1710
01:07:45,960 --> 01:07:48,630
on how to save
as many residents as possible.

1711
01:07:49,100 --> 01:07:51,670
That's when I began to feel a desire...

1712
01:07:51,670 --> 01:07:53,300
to save Team White.

1713
01:07:54,570 --> 01:07:56,440
- Did the talk go well?
- Yes.

1714
01:07:56,870 --> 01:08:00,040
First of all, Team White has no intention
of having wars.

1715
01:08:00,040 --> 01:08:01,080
I see.

1716
01:08:01,150 --> 01:08:03,350
- I'll leave the three of you alone.
- Okay.

1717
01:08:04,210 --> 01:08:07,220
They're on the same page as us.

1718
01:08:07,220 --> 01:08:09,320
They believe
that wars are meaningless now.

1719
01:08:09,320 --> 01:08:11,560
They're furious about how they've been
toyed with this whole time.

1720
01:08:11,560 --> 01:08:13,020
Our master plan is...

1721
01:08:13,590 --> 01:08:17,490
that except for Team Black, Team Blue,
and one sacrificed member of Team White,

1722
01:08:17,630 --> 01:08:18,960
every single resident survives.

1723
01:08:19,100 --> 01:08:20,600
We have enough lives.

1724
01:08:20,600 --> 01:08:24,230
We just have to divide the gold pieces.

1725
01:08:25,240 --> 01:08:27,570
I see
that you've been talking to Team White.

1726
01:08:27,570 --> 01:08:29,540
But the two of us think
it's better for us...

1727
01:08:29,540 --> 01:08:32,540
to avoid
talking to Team White and Team Blue.

1728
01:08:32,540 --> 01:08:34,310
- It would only provoke them...
- But...

1729
01:08:34,310 --> 01:08:37,280
That's not true.
I understand that you think...

1730
01:08:37,280 --> 01:08:39,450
I've grown emotionally attached
to Team White as a spy,

1731
01:08:39,450 --> 01:08:42,950
and that it might be
clouding my judgement.

1732
01:08:43,390 --> 01:08:47,190
But I'm telling you this
because I have Team White figured out...

1733
01:08:47,190 --> 01:08:49,630
- as much as Team Blue and Team Black.
- Okay.

1734
01:08:49,760 --> 01:08:51,400
Team White...

1735
01:08:51,400 --> 01:08:53,960
It's better if two of them come,
leaving just one person on their team.

1736
01:08:53,960 --> 01:08:55,470
- In the end...
- It's better if two of them come?

1737
01:08:55,470 --> 01:08:56,570
I mean, they'll switch teams to come.

1738
01:08:56,570 --> 01:08:57,700
- Where? They'll join our team?
- Where?

1739
01:08:57,700 --> 01:08:58,800
Team Gold or wherever.

1740
01:08:58,800 --> 01:08:59,940
I'm against that.

1741
01:08:59,940 --> 01:09:03,170
That'll decrease the amount we get.

1742
01:09:03,170 --> 01:09:05,580
If we don't receive that,

1743
01:09:05,580 --> 01:09:07,540
the chance of war will go up even more
in the end.

1744
01:09:08,480 --> 01:09:11,650
Luna, this is what I was worried about.

1745
01:09:11,650 --> 01:09:14,420
You're a pacifist
who wants to save everything.

1746
01:09:14,420 --> 01:09:16,990
- We're Team Gold.
- Right.

1747
01:09:16,990 --> 01:09:19,290
I don't want more team members.

1748
01:09:19,290 --> 01:09:22,560
I think it's more important
to keep the prize for ourselves.

1749
01:09:22,560 --> 01:09:24,860
- This is a game.
- I understand what you're saying.

1750
01:09:24,860 --> 01:09:27,060
Team White has three people.

1751
01:09:27,060 --> 01:09:28,500
Then it's one person each.

1752
01:09:28,500 --> 01:09:31,640
Getting just one person from Team Red...

1753
01:09:31,640 --> 01:09:34,670
can make it 6 against 6 at the end.

1754
01:09:34,670 --> 01:09:35,840
Why is it 6 against 6?

1755
01:09:35,840 --> 01:09:37,570
It's 8 against 5 right now.

1756
01:09:37,570 --> 01:09:40,180
I'm saying it'll be 6 against 6
excluding Vector.

1757
01:09:40,180 --> 01:09:41,780
I don't think it'll become 6 against 6.

1758
01:09:41,780 --> 01:09:45,080
I think if we keep up with this...

1759
01:09:45,080 --> 01:09:46,820
- If we get Team Red, we have eight.
- Yes.

1760
01:09:46,820 --> 01:09:48,890
Even including Black,
the game could end...

1761
01:09:48,890 --> 01:09:50,250
at 8 to 5.

1762
01:09:50,250 --> 01:09:53,720
If it becomes 8 against 5,
and those 5 start a war,

1763
01:09:53,720 --> 01:09:56,730
they'll buy weapons, even if we don't.

1764
01:09:56,730 --> 01:09:59,130
- That'll take away from the prize.
- Right.

1765
01:09:59,130 --> 01:10:01,530
We lost 100,000 dollars with one war.

1766
01:10:01,530 --> 01:10:05,300
Losing 100,000 dollars
and dividing the rest among the 8 of us...

1767
01:10:05,300 --> 01:10:06,970
is much less than
not losing 100,000 dollars...

1768
01:10:06,970 --> 01:10:08,070
and dividing it all among 10.

1769
01:10:08,410 --> 01:10:09,810
That's what I'm trying to say.

1770
01:10:09,810 --> 01:10:12,240
Black has been the common enemy.

1771
01:10:12,240 --> 01:10:15,450
But if we try to be greedy here,
Black will have all the power again.

1772
01:10:15,450 --> 01:10:17,780
So I'm saying it's best
to get rid of the war altogether...

1773
01:10:17,780 --> 01:10:19,820
and to start from there.

1774
01:10:19,820 --> 01:10:22,390
To get rid of Black,
we need to become one.

1775
01:10:22,520 --> 01:10:24,590
So this is a priority for me.

1776
01:10:24,590 --> 01:10:27,260
If we want to fight
over the prize after that,

1777
01:10:27,260 --> 01:10:28,860
we can play that game then.

1778
01:10:28,960 --> 01:10:30,790
- Right.
- She could be right.

1779
01:10:30,790 --> 01:10:33,630
We haven't experienced this before,

1780
01:10:33,630 --> 01:10:36,270
so we don't know how ugly people can get.

1781
01:10:36,270 --> 01:10:38,040
What do you think we were thinking...

1782
01:10:38,040 --> 01:10:40,770
about the prize of 100,000 dollars
when we started the war?

1783
01:10:40,770 --> 01:10:44,110
"If we lose here,
we won't get anything anyway,"

1784
01:10:44,110 --> 01:10:46,310
"so let's take 100,000 dollars
from everyone." That's what we said.

1785
01:10:46,640 --> 01:10:48,750
I think it's a top priority...

1786
01:10:48,750 --> 01:10:50,350
to create this peace.

1787
01:10:50,350 --> 01:10:52,080
We could also not receive it...

1788
01:10:52,080 --> 01:10:53,580
and have it go to Team Red.

1789
01:10:53,580 --> 01:10:55,220
Oh, what about this?

1790
01:10:55,220 --> 01:10:56,850
Persuade Team Blue somehow,

1791
01:10:56,850 --> 01:10:58,620
go to Team Blue,

1792
01:10:58,620 --> 01:11:00,360
and don't give Team Blue a life.

1793
01:11:03,290 --> 01:11:04,830
- Pitou's.
- That's a good idea.

1794
01:11:04,830 --> 01:11:06,000
- It's majority rule anyway.
- You're right.

1795
01:11:06,000 --> 01:11:07,500
Team White takes
the leader position again...

1796
01:11:07,500 --> 01:11:08,630
- You're right.
- and kill Team Blue.

1797
01:11:08,630 --> 01:11:10,470
That's better. Then...

1798
01:11:10,470 --> 01:11:11,970
- That'll be the start of peace.
- That'll bring us peace.

1799
01:11:11,970 --> 01:11:13,940
The currency will change to gold.

1800
01:11:13,940 --> 01:11:16,040
The five of us can keep our rights.

1801
01:11:16,040 --> 01:11:17,510
We can think of the share later.

1802
01:11:17,510 --> 01:11:18,510
That's it.

1803
01:11:18,510 --> 01:11:20,580
Can I bring Leia into this?

1804
01:11:20,740 --> 01:11:22,280
I don't know where Leia is right now.

1805
01:11:22,850 --> 01:11:24,280
Where are our teammates?

1806
01:11:24,550 --> 01:11:25,950
- Let's go and look for them.
- I'm not sure.

1807
01:11:27,180 --> 01:11:28,350
Where is everyone?

1808
01:11:29,450 --> 01:11:31,490
Have you eaten, Maillard?

1809
01:11:31,490 --> 01:11:32,690
Then do you want to talk?

1810
01:11:32,760 --> 01:11:33,860
Should we talk outside?

1811
01:11:33,920 --> 01:11:36,490
It was so funny in the beginning.
When we were guessing...

1812
01:11:36,990 --> 01:11:38,960
You know, that...

1813
01:11:43,930 --> 01:11:45,370
I first want to apologize.

1814
01:11:45,370 --> 01:11:47,440
- No, it's okay.
- I fully focused on my role.

1815
01:11:47,440 --> 01:11:48,710
- It doesn't matter.
- Okay.

1816
01:11:48,710 --> 01:11:50,740
I don't need an apology.

1817
01:11:50,740 --> 01:11:52,440
I think we were each playing our roles.

1818
01:11:53,110 --> 01:11:55,250
But regardless, both Team Red and I...

1819
01:11:55,250 --> 01:11:57,210
need to keep playing.

1820
01:11:57,210 --> 01:11:58,350
You're right.

1821
01:11:58,350 --> 01:12:00,050
I need to know the exact motivation.

1822
01:12:00,050 --> 01:12:01,650
- Especially...
- What motivation?

1823
01:12:01,750 --> 01:12:03,690
The people who deal mostly with diamonds,

1824
01:12:03,690 --> 01:12:05,420
Team Blue, Team Red, and Team White...

1825
01:12:06,320 --> 01:12:08,390
Were they not on your side?

1826
01:12:08,790 --> 01:12:10,160
I wasn't on anyone's side.

1827
01:12:12,500 --> 01:12:14,700
There's one thing I didn't understand.

1828
01:12:15,570 --> 01:12:18,200
Why did you open that to Paul?

1829
01:12:18,200 --> 01:12:20,140
I don't know what motivation you had
to do that.

1830
01:12:20,140 --> 01:12:23,540
I really don't understand,
so I want to know why.

1831
01:12:23,540 --> 01:12:25,080
Because I was working with White.

1832
01:12:25,580 --> 01:12:28,150
But White isn't planning to work with you.

1833
01:12:29,950 --> 01:12:32,120
There aren't any diamond players left.

1834
01:12:32,980 --> 01:12:35,490
Then what do they get by surrendering?

1835
01:12:36,750 --> 01:12:38,620
They want to bring you down, that's all.

1836
01:12:38,620 --> 01:12:41,430
I just really don't like
this sort of one-dimensional play.

1837
01:12:42,960 --> 01:12:44,090
I get that.

1838
01:12:45,900 --> 01:12:47,730
If we want to bring down Black,

1839
01:12:47,730 --> 01:12:49,530
we need to use gold, not diamonds.

1840
01:12:49,770 --> 01:12:53,570
(This morning, he heard
Team White's plans to move to Team Blue.)

1841
01:12:54,240 --> 01:12:57,170
If the diamond team forms an alliance,

1842
01:12:57,170 --> 01:12:58,410
I'll help them.

1843
01:12:59,340 --> 01:13:01,880
- But right now, Team Gold...
- Yes.

1844
01:13:03,280 --> 01:13:06,280
- already has five people.
- Right.

1845
01:13:06,280 --> 01:13:08,090
What are they talking about?

1846
01:13:08,450 --> 01:13:10,520
And if White...

1847
01:13:11,490 --> 01:13:13,820
- moves to another team,
- Yes.

1848
01:13:14,420 --> 01:13:15,730
there won't be any Team White players.

1849
01:13:15,830 --> 01:13:17,790
- Oh, they want to move over?
- Yes.

1850
01:13:17,860 --> 01:13:20,030
Then Team Gold will naturally win.

1851
01:13:20,230 --> 01:13:21,570
What?

1852
01:13:21,700 --> 01:13:23,930
What was that again?

1853
01:13:23,930 --> 01:13:25,370
Is White trying to move?

1854
01:13:25,870 --> 01:13:27,040
- Me?
- Yes.

1855
01:13:27,040 --> 01:13:28,840
He said you were moving to Team Gold.

1856
01:13:28,840 --> 01:13:29,940
- No.
- No.

1857
01:13:29,940 --> 01:13:31,210
You said you'd move to Team Blue.

1858
01:13:31,210 --> 01:13:32,510
- To Team Blue.
- To Team Blue.

1859
01:13:32,510 --> 01:13:34,680
I said I'd move to Team Blue earlier.

1860
01:13:35,050 --> 01:13:36,150
Maillard said...

1861
01:13:36,950 --> 01:13:39,450
White would bring me down.

1862
01:13:40,150 --> 01:13:41,690
- When?
- How? With what?

1863
01:13:41,690 --> 01:13:43,120
- I don't know.
- How? With what?

1864
01:13:43,120 --> 01:13:45,920
He said you'd give everything up,
move to Team Gold...

1865
01:13:45,920 --> 01:13:48,930
- I don't have that data.
- I don't know why he's saying that.

1866
01:13:49,190 --> 01:13:51,730
- Why is he playing like this?
- He said you'd get rid of me.

1867
01:13:52,560 --> 01:13:54,100
Because that's the best I have.

1868
01:13:54,100 --> 01:13:55,170
No.

1869
01:13:55,170 --> 01:13:56,730
You had no reason to say all that.

1870
01:13:56,730 --> 01:13:59,570
Look. I have nothing to gain here.

1871
01:14:00,440 --> 01:14:02,940
- No, you did, but...
- I'm just going to help the diamonds.

1872
01:14:02,940 --> 01:14:04,010
No, you had something to gain,

1873
01:14:04,010 --> 01:14:05,480
but you keep throwing it away.

1874
01:14:05,480 --> 01:14:08,380
- What are you talking about?
- Maillard, we want to talk.

1875
01:14:08,380 --> 01:14:10,480
I just don't understand what you're doing.

1876
01:14:10,480 --> 01:14:12,120
- I'm speechless.
- Just a second.

1877
01:14:12,250 --> 01:14:14,080
Let's talk for a second.

1878
01:14:14,080 --> 01:14:16,520
Black did things I couldn't understand.

1879
01:14:16,520 --> 01:14:18,690
Because Vector didn't protect Donkey,

1880
01:14:18,690 --> 01:14:20,190
they revealed everything.

1881
01:14:20,760 --> 01:14:23,330
So I couldn't protect my team.

1882
01:14:23,330 --> 01:14:25,400
He caused harm in a way.

1883
01:14:25,400 --> 01:14:28,670
Despite knowing all of that,

1884
01:14:28,930 --> 01:14:31,130
I thought we could form
a healthy alliance...

1885
01:14:31,130 --> 01:14:34,770
and all get on one boat together.

1886
01:14:34,770 --> 01:14:36,770
That's why I thought
I could talk to Black...

1887
01:14:36,770 --> 01:14:40,340
and move things forward in a positive way.

1888
01:14:40,780 --> 01:14:42,280
I need to know the exact motivation.

1889
01:14:42,280 --> 01:14:44,650
"So tell me what you're sure of."

1890
01:14:44,650 --> 01:14:46,850
"If you give me this information,
I'll get on one boat with you..."

1891
01:14:46,850 --> 01:14:47,920
"and go to the diamond side."

1892
01:14:47,920 --> 01:14:49,650
I was trying to make that deal with him,

1893
01:14:49,650 --> 01:14:51,290
but he didn't want to believe that.

1894
01:14:51,290 --> 01:14:54,360
Maillard said
Team White would bring me down.

1895
01:14:54,860 --> 01:14:57,460
He was just trying to escape by himself.

1896
01:14:57,460 --> 01:14:58,660
I hated that.

1897
01:14:58,660 --> 01:15:01,430
I no longer wanted to do anything
that was good for that punk.

1898
01:15:01,700 --> 01:15:04,130
He was all over the place.

1899
01:15:04,130 --> 01:15:05,340
That made me angry.

1900
01:15:05,340 --> 01:15:07,700
Then I went to Leia, Team White's leader.

1901
01:15:08,310 --> 01:15:11,510
When it comes down to it,
we went to war...

1902
01:15:11,510 --> 01:15:12,640
and lost 100,000 dollars.

1903
01:15:12,640 --> 01:15:14,680
To put it frankly.

1904
01:15:14,680 --> 01:15:16,110
So to be honest,

1905
01:15:16,110 --> 01:15:18,680
I don't want to be in this game
with Black.

1906
01:15:18,680 --> 01:15:21,650
My main premise is to prevent a war.

1907
01:15:21,650 --> 01:15:24,550
But Leia also expressed displeasure...

1908
01:15:24,550 --> 01:15:26,560
with her relationship with Black.

1909
01:15:26,560 --> 01:15:29,760
For that reason, I no longer wanted
to push more diamonds his way.

1910
01:15:29,760 --> 01:15:31,860
So I want them to go to Team Gold.

1911
01:15:31,860 --> 01:15:33,430
- Who?
- Everyone.

1912
01:15:33,660 --> 01:15:35,400
I want us to trade with gold.

1913
01:15:35,530 --> 01:15:38,070
- So...
- You want Team Gold to win, right?

1914
01:15:38,070 --> 01:15:39,170
Yes.

1915
01:15:39,170 --> 01:15:40,270
- Sounds good.
- Okay.

1916
01:15:40,270 --> 01:15:42,470
She said she'd also side with Team Gold...

1917
01:15:42,470 --> 01:15:45,480
through the relocation policy.

1918
01:15:45,940 --> 01:15:49,350
Make everyone choose Team Gold.

1919
01:15:49,350 --> 01:15:51,050
Right, if Team Gold wins,

1920
01:15:51,050 --> 01:15:52,820
- Black might not get any of the prize.
- Yes.

1921
01:15:52,920 --> 01:15:54,680
That's why I'm saying
we should go to Team Gold.

1922
01:15:54,750 --> 01:15:56,090
- Okay, I got it.
- Okay.

1923
01:15:56,090 --> 01:15:58,020
I felt that there were no longer...

1924
01:15:58,020 --> 01:16:02,160
any people who wanted to play
on the diamond side.

1925
01:16:02,160 --> 01:16:06,560
So I wanted to get closer to Team Gold.

1926
01:16:06,560 --> 01:16:09,730
So I'm planning to give them
all of my resources...

1927
01:16:09,730 --> 01:16:12,270
and relocate.

1928
01:16:12,270 --> 01:16:16,540
I'm going to move all resources, lives,
and credits...

1929
01:16:17,340 --> 01:16:19,240
to Team Gold.

1930
01:16:19,480 --> 01:16:21,040
I'm going to kill Donkey too.

1931
01:16:21,240 --> 01:16:22,510
- Why?
- Why Donkey?

1932
01:16:22,510 --> 01:16:23,750
Donkey...

1933
01:16:23,750 --> 01:16:25,920
- is a spy for Black.
- What?

1934
01:16:25,920 --> 01:16:27,420
He's a spy for Black.

1935
01:16:27,420 --> 01:16:28,690
- Really?
- Yes.

1936
01:16:28,690 --> 01:16:30,090
- I knew it too.
- Is this a fact?

1937
01:16:30,090 --> 01:16:33,390
- Yes, after productive activities today,
- Yes.

1938
01:16:33,390 --> 01:16:34,960
Donkey said so to me.

1939
01:16:34,960 --> 01:16:37,560
I thought Donkey sharing things with us...

1940
01:16:37,560 --> 01:16:39,560
- was okay.
- Right.

1941
01:16:39,560 --> 01:16:41,900
But Black shared this information...

1942
01:16:41,900 --> 01:16:43,430
with Paul.

1943
01:16:43,430 --> 01:16:46,340
As soon as you say that,
it'll spread throughout the community.

1944
01:16:46,340 --> 01:16:48,370
- Of course.
- There are no secrets.

1945
01:16:48,370 --> 01:16:50,110
- Right.
- From that point,

1946
01:16:50,110 --> 01:16:53,580
Team Red can no longer keep
Donkey among us.

1947
01:16:53,580 --> 01:16:56,950
If we keep him on our team...
knowing he's a collaborator,

1948
01:16:56,950 --> 01:16:59,350
Team White will lose trust in Team Red.

1949
01:17:00,280 --> 01:17:01,820
- Can I join?
- Yes, you can.

1950
01:17:02,320 --> 01:17:03,790
I told everyone you were a spy.

1951
01:17:04,420 --> 01:17:05,760
Vector did?

1952
01:17:05,760 --> 01:17:07,160
- I did.
- You did?

1953
01:17:07,390 --> 01:17:08,930
I thought everyone would find out anyway.

1954
01:17:10,160 --> 01:17:12,560
You and I know the code.

1955
01:17:12,660 --> 01:17:15,000
A code snipe is certain death anyway.

1956
01:17:15,000 --> 01:17:16,230
How do you know the code?

1957
01:17:17,130 --> 01:17:19,200
- I told him. I'm sorry.
- Okay.

1958
01:17:19,200 --> 01:17:20,900
- Stay in Team Red, Izaha.
- Okay.

1959
01:17:20,900 --> 01:17:22,910
Because you can't attack
the only person on a team.

1960
01:17:25,310 --> 01:17:26,510
If you switch to Team Gold,

1961
01:17:26,510 --> 01:17:28,910
we need to move to Team Gold too,
except one person, right?

1962
01:17:28,910 --> 01:17:29,950
Yes.

1963
01:17:30,410 --> 01:17:32,780
No, I don't want you to go.

1964
01:17:33,480 --> 01:17:35,490
I don't want to play this game
with this punk.

1965
01:17:36,120 --> 01:17:37,120
Got it.

1966
01:17:44,830 --> 01:17:46,700
I didn't feel betrayed or anything.

1967
01:17:46,700 --> 01:17:49,500
When I saw Donkey and how he was feeling,
I did feel bad.

1968
01:17:49,500 --> 01:17:51,470
Because Donkey didn't choose...

1969
01:17:51,470 --> 01:17:53,040
to be the spy.

1970
01:17:53,040 --> 01:17:55,170
I'm sure there were times...

1971
01:17:55,170 --> 01:17:58,980
he had to sell information to Black
because of his role.

1972
01:17:58,980 --> 01:18:01,710
"It must've been hard for Donkey."
That's what I thought.

1973
01:18:02,650 --> 01:18:04,850
How about we talk?

1974
01:18:04,850 --> 01:18:07,080
I thought of a good idea.

1975
01:18:07,080 --> 01:18:08,220
Okay.

1976
01:18:08,220 --> 01:18:12,360
We thought of a way for all of us to live.

1977
01:18:12,360 --> 01:18:15,260
First, I think it's important
for us to actively use...

1978
01:18:15,260 --> 01:18:16,890
- the relocation option.
- You're right. Yes.

1979
01:18:16,890 --> 01:18:18,190
So we want...

1980
01:18:18,630 --> 01:18:22,770
to propose that
Team White takes over Team Blue.

1981
01:18:23,230 --> 01:18:24,500
Take over?

1982
01:18:24,500 --> 01:18:27,440
Two of you can go and take the majority.

1983
01:18:27,440 --> 01:18:31,110
If you don't give Pitou a life,
Pitou will be eliminated.

1984
01:18:31,110 --> 01:18:33,680
Then we can control Team Blue.

1985
01:18:33,840 --> 01:18:35,210
If we do that,

1986
01:18:35,210 --> 01:18:37,410
we can make gold the new trading currency.

1987
01:18:37,410 --> 01:18:41,050
Then we want to share the gold
amongst all of us.

1988
01:18:41,050 --> 01:18:42,950
And there will be no war at all.

1989
01:18:42,950 --> 01:18:45,560
Where will we send Pitou, then?

1990
01:18:45,560 --> 01:18:46,960
- Home.
- Home.

1991
01:18:49,160 --> 01:18:51,090
She has to take responsibility
for war crimes.

1992
01:18:52,000 --> 01:18:53,700
- We're going to send her home?
- Yes.

1993
01:18:53,930 --> 01:18:55,270
That will only make...

1994
01:18:55,270 --> 01:18:56,400
Team White get...

1995
01:18:56,400 --> 01:18:59,100
- some amount of the prize money.
- So today,

1996
01:18:59,100 --> 01:19:01,170
- we'll send two people to Team Blue,
- Yes.

1997
01:19:01,170 --> 01:19:02,270
and make them change the leader...

1998
01:19:02,270 --> 01:19:03,370
- tomorrow morning.
- Right.

1999
01:19:03,670 --> 01:19:04,840
Okay. Then all of us can...

2000
01:19:04,840 --> 01:19:06,040
- at least survive.
- Right.

2001
01:19:06,040 --> 01:19:07,640
We need to think some more to decide...

2002
01:19:07,640 --> 01:19:09,510
- whether we'll send Pitou home or not.
- Okay.

2003
01:19:09,610 --> 01:19:11,750
Then for now, Team Gold...

2004
01:19:11,750 --> 01:19:13,420
won't have more members?

2005
01:19:13,420 --> 01:19:16,290
For the time being,
we'll keep this system of five people.

2006
01:19:16,290 --> 01:19:18,890
To be honest, forming an alliance...

2007
01:19:18,890 --> 01:19:20,790
will be safe for us.

2008
01:19:20,790 --> 01:19:22,760
You know,

2009
01:19:22,790 --> 01:19:24,730
I'm not sure
if this is the right expression,

2010
01:19:25,460 --> 01:19:27,260
you should send one hostage
somewhere else.

2011
01:19:27,260 --> 01:19:28,700
(You should send one hostage
somewhere else.)

2012
01:19:30,630 --> 01:19:32,540
This 5-3-3 arrangement...

2013
01:19:32,540 --> 01:19:34,940
might make people feel uneasy
since the transaction is still pending.

2014
01:19:35,040 --> 01:19:37,440
- Especially we...
- So what do you fear in the end?

2015
01:19:37,440 --> 01:19:40,440
You're afraid Team Gold takes everything
in the end, right?

2016
01:19:40,440 --> 01:19:41,480
Yes.

2017
01:19:41,480 --> 01:19:43,350
So you want to send one of us...

2018
01:19:43,350 --> 01:19:44,410
- to another team?
- Right.

2019
01:19:44,410 --> 01:19:45,520
As a hostage.

2020
01:19:47,650 --> 01:19:49,250
Then four of us can do it.

2021
01:19:49,550 --> 01:19:50,690
I mean, sending one person...

2022
01:19:50,690 --> 01:19:51,760
- won't make a hostage.
- It won't make a hostage.

2023
01:19:51,760 --> 01:19:52,960
Then send two away.

2024
01:19:53,160 --> 01:19:54,190
No.

2025
01:19:54,190 --> 01:19:56,230
Do you have doubts?

2026
01:19:56,490 --> 01:19:57,530
If you're suspicious,

2027
01:19:57,530 --> 01:19:59,360
- you need to start with five people.
- She's right.

2028
01:19:59,360 --> 01:20:01,970
That's why we're asking this.

2029
01:20:02,070 --> 01:20:04,800
- We can't take all the risks.
- We can't...

2030
01:20:04,800 --> 01:20:06,640
- We can't do that.
- We can't.

2031
01:20:06,770 --> 01:20:08,570
I have a feeling...

2032
01:20:08,570 --> 01:20:10,970
that we're taking advantage
of Luna's position.

2033
01:20:10,970 --> 01:20:13,740
We're making even Team White
use our gold...

2034
01:20:13,740 --> 01:20:14,880
- For the time being.
- for now.

2035
01:20:14,880 --> 01:20:17,510
We will successfully roll out gold...

2036
01:20:17,510 --> 01:20:21,180
and only we
who have the actual right to issue it...

2037
01:20:21,180 --> 01:20:24,490
will be able to get a large amount
of prize money.

2038
01:20:24,650 --> 01:20:27,960
That's a reasonable choice we can make.

2039
01:20:27,960 --> 01:20:29,530
But honestly,

2040
01:20:29,530 --> 01:20:31,490
we can't openly say it to everyone...

2041
01:20:31,490 --> 01:20:34,230
because I don't want our plan to leak.

2042
01:20:34,230 --> 01:20:38,270
From Luna's position, she said it
as a strategy for Team White to survive,

2043
01:20:38,270 --> 01:20:40,770
but I don't agree...

2044
01:20:40,770 --> 01:20:41,940
to that method.

2045
01:20:42,070 --> 01:20:43,670
- My plan is simple.
- Yes.

2046
01:20:43,670 --> 01:20:46,710
I think there's a possibility...

2047
01:20:46,710 --> 01:20:49,080
that 5 of us can unite as 1.

2048
01:20:49,080 --> 01:20:52,980
We cannot rescue
both Team White and Team Red...

2049
01:20:52,980 --> 01:20:54,650
and distribute things equally.

2050
01:20:54,650 --> 01:20:57,790
So in the end, the thing is,
what our priority is.

2051
01:20:57,820 --> 01:20:58,890
I think it should be Team Red.

2052
01:20:58,890 --> 01:21:01,290
- That has been our stance so far.
- Right.

2053
01:21:01,290 --> 01:21:03,090
But now, since Luna and Team White...

2054
01:21:03,090 --> 01:21:04,490
- came up with a good proposal,
- Yes.

2055
01:21:04,490 --> 01:21:05,930
- I got swayed all of a sudden.
- I see.

2056
01:21:05,930 --> 01:21:07,360
But I don't want to go in that direction.

2057
01:21:07,530 --> 01:21:09,570
- Luna needs to understand that, as I see.
- Okay.

2058
01:21:09,700 --> 01:21:11,940
I can see Luna wants
to protect Team White.

2059
01:21:11,940 --> 01:21:13,240
I don't know. Now it's...

2060
01:21:26,680 --> 01:21:30,450
The weapon dealer should set
today's war cost and the weapon cost...

2061
01:21:30,450 --> 01:21:35,120
by the number of diamonds and gold each.

2062
01:21:39,830 --> 01:21:41,560
The war cost will be zero diamonds...

2063
01:21:41,560 --> 01:21:43,130
and 200 items of gold.

2064
01:21:45,300 --> 01:21:47,770
The war cost has been set.

2065
01:21:48,670 --> 01:21:51,370
Please set the weapon cost.

2066
01:22:05,960 --> 01:22:08,120
The number of diamonds will be set
in the order of weapons A, B, and C.

2067
01:22:08,120 --> 01:22:10,030
It will be 90, 70, and 40.

2068
01:22:12,000 --> 01:22:13,830
(Today's war cost is
0 diamonds and 200 gold pieces.)

2069
01:22:15,100 --> 01:22:17,330
Based on gold, the cost
of the weapons A, B, and C each...

2070
01:22:17,870 --> 01:22:19,600
will be set at ten quintillion pieces.

2071
01:22:23,840 --> 01:22:28,040
Both the war cost and the weapon cost
have been set.

2072
01:22:28,040 --> 01:22:31,410
Now, you may leave the Community Center.

2073
01:22:31,710 --> 01:22:32,820
Thank you.

2074
01:22:33,750 --> 01:22:36,490
To show that I favor teams
with diamonds far more,

2075
01:22:36,490 --> 01:22:39,220
I set the number of diamonds to 0
and gold pieces to 200.

2076
01:22:39,220 --> 01:22:40,590
Zero and two hundred...

2077
01:22:40,590 --> 01:22:41,930
shows a clear difference.

2078
01:22:41,930 --> 01:22:44,730
I set the costs like that for show.

2079
01:22:44,730 --> 01:22:45,730
When a war breaks out,

2080
01:22:45,730 --> 01:22:48,400
the situation should be advantageous
for the diamond team.

2081
01:22:48,400 --> 01:22:52,340
So, for the diamond team,
I set a reasonable cost for weapons.

2082
01:22:52,400 --> 01:22:57,070
And I set a price that's completely
out of reach by gold pieces,

2083
01:22:57,070 --> 01:22:59,440
so that they won't be able to buy weapons.
That was my goal.

2084
01:22:59,840 --> 01:23:01,380
- You want me to walk the walk.
- Walk the walk.

2085
01:23:01,380 --> 01:23:03,150
- I understood that. Okay.
- Okay.

2086
01:23:03,450 --> 01:23:05,280
It's about resource distribution...

2087
01:23:05,280 --> 01:23:06,380
- Okay.
- for exchange.

2088
01:23:06,380 --> 01:23:07,680
- I forgot. We need to make a trade.
- We need to trade.

2089
01:23:07,680 --> 01:23:10,720
The trading for Day Six will begin.

2090
01:23:10,990 --> 01:23:15,460
Currently, the Community Town Platform's
official resource is diamonds.

2091
01:23:15,730 --> 01:23:18,900
You cannot use gold on the Platform.

2092
01:23:19,160 --> 01:23:21,730
However, if you trade using gold,

2093
01:23:21,730 --> 01:23:25,070
you can use the Trading Station.

2094
01:23:25,540 --> 01:23:27,240
Today's war cost...

2095
01:23:27,240 --> 01:23:28,570
- Wait.
- Wait!

2096
01:23:29,340 --> 01:23:31,170
are zero diamonds...

2097
01:23:31,540 --> 01:23:33,810
and 200 gold pieces.

2098
01:23:33,910 --> 01:23:37,110
She says 0 diamonds
and 200 gold pieces for the war cost.

2099
01:23:37,450 --> 01:23:38,610
Why would anybody wage a war?

2100
01:23:39,280 --> 01:23:41,320
They're making a joke.

2101
01:23:41,320 --> 01:23:43,220
- Tell them to get lost.
- Tell them to get lost, seriously.

2102
01:23:43,220 --> 01:23:44,590
That's crazy. We need to spend 200 pieces.

2103
01:23:44,650 --> 01:23:46,760
The leader of a team
that wants to wage a war...

2104
01:23:46,760 --> 01:23:49,860
should visit Community Center
during the trading hours...

2105
01:23:49,860 --> 01:23:52,200
and declare war.

2106
01:23:52,930 --> 01:23:55,570
This concludes the announcement
from Community Center.

2107
01:24:12,720 --> 01:24:13,980
Are you going for a trade?

2108
01:24:14,650 --> 01:24:16,050
Yes, I want to end the game.

2109
01:24:22,490 --> 01:24:24,030
Just have a talk with me, and go.

2110
01:24:27,500 --> 01:24:28,600
What should we do?

2111
01:24:30,200 --> 01:24:31,630
- I will go to Team Gold.
- Okay.

2112
01:24:31,630 --> 01:24:32,940
Then when they snipe,

2113
01:24:32,940 --> 01:24:34,870
I might die, but you can survive.

2114
01:24:34,870 --> 01:24:36,570
So are you going to move today?

2115
01:24:36,570 --> 01:24:37,610
- No.
- Okay.

2116
01:24:37,610 --> 01:24:39,110
- I can't go today.
- Okay.

2117
01:24:39,380 --> 01:24:40,680
I need to kill Donkey before I go.

2118
01:24:40,680 --> 01:24:42,850
- All right. You can go tomorrow.
- Okay.

2119
01:24:42,850 --> 01:24:44,780
How many of each item should I leave?

2120
01:24:45,180 --> 01:24:47,350
I'm not sure about diamonds.
How about 100?

2121
01:24:47,350 --> 01:24:48,580
- A 100 diamonds?
- Yes.

2122
01:24:48,890 --> 01:24:51,490
We're going to produce credits tomorrow.

2123
01:24:51,490 --> 01:24:54,260
So 10 at most will be enough.

2124
01:24:54,490 --> 01:24:56,660
- Let's make it 15.
- Okay.

2125
01:24:58,260 --> 01:25:00,200
- Now, life...
- You don't need it.

2126
01:25:00,200 --> 01:25:01,560
Starting tomorrow, I don't need it.

2127
01:25:01,600 --> 01:25:03,000
- I need it only for today.
- Today, anyway...

2128
01:25:03,000 --> 01:25:04,500
- I only need two.
- Right.

2129
01:25:04,500 --> 01:25:05,740
From tomorrow, I don't need it.

2130
01:25:06,570 --> 01:25:08,270
- Isn't it trading hours now?
- What?

2131
01:25:08,340 --> 01:25:09,670
Isn't it trading hours now?

2132
01:25:16,750 --> 01:25:18,050
The war cost... I see.

2133
01:25:18,050 --> 01:25:20,220
We won't be able to wage a war using gold.

2134
01:25:21,250 --> 01:25:22,390
Darn it.

2135
01:25:23,990 --> 01:25:25,990
I guess all the gold is at Hub.

2136
01:25:26,390 --> 01:25:28,990
I'll wait here.
Please bring the leader of Team Gold.

2137
01:25:28,990 --> 01:25:30,190
- I'll go find him.
- Okay.

2138
01:25:32,230 --> 01:25:35,000
All right. I'll stand one more day
to harass you...

2139
01:25:35,000 --> 01:25:36,270
and die by a gunshot.

2140
01:25:36,330 --> 01:25:38,400
I wanted to take Donkey with me,
but I don't think I can.

2141
01:25:38,900 --> 01:25:40,070
It's too dangerous.

2142
01:25:42,170 --> 01:25:43,810
I think we need to go up there
for a while.

2143
01:25:43,810 --> 01:25:45,580
- Let's go and talk in the room.
- Let's go.

2144
01:25:45,780 --> 01:25:47,280
Can we talk here?

2145
01:25:47,440 --> 01:25:49,050
Aren't we making a trade with Team Red?

2146
01:25:49,050 --> 01:25:52,120
We need to talk first to trade.

2147
01:25:52,420 --> 01:25:53,550
Team Gold!

2148
01:25:53,550 --> 01:25:55,220
- We...
- Let's trade!

2149
01:25:55,590 --> 01:25:58,520
Wait. We need to talk
among ourselves first.

2150
01:25:58,520 --> 01:26:00,560
Will you talk? We'll wait
at the Community Center.

2151
01:26:00,560 --> 01:26:02,830
- We still have time.
- We haven't discussed it yet.

2152
01:26:02,830 --> 01:26:04,090
- We'll sort it out and talk to you.
- Okay. Go ahead.

2153
01:26:04,090 --> 01:26:05,430
- We'll be there soon.
- I'll wait at the Community Center.

2154
01:26:10,500 --> 01:26:12,800
Did things go as he said earlier?

2155
01:26:12,800 --> 01:26:14,200
First of all, Donkey will leave today.

2156
01:26:14,240 --> 01:26:15,640
- Leave?
- Yes.

2157
01:26:15,640 --> 01:26:18,810
I'm leaving, anyway,

2158
01:26:18,810 --> 01:26:20,880
- because I'm on Vector's side, right?
- Right.

2159
01:26:20,880 --> 01:26:22,380
- I'm sorry.
- No, it's fine.

2160
01:26:22,480 --> 01:26:23,780
Isn't Team Gold's leader coming?

2161
01:26:23,780 --> 01:26:25,180
He'll come with resources.

2162
01:26:25,480 --> 01:26:28,480
I guess it takes time
since they need to talk among themselves.

2163
01:26:29,120 --> 01:26:31,650
- They can't go on like this. Come on!
- Okay.

2164
01:26:32,190 --> 01:26:33,660
- Right.
- Tell him to hurry!

2165
01:26:33,660 --> 01:26:34,890
I got it.

2166
01:26:35,160 --> 01:26:37,960
Team Gold is so naive.

2167
01:26:39,830 --> 01:26:41,930
They have no idea
what this war cost means.

2168
01:26:43,070 --> 01:26:45,200
As soon as the trading hour started,

2169
01:26:45,200 --> 01:26:47,440
the war cost was shown.

2170
01:26:47,440 --> 01:26:50,440
It was set at 0 diamonds
and 200 gold pieces.

2171
01:26:50,440 --> 01:26:52,010
Zero diamonds means...

2172
01:26:52,010 --> 01:26:54,880
that a war can be waged at random.

2173
01:26:54,880 --> 01:26:59,420
If just one leader of the teams
that joined Black...

2174
01:26:59,420 --> 01:27:01,180
declares war,

2175
01:27:01,180 --> 01:27:04,120
the process of building trust
with Team Gold...

2176
01:27:04,120 --> 01:27:05,860
will break down.

2177
01:27:05,860 --> 01:27:08,620
So, I was standing at the entrance
of the Community Center...

2178
01:27:08,620 --> 01:27:11,560
so that other leaders can't enter.

2179
01:27:11,960 --> 01:27:15,570
Team Red and Team White
want to join Team Gold.

2180
01:27:15,570 --> 01:27:17,670
- They want to join Team Gold?
- Yes. They want to join us.

2181
01:27:17,830 --> 01:27:20,700
However, we told them
it's not easy to do so.

2182
01:27:20,700 --> 01:27:22,610
We can consider Team Gold
has citizenship...

2183
01:27:22,610 --> 01:27:25,980
and Team Red and Team Blue have residency.

2184
01:27:26,080 --> 01:27:28,510
In that case, how would you
distribute things?

2185
01:27:28,510 --> 01:27:29,510
We haven't decided yet.

2186
01:27:29,510 --> 01:27:31,510
- We need to decide from now on.
- We need to decide.

2187
01:27:31,510 --> 01:27:35,150
However, since the total amount of gold
is made public in transparent manner,

2188
01:27:35,150 --> 01:27:36,550
it's not a bad idea...

2189
01:27:36,550 --> 01:27:38,250
that we say, "You can request anything."

2190
01:27:38,650 --> 01:27:40,720
This is how I feel.

2191
01:27:40,720 --> 01:27:41,990
I think it's a very good strategy.

2192
01:27:41,990 --> 01:27:45,060
But Team White needs
to make a decision on one matter.

2193
01:27:45,060 --> 01:27:46,500
They need to make some sacrifices.

2194
01:27:46,500 --> 01:27:49,200
- They said they'll take care of it.
- They're ready to take the hit.

2195
01:27:49,200 --> 01:27:52,570
In other respects, it's pretty possible...

2196
01:27:55,070 --> 01:27:57,770
In case even one person is enticed
and a war is declared,

2197
01:27:57,840 --> 01:27:59,340
the trading won't happen.

2198
01:28:02,980 --> 01:28:04,710
How are things going?

2199
01:28:05,720 --> 01:28:06,880
What is it, Blue?

2200
01:28:07,350 --> 01:28:08,750
- Excuse me?
- What is it?

2201
01:28:08,990 --> 01:28:10,090
You don't know what to do?

2202
01:28:10,090 --> 01:28:11,920
- No. Just in case...
- What is it, Blue?

2203
01:28:11,920 --> 01:28:13,390
Don't let her come in here.

2204
01:28:14,790 --> 01:28:15,960
Why?

2205
01:28:15,990 --> 01:28:17,330
No. Now I'm...

2206
01:28:17,330 --> 01:28:18,860
- concerned about something.
- I see.

2207
01:28:19,830 --> 01:28:20,830
He says he's concerned about something.

2208
01:28:20,830 --> 01:28:22,160
Tell Team Gold's leader to hurry...

2209
01:28:22,160 --> 01:28:23,330
if they want to survive.

2210
01:28:23,330 --> 01:28:24,770
- Okay.
- Who should come here?

2211
01:28:24,770 --> 01:28:26,540
Team Gold. Wait a minute.

2212
01:28:27,000 --> 01:28:29,410
- Let's go. We'd better go somewhere else.
- Okay.

2213
01:28:30,210 --> 01:28:32,040
What's going on, all of a sudden?

2214
01:28:40,550 --> 01:28:43,490
If one of us leaves,

2215
01:28:43,490 --> 01:28:46,060
we might have
to give that team a lot of gold...

2216
01:28:46,060 --> 01:28:48,520
- to show that we're on the same side.
- Yes.

2217
01:28:48,520 --> 01:28:49,530
- So...
- But...

2218
01:28:49,530 --> 01:28:52,360
that's already impossible...

2219
01:28:52,360 --> 01:28:54,030
because do you seriously think
Pitou will accept us?

2220
01:28:54,030 --> 01:28:55,730
We can go after Pitou leaves.

2221
01:28:57,530 --> 01:28:58,770
- What?
- It's Team Red.

2222
01:28:58,770 --> 01:29:00,200
- It's Team Red.
- They're here.

2223
01:29:00,300 --> 01:29:02,840
- Hello.
- Hi, do you need more time to discuss?

2224
01:29:02,840 --> 01:29:04,470
Maybe five more minutes?

2225
01:29:04,470 --> 01:29:06,080
- Can you hurry up? We're in a rush.
- Okay.

2226
01:29:06,080 --> 01:29:07,280
- I'll be waiting.
- Okay.

2227
01:29:08,140 --> 01:29:09,980
Why does he keep rushing us?

2228
01:29:09,980 --> 01:29:11,780
Because we haven't said anything,

2229
01:29:11,780 --> 01:29:13,280
they think we've changed our minds.

2230
01:29:13,280 --> 01:29:14,820
So let's make a trade first.

2231
01:29:14,820 --> 01:29:16,620
- I think we can give them a lot of gold.
- No, wait.

2232
01:29:16,620 --> 01:29:18,190
Let me just say this.

2233
01:29:18,190 --> 01:29:19,620
You all have great ideas.

2234
01:29:19,620 --> 01:29:22,660
But what's very regrettable is,

2235
01:29:23,030 --> 01:29:24,460
when we come up with a strategy,

2236
01:29:24,460 --> 01:29:26,960
we agree on one by the morning.

2237
01:29:26,960 --> 01:29:29,630
But if you rush us to do it...

2238
01:29:29,630 --> 01:29:31,170
- But we already have a plan.
- No.

2239
01:29:31,170 --> 01:29:32,670
That's not how it should be done.

2240
01:29:32,670 --> 01:29:34,040
We must...

2241
01:29:34,040 --> 01:29:35,500
- take the lead and win.
- True.

2242
01:29:35,500 --> 01:29:39,080
To make that happen,
we should talk about it first...

2243
01:29:39,080 --> 01:29:41,410
- because information always leaks.
- Right.

2244
01:29:41,410 --> 01:29:43,080
And once it's finalized,

2245
01:29:43,080 --> 01:29:45,250
we can carry out the plan
within our boundary...

2246
01:29:45,250 --> 01:29:47,420
and come back to talk about it again.

2247
01:29:47,420 --> 01:29:50,390
We don't want
to hurt each other's feelings.

2248
01:29:53,490 --> 01:29:54,490
- So...
- What I'm saying is...

2249
01:29:54,490 --> 01:29:56,490
- Let's work on the details first.
- Firstly...

2250
01:29:56,490 --> 01:29:58,330
- There are people waiting outside.
- Okay.

2251
01:29:58,330 --> 01:30:00,030
- We can...
- Let's decide the trade ratio.

2252
01:30:00,030 --> 01:30:01,100
- Yes.
- Let's decide...

2253
01:30:01,100 --> 01:30:02,230
- the trade ratio first.
- First,

2254
01:30:02,230 --> 01:30:03,730
- First...
- we need credits.

2255
01:30:03,730 --> 01:30:04,730
Credits?

2256
01:30:04,970 --> 01:30:07,270
Team Gold's leader is too naive.

2257
01:30:07,270 --> 01:30:09,540
If you don't get here now, you're doomed.

2258
01:30:11,270 --> 01:30:13,040
They've never seen the war before.

2259
01:30:13,040 --> 01:30:15,040
They have no idea
how brutal this place is.

2260
01:30:15,680 --> 01:30:16,880
What's there to discuss?

2261
01:30:16,880 --> 01:30:19,480
If they attack first,
you can't make any trades.

2262
01:30:21,280 --> 01:30:23,850
I was at risk.

2263
01:30:23,850 --> 01:30:25,020
Because...

2264
01:30:25,020 --> 01:30:26,720
it's a volatile situation,

2265
01:30:26,720 --> 01:30:28,360
but Team Gold is too slow.

2266
01:30:28,620 --> 01:30:31,090
In a situation like this,

2267
01:30:31,090 --> 01:30:32,530
taking too long to make a decision
puts them at a serious disadvantage.

2268
01:30:32,530 --> 01:30:33,960
It was very frustrating.

2269
01:30:44,970 --> 01:30:46,410
Have you heard?

2270
01:30:46,410 --> 01:30:48,380
No, I don't know the exact story.

2271
01:30:48,380 --> 01:30:49,480
But...

2272
01:30:49,680 --> 01:30:50,710
I saw everyone taking it,

2273
01:30:50,710 --> 01:30:52,950
- so I took it just in case.
- Okay. Then wait here.

2274
01:30:53,180 --> 01:30:54,820
There might be a trade.

2275
01:30:55,650 --> 01:30:56,890
With Team Gold?

2276
01:30:56,890 --> 01:30:58,420
Team Gold...

2277
01:30:58,420 --> 01:31:00,490
We'll have to keep trading
with Team Gold anyway.

2278
01:31:00,490 --> 01:31:01,690
We'll also do the distribution.

2279
01:31:02,290 --> 01:31:03,460
Why do that with Team Gold?

2280
01:31:04,490 --> 01:31:06,330
- What do you mean?
- What?

2281
01:31:06,330 --> 01:31:07,560
You said you were going to trade
with Team Gold.

2282
01:31:07,560 --> 01:31:08,760
- No.
- Can't we?

2283
01:31:09,730 --> 01:31:11,030
Do you want to?

2284
01:31:11,470 --> 01:31:12,470
It's our choice.

2285
01:31:13,670 --> 01:31:16,240
Why are you all angry?

2286
01:31:16,570 --> 01:31:18,410
- Are you angry? I get it.
- So...

2287
01:31:18,410 --> 01:31:20,210
- I'm angry at the role.
- You can't help it.

2288
01:31:20,210 --> 01:31:21,410
- And...
- It makes sense why you're angry at me.

2289
01:31:21,410 --> 01:31:22,950
No, I'm angry at the role.

2290
01:31:22,950 --> 01:31:24,480
I'm not angry at you individually.

2291
01:31:24,480 --> 01:31:27,480
I'm not in a situation...

2292
01:31:27,480 --> 01:31:31,190
where I can talk to someone with that role
right now.

2293
01:31:31,190 --> 01:31:32,690
- I understand.
- Yes.

2294
01:31:34,190 --> 01:31:36,490
Are you trying to trade gold
with Team Gold?

2295
01:31:36,490 --> 01:31:39,090
- Yes.
- Do you agree...

2296
01:31:39,090 --> 01:31:41,430
- with what we talked about earlier?
- Yes.

2297
01:31:41,430 --> 01:31:43,030
That's what we're going to do.

2298
01:31:43,030 --> 01:31:44,370
- Stop here.
- Stop?

2299
01:31:44,370 --> 01:31:46,140
Because we think...

2300
01:31:46,140 --> 01:31:47,900
- war might declare when we go in.
- We can talk here.

2301
01:31:47,900 --> 01:31:49,210
- Me? I'm not going in.
- Yes.

2302
01:31:49,210 --> 01:31:50,970
- I know you're not going in.
- We're against the war.

2303
01:31:50,970 --> 01:31:52,110
- Who?
- Me too.

2304
01:31:53,880 --> 01:31:54,940
Team Blue.

2305
01:31:55,780 --> 01:31:58,380
- Did Team Blue say that?
- Team Blue and Leia.

2306
01:31:59,380 --> 01:32:00,580
Did I say I was going to start a war?

2307
01:32:01,720 --> 01:32:02,790
For now.

2308
01:32:03,490 --> 01:32:05,520
I'm siding with Team Gold.

2309
01:32:05,520 --> 01:32:06,720
- Are you?
- Yes.

2310
01:32:07,690 --> 01:32:09,060
Are you going to play with gold or not?

2311
01:32:09,060 --> 01:32:10,960
- Let's do that.
- Okay.

2312
01:32:11,190 --> 01:32:12,390
Let's play with gold,

2313
01:32:12,390 --> 01:32:14,500
- and I plan to relocate my team.
- Okay.

2314
01:32:14,830 --> 01:32:16,100
I'm going to remain then.

2315
01:32:16,100 --> 01:32:17,270
That's up to you to decide.

2316
01:32:17,270 --> 01:32:18,270
Okay.

2317
01:32:19,070 --> 01:32:20,900
Are they all taking sides with Team Gold?

2318
01:32:21,070 --> 01:32:22,440
It looks like it.

2319
01:32:22,440 --> 01:32:24,170
But if Team White chooses the gold,

2320
01:32:24,170 --> 01:32:25,410
- they have nothing to gain.
- So they're all transferring...

2321
01:32:25,410 --> 01:32:26,940
except one.

2322
01:32:26,940 --> 01:32:28,180
That person's giving up on the prize?

2323
01:32:28,180 --> 01:32:29,180
Yes.

2324
01:32:29,580 --> 01:32:30,980
Did they tell you to bring this?

2325
01:32:30,980 --> 01:32:32,150
Did they tell you to side with Team Gold
if you want to survive?

2326
01:32:32,150 --> 01:32:33,150
But I'm not sure...

2327
01:32:33,450 --> 01:32:35,450
if they're letting me in.

2328
01:32:35,450 --> 01:32:37,950
The truth is, they don't need you.

2329
01:32:38,190 --> 01:32:39,190
No.

2330
01:32:40,690 --> 01:32:43,030
But if they all transfer to Team Gold,

2331
01:32:43,890 --> 01:32:46,760
you need to know that I have no choice
but to side with them.

2332
01:32:46,760 --> 01:32:48,200
Yes. Of course.

2333
01:32:49,060 --> 01:32:51,430
I'm going to do whatever it takes
for me to survive.

2334
01:32:51,430 --> 01:32:52,430
I agree.

2335
01:32:52,570 --> 01:32:53,900
- And...
- Anyway, why are you selling diamonds?

2336
01:32:53,900 --> 01:32:55,100
Do they need diamonds?

2337
01:32:55,100 --> 01:32:57,370
I brought them for no reason.

2338
01:32:57,870 --> 01:32:59,170
For real. I just brought them.

2339
01:32:59,940 --> 01:33:01,780
It'd be nice to keep the diamonds.

2340
01:33:02,850 --> 01:33:05,310
The spy in Team Blue might be Pitou.

2341
01:33:07,580 --> 01:33:09,950
If she starts a war inside,
we can't make any trades.

2342
01:33:10,450 --> 01:33:11,520
Make sure she doesn't come in.

2343
01:33:11,920 --> 01:33:13,390
I'll stay here, but...

2344
01:33:17,960 --> 01:33:19,130
That's it for now.

2345
01:33:19,130 --> 01:33:21,860
- Okay. Let's start with the bigger cause.
- Yes.

2346
01:33:22,260 --> 01:33:23,270
I'm leaving.

2347
01:33:24,600 --> 01:33:27,040
- Do you want to talk together?
- Wait. Leia.

2348
01:33:27,040 --> 01:33:30,210
- Hold on.
- Can someone explain to me...

2349
01:33:30,210 --> 01:33:32,640
what's going on?

2350
01:33:32,640 --> 01:33:35,340
Are you saying that because you're worried
I might side with them?

2351
01:33:35,950 --> 01:33:37,810
No, you're not the variable right now.

2352
01:33:38,150 --> 01:33:40,480
I said the same thing to Vector.

2353
01:33:40,480 --> 01:33:42,720
I'm going to go with the majority
regardless of who that is.

2354
01:33:42,720 --> 01:33:45,050
- Okay.
- But if you don't tell me the outcome,

2355
01:33:45,050 --> 01:33:47,020
I wouldn't know what to do with these.

2356
01:33:47,020 --> 01:33:50,190
I don't know what the final decision is
going to be yet.

2357
01:33:50,190 --> 01:33:51,630
There are so many variables,

2358
01:33:51,630 --> 01:33:52,660
and other teams can also be variables.

2359
01:33:52,660 --> 01:33:54,160
So I'll tell you my plan first.

2360
01:33:54,160 --> 01:33:56,730
I was planning to send these two
to your team.

2361
01:33:57,270 --> 01:33:59,100
That's my plan for now.

2362
01:33:59,100 --> 01:34:00,470
- For now?
- Yes.

2363
01:34:01,470 --> 01:34:03,110
But he's saying otherwise.

2364
01:34:03,110 --> 01:34:05,540
He can't afford to care about us.

2365
01:34:05,540 --> 01:34:07,610
He has to make a decision
with his team first.

2366
01:34:08,340 --> 01:34:09,680
I'm going to rest now.

2367
01:34:09,680 --> 01:34:12,010
If you have anything to say,
tell me at once.

2368
01:34:26,000 --> 01:34:28,830
Two hours into the trading session.

2369
01:34:29,500 --> 01:34:31,700
- Let's start with 45 1st.
- We'll start from there.

2370
01:34:31,700 --> 01:34:33,900
- Or go less?
- We'll go as low as possible.

2371
01:34:33,900 --> 01:34:35,540
But I already said 15.

2372
01:34:35,540 --> 01:34:38,370
We can't go any lower
than what we said yesterday.

2373
01:34:38,370 --> 01:34:39,640
- Right.
- They'll be upset.

2374
01:34:39,640 --> 01:34:41,140
- But I think...
- That will make them upset.

2375
01:34:41,140 --> 01:34:42,650
- Keep that in here.
- the number of gold right now..

2376
01:34:42,650 --> 01:34:44,050
- It's meaningless.
- is pointless.

2377
01:34:44,050 --> 01:34:46,580
- We can give them as many as they want.
- We can always issue more later.

2378
01:34:46,580 --> 01:34:48,950
Let's say the max number is 60.

2379
01:34:48,950 --> 01:34:50,250
How many credits should we get in return?

2380
01:34:50,250 --> 01:34:51,250
- But...
- You're talking like you're not going.

2381
01:34:51,250 --> 01:34:52,960
- I think...
- Let's settle it here.

2382
01:34:52,960 --> 01:34:54,420
- That might not work.
- I'm sorry,

2383
01:34:54,420 --> 01:34:56,060
but if that happens...

2384
01:34:56,930 --> 01:34:59,730
I'm struggling...

2385
01:34:59,730 --> 01:35:01,930
to unite everyone's opinion.

2386
01:35:01,930 --> 01:35:04,730
That process is never easy.

2387
01:35:05,030 --> 01:35:07,470
Why do we always run out of time
every time we have a meeting?

2388
01:35:07,470 --> 01:35:09,740
So many people, so many opinions.

2389
01:35:09,740 --> 01:35:11,740
It takes a long time
to reach a conclusion.

2390
01:35:11,740 --> 01:35:13,810
We ended up making Team Red rush us.

2391
01:35:13,810 --> 01:35:15,010
I felt bad for them.

2392
01:35:15,680 --> 01:35:17,080
We can ask for as many diamonds
as possible.

2393
01:35:17,080 --> 01:35:18,080
They're not worth anything.

2394
01:35:18,080 --> 01:35:19,150
- So it doesn't matter.
- It doesn't matter.

2395
01:35:19,150 --> 01:35:20,550
We can go with that.

2396
01:35:20,550 --> 01:35:22,690
- Okay. Let's go.
- Let's go now.

2397
01:35:24,090 --> 01:35:25,090
Let's go.

2398
01:35:28,160 --> 01:35:29,890
- I'm sorry.
- Sorry about that.

2399
01:35:29,890 --> 01:35:30,990
It's okay.

2400
01:35:31,330 --> 01:35:33,330
Team Gold didn't come out.

2401
01:35:33,330 --> 01:35:35,860
I told them to hurry up and make a trade.

2402
01:35:35,860 --> 01:35:37,030
They were like, "Just five more minutes."

2403
01:35:37,030 --> 01:35:39,440
I heard them talking inside the building.

2404
01:35:39,440 --> 01:35:40,900
Then it occurred to me,

2405
01:35:40,900 --> 01:35:44,710
"What's taking them so long
when they don't know what we're offering?"

2406
01:35:44,710 --> 01:35:47,780
We were planning to give them
everything we had.

2407
01:35:47,780 --> 01:35:49,280
Once they hear what we have to offer,

2408
01:35:49,280 --> 01:35:51,580
they'll have to come up with a new plan.

2409
01:35:51,580 --> 01:35:53,950
They need to settle
the internal situation first...

2410
01:35:53,950 --> 01:35:56,650
before they deal
with the external situation.

2411
01:35:56,650 --> 01:35:59,390
How can they come up with a good idea
given that situation?

2412
01:35:59,390 --> 01:36:00,760
That's what occurred to me.

2413
01:36:00,760 --> 01:36:04,990
We must all fight for Team Black's doom.

2414
01:36:04,990 --> 01:36:07,360
We believe Team Gold was our only option.

2415
01:36:07,360 --> 01:36:09,670
So we tried to mix our resources
as much as possible...

2416
01:36:09,670 --> 01:36:12,970
as if we're in the same boat.

2417
01:36:13,670 --> 01:36:15,000
I'm okay with everything else.

2418
01:36:15,340 --> 01:36:17,410
I'm okay with the fact
that they're siding with Team Gold.

2419
01:36:17,840 --> 01:36:19,480
But if they side with Team Gold,

2420
01:36:19,480 --> 01:36:22,440
they might backstab us.

2421
01:36:22,440 --> 01:36:25,080
Because Team Gold can issue
without a limit.

2422
01:36:25,080 --> 01:36:28,150
What I'm saying is,
can you trust Team Gold on that?

2423
01:36:28,150 --> 01:36:30,020
That's their nature.

2424
01:36:31,090 --> 01:36:33,760
I think I should talk to Team Gold too.

2425
01:36:34,560 --> 01:36:37,360
- We need time to talk about it.
- Yes, that's true.

2426
01:36:37,360 --> 01:36:40,300
- First, we...
- There are too many people on the team.

2427
01:36:40,300 --> 01:36:41,730
- We...
- There's no time to discuss.

2428
01:36:41,730 --> 01:36:44,670
If war had been declared,
we couldn't have made the trade.

2429
01:36:44,670 --> 01:36:47,770
Team Blue might be
making a move right now.

2430
01:36:47,770 --> 01:36:50,140
If any of Team Black's spies
had started war,

2431
01:36:50,140 --> 01:36:51,370
we couldn't have made a trade.

2432
01:36:51,370 --> 01:36:52,780
You should've been here already.

2433
01:36:53,310 --> 01:36:55,340
We need to seize the Community Center.

2434
01:37:02,650 --> 01:37:03,750
- I'm sorry.
- No.

2435
01:37:03,750 --> 01:37:04,820
I'm sorry.

2436
01:37:04,820 --> 01:37:07,160
- We were making a decision together.
- I'm sorry.

2437
01:37:07,490 --> 01:37:08,620
First of all,

2438
01:37:08,960 --> 01:37:10,830
there was a spy in my team.

2439
01:37:11,160 --> 01:37:12,590
His name was Donkey.

2440
01:37:13,000 --> 01:37:15,100
I can't keep a spy alive.

2441
01:37:15,100 --> 01:37:16,900
- It's too risky for us.
- True.

2442
01:37:16,900 --> 01:37:19,300
So Donkey's going to die today.

2443
01:37:21,200 --> 01:37:23,170
We have to keep one in our team.

2444
01:37:23,170 --> 01:37:25,640
But while Donkey was working as a spy,

2445
01:37:25,640 --> 01:37:28,180
he found out the values code
of Izaha and me...

2446
01:37:28,180 --> 01:37:29,910
and handed them over to Team Black.

2447
01:37:29,910 --> 01:37:31,950
So if he comes after us personally,

2448
01:37:31,950 --> 01:37:33,880
we could die anytime.

2449
01:37:34,450 --> 01:37:38,050
You may accept me onto your team.

2450
01:37:38,050 --> 01:37:40,590
But if that's impossible,
I'm going to die today.

2451
01:37:41,620 --> 01:37:43,690
I'm going to keep Izaha in Team Red.

2452
01:37:44,090 --> 01:37:46,060
The reason we invited you here today is,

2453
01:37:46,060 --> 01:37:50,170
we're giving you
all the resources we have.

2454
01:37:52,570 --> 01:37:54,670
If you accept my relocation request
tomorrow,

2455
01:37:54,670 --> 01:37:56,140
I plan to play on Team Gold.

2456
01:37:56,140 --> 01:37:57,470
The reason I'm relocating is,

2457
01:37:57,470 --> 01:37:59,880
Izaha must remain alone in Team Red
to avoid consuming lives,

2458
01:37:59,880 --> 01:38:02,950
and at the same time,
even if he's attacked,

2459
01:38:02,950 --> 01:38:04,710
he's unlikely to die.

2460
01:38:04,710 --> 01:38:06,450
No. We have to discuss...

2461
01:38:06,450 --> 01:38:09,020
whether to accept you...

2462
01:38:09,020 --> 01:38:10,750
- That's your call.
- or not.

2463
01:38:10,750 --> 01:38:12,520
- To play safe...
- That's your call.

2464
01:38:12,520 --> 01:38:14,790
If you don't accept me,
I'm going to die tomorrow.

2465
01:38:14,790 --> 01:38:16,020
- Only then...
- That's not necessary.

2466
01:38:16,020 --> 01:38:17,360
Yes, it is necessary.

2467
01:38:17,360 --> 01:38:19,090
If you don't accept me, I must die.

2468
01:38:19,090 --> 01:38:21,960
So Izaha can survive in Team Red.

2469
01:38:24,130 --> 01:38:26,400
Then let's give them lives tomorrow.

2470
01:38:26,400 --> 01:38:27,800
We don't need lives.

2471
01:38:27,800 --> 01:38:30,940
The only reason we're giving them lives
is that Maillard is switching teams.

2472
01:38:30,940 --> 01:38:32,240
- That's right.
- So let's hold off on that.

2473
01:38:32,240 --> 01:38:33,540
- We'll decide tomorrow.
- Yes, tomorrow.

2474
01:38:33,540 --> 01:38:35,280
- We don't need them.
- We'll decide on the lives tomorrow.

2475
01:38:35,380 --> 01:38:36,950
Let's trade diamonds for credits, then.

2476
01:38:36,950 --> 01:38:39,510
We'll trade diamonds for gold.

2477
01:38:39,750 --> 01:38:40,780
How much...

2478
01:38:40,780 --> 01:38:42,520
How much are you thinking per person?

2479
01:38:42,520 --> 01:38:44,250
- If you're dividing it, I mean.
- We thought...

2480
01:38:44,250 --> 01:38:45,720
each member could get 15,

2481
01:38:45,720 --> 01:38:48,720
but now that
Donkey won't survive the night,

2482
01:38:48,720 --> 01:38:50,730
we can offer 30.

2483
01:38:54,230 --> 01:38:56,670
You'll have 30 on hand...

2484
01:38:56,670 --> 01:38:59,740
and help us make this the new currency.

2485
01:39:01,570 --> 01:39:02,800
We can offer 40.

2486
01:39:03,310 --> 01:39:05,210
It's not like I want a lot,

2487
01:39:05,440 --> 01:39:07,210
but you can give us...

2488
01:39:07,210 --> 01:39:08,910
around 50 for now,

2489
01:39:08,910 --> 01:39:10,580
and reevaluate its value...

2490
01:39:10,580 --> 01:39:11,980
- by issuing more if necessary.
- Sure.

2491
01:39:11,980 --> 01:39:13,220
The amount...

2492
01:39:13,220 --> 01:39:14,320
- is practically irrelevant for now.
- Fifty, then?

2493
01:39:14,320 --> 01:39:16,390
- Yes, 50.
- We'll agree to that.

2494
01:39:16,390 --> 01:39:18,120
You'll trade with 50 gold?

2495
01:39:18,120 --> 01:39:19,520
Yes, I'll trade with 50 gold,

2496
01:39:19,520 --> 01:39:20,990
but I'll split that in two.

2497
01:39:20,990 --> 01:39:23,030
You'll swap once for diamonds,

2498
01:39:23,030 --> 01:39:24,930
- and once for credits.
- Then credits.

2499
01:39:24,930 --> 01:39:27,030
- Got it.
- We'll need two transactions.

2500
01:39:27,030 --> 01:39:29,160
Sure. Leaders, off you go.

2501
01:39:29,160 --> 01:39:30,530
(Team Red's Resources:
298 diamonds, 9 lives, 30 credits)

2502
01:39:30,530 --> 01:39:31,900
(Team Red's Resources:
298 diamonds, 9 lives, 29 credits)

2503
01:39:32,670 --> 01:39:34,940
The Trading Station has been activated.

2504
01:39:40,140 --> 01:39:41,980
(Trade: 10 credits for 25 gold)

2505
01:39:41,980 --> 01:39:44,580
Team Gold's 25 gold...

2506
01:39:44,580 --> 01:39:47,720
was traded for Team Red's ten credits.

2507
01:39:48,150 --> 01:39:50,020
- All right.
- Team Red...

2508
01:39:50,020 --> 01:39:51,250
is now in possession of gold.

2509
01:39:51,250 --> 01:39:53,090
- We'll trade again.
- Sure.

2510
01:39:53,590 --> 01:39:54,990
(Team Red's Resources:
298 diamonds, 9 lives, 19 credits)

2511
01:39:55,290 --> 01:39:57,430
The Trading Station has been activated.

2512
01:39:57,430 --> 01:39:59,330
- Let's trade diamonds for gold.
- Got it.

2513
01:40:00,000 --> 01:40:03,770
(Trade: 198 diamonds for 25 gold)

2514
01:40:03,770 --> 01:40:07,500
(Trade: 198 diamonds for 25 gold)

2515
01:40:07,670 --> 01:40:10,370
Team Gold's 25 gold...

2516
01:40:10,540 --> 01:40:14,840
was traded for Team Red's 198 diamonds.

2517
01:40:15,240 --> 01:40:18,080
The traded amount has been updated
in your inventory.

2518
01:40:23,290 --> 01:40:25,490
None of the offers...

2519
01:40:25,590 --> 01:40:26,820
made any sense.

2520
01:40:26,820 --> 01:40:28,660
I just couldn't understand it.

2521
01:40:28,660 --> 01:40:31,190
Dividing it all evenly...

2522
01:40:31,190 --> 01:40:34,200
so everyone has the same gold?

2523
01:40:34,330 --> 01:40:36,000
How does that benefit any of us?

2524
01:40:36,330 --> 01:40:39,200
If you wanted someone on your team,

2525
01:40:39,330 --> 01:40:42,640
you should've at least tried to bargain
by saying they'd get more.

2526
01:40:42,840 --> 01:40:44,940
I just think that's Negotiation 101.

2527
01:40:45,140 --> 01:40:47,810
I brought all the resources our team had
to the table,

2528
01:40:47,980 --> 01:40:51,580
but they don't even realize their value.

2529
01:40:51,880 --> 01:40:54,650
They have no concept
of the weight and value...

2530
01:40:54,650 --> 01:40:57,950
that 300 diamonds hold in our community.

2531
01:40:58,220 --> 01:41:01,290
On top of that, when I said I wanted...

2532
01:41:01,290 --> 01:41:03,030
to switch over to Team Gold,

2533
01:41:03,160 --> 01:41:05,290
they said they couldn't give me
an answer right away...

2534
01:41:05,290 --> 01:41:07,160
and had to discuss it first.

2535
01:41:07,400 --> 01:41:08,660
They told me to stay put.

2536
01:41:08,660 --> 01:41:11,230
When I said I'd just leave
if they wouldn't take me,

2537
01:41:11,230 --> 01:41:12,970
they told me
that wasn't what they wanted either.

2538
01:41:12,970 --> 01:41:14,770
Hearing that made me realize...

2539
01:41:14,770 --> 01:41:16,840
all their talk and strategy
was just armchair theory.

2540
01:41:16,940 --> 01:41:18,770
They were way too naive about the game,

2541
01:41:18,770 --> 01:41:20,840
and I just couldn't wrap my head
around it.

2542
01:41:20,940 --> 01:41:22,940
I have some reservations about Reboot.

2543
01:41:22,940 --> 01:41:23,950
I see.

2544
01:41:23,950 --> 01:41:27,050
I kept saying Ugong was a spy
and that we had a spy among us,

2545
01:41:27,050 --> 01:41:29,620
- but Reboot kept shutting me down.
- Right.

2546
01:41:29,750 --> 01:41:32,020
- We need to swap leaders.
- You should tomorrow.

2547
01:41:32,020 --> 01:41:34,160
- Let's pick a different leader tomorrow.
- Sure.

2548
01:41:34,160 --> 01:41:35,790
He won't do anything before that, right?

2549
01:41:36,160 --> 01:41:37,530
Don't be obvious about it.

2550
01:41:37,530 --> 01:41:38,830
- Let's not do that.
- He can't know.

2551
01:41:38,830 --> 01:41:41,100
If someone's being eliminated,
it'll be me.

2552
01:41:41,100 --> 01:41:42,830
I'm the one who's been mentioning a spy.

2553
01:41:44,630 --> 01:41:45,870
The trade is done.

2554
01:41:45,870 --> 01:41:47,440
Thank you. Good job, guys.

2555
01:41:47,440 --> 01:41:49,640
Thank you for that. Goodness.

2556
01:41:51,310 --> 01:41:53,110
What trade is Team Blue looking for?

2557
01:41:53,840 --> 01:41:55,810
I won't know until we talk.

2558
01:41:55,810 --> 01:41:57,910
I have no idea what's going on right now.

2559
01:41:59,350 --> 01:42:01,550
I've already told you
I'm following Red's lead.

2560
01:42:02,150 --> 01:42:04,250
If I'm being honest,

2561
01:42:04,250 --> 01:42:06,120
Team Gold still scares me.

2562
01:42:06,120 --> 01:42:07,420
- That's understandable.
- Team Gold...

2563
01:42:07,420 --> 01:42:09,190
has unlimited issuance rights.

2564
01:42:10,130 --> 01:42:12,760
- They won't issue any after the voting.
- Let's head up for now.

2565
01:42:12,760 --> 01:42:14,760
- Thanks for today.
- Thanks.

2566
01:42:15,430 --> 01:42:16,870
- Don't cast your vote, then.
- Right.

2567
01:42:17,030 --> 01:42:19,430
Gold will be nullified,
and diamonds will become...

2568
01:42:19,430 --> 01:42:21,770
- the main currency.
- Are you still holding on to diamonds?

2569
01:42:21,770 --> 01:42:23,470
- A little, yes.
- Right.

2570
01:42:25,810 --> 01:42:28,310
They already went up
when I needed to trade.

2571
01:42:28,380 --> 01:42:29,740
- Trade what?
- Gold?

2572
01:42:31,280 --> 01:42:32,450
Team Gold's leader!

2573
01:42:33,250 --> 01:42:35,680
- Can we talk?
- Team Blue wants to trade.

2574
01:42:35,980 --> 01:42:37,290
- With us?
- Yes.

2575
01:42:37,290 --> 01:42:38,320
Trade what?

2576
01:42:38,650 --> 01:42:40,760
I can't help it
if you don't need what I have.

2577
01:42:40,760 --> 01:42:42,520
I think we'll be fine.

2578
01:42:42,520 --> 01:42:44,460
We can't make any more deals...

2579
01:42:44,460 --> 01:42:45,590
- because that's all we brought.
- Right.

2580
01:42:45,590 --> 01:42:47,030
- We got it for now.
- Sure.

2581
01:42:47,400 --> 01:42:49,430
There's no need to give her any gold.

2582
01:42:49,430 --> 01:42:51,070
She suddenly wants gold, right?

2583
01:42:51,070 --> 01:42:52,570
Yes, but we don't need to trade with her.

2584
01:42:52,700 --> 01:42:54,400
- We got it for now.
- What did you want to trade?

2585
01:42:55,940 --> 01:42:57,140
- Lives?
- I don't need lives to survive.

2586
01:42:57,140 --> 01:43:00,580
She's offering lives,
which I think is a good deal.

2587
01:43:01,240 --> 01:43:03,580
I think we're good for now.

2588
01:43:03,580 --> 01:43:05,250
- You are?
- Got it, then.

2589
01:43:06,980 --> 01:43:08,650
I can't be bothered to go back down there.

2590
01:43:09,890 --> 01:43:12,390
Team Blue has finally come to her senses.

2591
01:43:12,550 --> 01:43:13,920
They're set with lives for now.

2592
01:43:13,920 --> 01:43:16,290
I guess they have enough.
It didn't sound like they were bluffing.

2593
01:43:16,790 --> 01:43:18,360
- They might not need any more.
- Right.

2594
01:43:18,830 --> 01:43:20,560
- What about me, then?
- What do you mean?

2595
01:43:21,130 --> 01:43:25,330
They're only acting this way
because they don't trust you enough...

2596
01:43:25,330 --> 01:43:27,900
to accept you just yet.

2597
01:43:27,900 --> 01:43:31,640
By the looks of it, Team Gold is on edge
and suspicious of everyone.

2598
01:43:32,110 --> 01:43:33,540
They even doubt one another.

2599
01:43:34,280 --> 01:43:35,380
See how it goes for now.

2600
01:43:35,840 --> 01:43:37,950
Then there's nothing I can do.

2601
01:43:38,210 --> 01:43:40,650
Don't say that.
Just hang in there for a bit.

2602
01:43:42,680 --> 01:43:44,820
Good job, guys.
We completed our first trade.

2603
01:43:44,820 --> 01:43:45,920
We're in business now.

2604
01:43:45,920 --> 01:43:47,990
I'd like a debrief. What happened?

2605
01:43:47,990 --> 01:43:49,820
Donkey was outed as a spy,

2606
01:43:49,820 --> 01:43:53,660
and Maillard says
he's willing to be eliminated,

2607
01:43:53,660 --> 01:43:55,100
but we're going to talk him out of it.

2608
01:43:55,960 --> 01:43:59,270
Team Blue suddenly wanted
to trade with us, but we declined.

2609
01:44:00,340 --> 01:44:01,740
We should stick to our principles.

2610
01:44:01,740 --> 01:44:03,570
- That's right.
- We gave her a chance yesterday.

2611
01:44:04,010 --> 01:44:06,140
Could she do something crazy...

2612
01:44:06,140 --> 01:44:07,240
just because we turned her down?

2613
01:44:07,240 --> 01:44:10,310
If she starts a war, we can react to that.

2614
01:44:10,650 --> 01:44:12,350
She wants gold,

2615
01:44:12,680 --> 01:44:14,550
but Team Blue has nothing we want.

2616
01:44:14,620 --> 01:44:16,120
There's no need
to throw our resources away.

2617
01:44:16,120 --> 01:44:17,590
If she had agreed yesterday,

2618
01:44:17,590 --> 01:44:19,050
- she'd have gotten a good deal.
- Right.

2619
01:44:19,050 --> 01:44:20,960
- Always sell at the top, right?
- She missed her chance.

2620
01:44:21,720 --> 01:44:24,260
We're not doubting each other, right?

2621
01:44:24,590 --> 01:44:26,490
I hope there isn't any doubt.

2622
01:44:26,630 --> 01:44:29,430
Unless there's definitive proof...

2623
01:44:29,430 --> 01:44:31,130
Does anyone know where Ugong is?

2624
01:44:31,130 --> 01:44:32,300
His shoes are gone.

2625
01:44:32,300 --> 01:44:35,100
- Where did he go in the rain?
- That's why I think he went somewhere.

2626
01:44:35,100 --> 01:44:36,970
At times like this,
your suspicion is justified.

2627
01:44:36,970 --> 01:44:39,570
- This is understandable.
- There have been multiple occasions.

2628
01:44:39,570 --> 01:44:41,110
I'm not on that same level yet.

2629
01:44:41,810 --> 01:44:43,480
There's no harm in being on alert.

2630
01:44:43,480 --> 01:44:44,650
That's all.

2631
01:44:45,510 --> 01:44:48,950
The leader wants to keep
the five original members together.

2632
01:44:48,950 --> 01:44:50,690
I'm concerned...

2633
01:44:50,920 --> 01:44:53,090
- we'll have too many mouths to feed.
- Too many mouths.

2634
01:44:53,090 --> 01:44:55,620
If I had it my way,

2635
01:44:55,620 --> 01:44:58,260
I'd figure out a way
to become the leader...

2636
01:44:58,460 --> 01:44:59,660
and then...

2637
01:45:01,000 --> 01:45:03,200
clean house a bit.

2638
01:45:03,270 --> 01:45:05,470
After I clean house,
I'll accept you as a teammate.

2639
01:45:05,570 --> 01:45:08,040
I think having the ideal head count...

2640
01:45:08,040 --> 01:45:09,540
is the best option for us.

2641
01:45:09,540 --> 01:45:11,510
- I get it for now.
- Please don't tell anyone this.

2642
01:45:11,510 --> 01:45:12,940
- Keep it to yourself.
- I got it.

2643
01:45:12,940 --> 01:45:14,280
- You should go first.
- Right.

2644
01:45:18,780 --> 01:45:20,050
This is tough.

2645
01:45:21,920 --> 01:45:24,750
(Ugong hangs back a little
to stay under the radar.)

2646
01:45:30,560 --> 01:45:33,530
I was already thinking
I'd be leaving today.

2647
01:45:33,530 --> 01:45:35,160
"Donkey, you'll be eliminated today."

2648
01:45:35,160 --> 01:45:39,030
After hearing that,
I knew I was going home,

2649
01:45:39,030 --> 01:45:40,400
but it still felt unfair.

2650
01:45:40,570 --> 01:45:43,310
I thought there'd be room for negotiation,

2651
01:45:43,310 --> 01:45:46,240
and I wanted to talk things through.

2652
01:45:46,340 --> 01:45:49,240
I was willing to lay out
everything I'd done,

2653
01:45:49,410 --> 01:45:50,910
but nobody even asked.

2654
01:45:51,210 --> 01:45:53,150
It weighed heavily on me,
and my mind was screaming.

2655
01:45:54,020 --> 01:45:56,990
What upset me the most was that...

2656
01:45:58,250 --> 01:46:01,620
Over the past five days,
we had fun competing together,

2657
01:46:01,760 --> 01:46:03,660
and Team Red was so strong.

2658
01:46:03,760 --> 01:46:05,730
Everything we'd been through,

2659
01:46:05,730 --> 01:46:08,430
from the wars and battles
to the quizzes...

2660
01:46:08,430 --> 01:46:11,030
and the moments
where our teamwork came through,

2661
01:46:11,030 --> 01:46:12,400
flashed before me.

2662
01:46:12,700 --> 01:46:16,000
On top of that,
the other two always looked out for me.

2663
01:46:16,570 --> 01:46:18,110
I felt guilty lying to them,

2664
01:46:18,510 --> 01:46:21,980
and leaving the compound like this
wasn't how I pictured it at all.

2665
01:46:22,110 --> 01:46:24,810
It was really heartbreaking.

2666
01:46:24,980 --> 01:46:27,280
What a bummer.

2667
01:46:30,920 --> 01:46:32,350
I'm done packing.

2668
01:46:33,590 --> 01:46:35,420
I'm really sorry about everything.

2669
01:46:36,890 --> 01:46:38,660
You played your role.

2670
01:46:43,130 --> 01:46:45,200
- I mean...
- Yes, that's true.

2671
01:46:47,870 --> 01:46:48,870
Good job, guys.

2672
01:46:49,140 --> 01:46:50,570
- You too.
- Right.

2673
01:46:50,570 --> 01:46:52,840
- I had fun.
- Me too. You're right.

2674
01:46:53,580 --> 01:46:55,380
I can't believe you're all leaving.

2675
01:46:55,380 --> 01:46:58,250
I said I'd follow Red's lead,
but you're all leaving me.

2676
01:46:59,410 --> 01:47:02,050
I don't want you guys to leave.

2677
01:47:02,950 --> 01:47:06,490
It's my last request.

2678
01:47:07,690 --> 01:47:10,460
I could leave
after explaining everything I did...

2679
01:47:10,460 --> 01:47:12,560
with complete transparency.

2680
01:47:12,690 --> 01:47:15,430
My goal is for you two
to make it to the end...

2681
01:47:16,830 --> 01:47:18,170
and win the whole thing.

2682
01:47:19,900 --> 01:47:21,870
One of my two main goals...

2683
01:47:23,610 --> 01:47:26,010
was to lead Team Red to victory.

2684
01:47:42,060 --> 01:47:43,190
Team Red should prevail.

2685
01:47:43,190 --> 01:47:44,390
- You should.
- Right.

2686
01:47:46,160 --> 01:47:47,160
I know.

2687
01:47:47,400 --> 01:47:49,030
You did the best you could.

2688
01:47:49,030 --> 01:47:50,170
Exactly. You did great.

2689
01:47:54,770 --> 01:47:55,800
Come on.

2690
01:47:56,470 --> 01:48:00,280
I totally get why you did like that.

2691
01:48:00,280 --> 01:48:01,880
Right, of course.

2692
01:48:03,380 --> 01:48:04,410
I know.

2693
01:48:14,160 --> 01:48:16,360
- I talked to Team Gold and...
- Yes?

2694
01:48:16,360 --> 01:48:17,360
They're so...

2695
01:48:18,560 --> 01:48:20,160
- What about Team Gold?
- What a bunch of boomers.

2696
01:48:20,160 --> 01:48:21,200
Right.

2697
01:48:21,730 --> 01:48:22,860
They're not easy to deal with.

2698
01:48:23,730 --> 01:48:26,330
The decision-making is complicated
as there are a lot of people.

2699
01:48:26,330 --> 01:48:27,640
It's really complicated with Team Gold.

2700
01:48:30,740 --> 01:48:31,940
Will Team Black make a profit...

2701
01:48:31,940 --> 01:48:33,740
if Team White wins?

2702
01:48:34,740 --> 01:48:35,910
I'm not sure about that.

2703
01:48:35,910 --> 01:48:38,110
But what's certain
about the information we have...

2704
01:48:38,110 --> 01:48:41,520
is that it's a disadvantage to Team Black
if Team Gold wins.

2705
01:48:41,820 --> 01:48:43,150
We can't be sure about that.

2706
01:48:43,150 --> 01:48:44,420
If we think about it,

2707
01:48:44,420 --> 01:48:46,990
leaving diamonds...

2708
01:48:47,190 --> 01:48:48,890
- might be better for us.
- Right.

2709
01:48:48,890 --> 01:48:50,560
- You've left some, right?
- Right.

2710
01:48:50,960 --> 01:48:52,130
- We have 100.
- Right.

2711
01:48:52,130 --> 01:48:53,700
Even if Team Black
doesn't choose diamonds,

2712
01:48:53,700 --> 01:48:56,970
we can have more people
to choose diamonds.

2713
01:48:57,430 --> 01:48:59,100
- Do you get what I'm saying?
- No, I don't.

2714
01:49:00,240 --> 01:49:01,340
So...

2715
01:49:01,700 --> 01:49:05,140
if Team White stays with us
without going to Team Gold,

2716
01:49:05,140 --> 01:49:06,770
even if Donkey leaves,

2717
01:49:06,770 --> 01:49:08,340
there are seven of us...

2718
01:49:08,340 --> 01:49:10,110
- while there are five of them.
- I get that we're bigger in number.

2719
01:49:10,250 --> 01:49:12,680
We'll make it 7 against 5...

2720
01:49:12,680 --> 01:49:14,520
and we'll keep diamonds to our advantage.

2721
01:49:14,520 --> 01:49:15,850
- Team Black doesn't have any anyway.
- Right.

2722
01:49:15,850 --> 01:49:17,390
We won't give away any of our diamonds
through the Platform.

2723
01:49:17,590 --> 01:49:19,020
We won't give any diamonds
through the Platform...

2724
01:49:19,020 --> 01:49:20,390
- and we'll win with our diamonds?
- Right.

2725
01:49:20,390 --> 01:49:22,020
We can do that if we are
to completely abandon Team Black.

2726
01:49:22,020 --> 01:49:24,630
He only has one right now.
That isn't a lot.

2727
01:49:24,630 --> 01:49:26,730
We'll forget about that.
Even if new diamonds get issued,

2728
01:49:26,730 --> 01:49:29,560
we won't use the Platform at all
to prevent him from getting diamonds.

2729
01:49:29,660 --> 01:49:32,200
This is possible
without teaming up with them.

2730
01:49:32,200 --> 01:49:34,000
This is a much safer way for us...

2731
01:49:34,000 --> 01:49:35,640
than working with Team Gold.

2732
01:49:35,640 --> 01:49:37,570
It's because Team Gold
is being too conservative.

2733
01:49:37,570 --> 01:49:38,640
Right.

2734
01:49:40,110 --> 01:49:41,840
- She has a point.
- Right.

2735
01:49:42,080 --> 01:49:45,580
"I want Black dead." If this is the goal,

2736
01:49:45,580 --> 01:49:48,880
- we should consider using that method.
- Right. Okay.

2737
01:49:48,880 --> 01:49:50,790
- We'll...
- Team White is with us as well.

2738
01:49:50,790 --> 01:49:52,850
We'll consider that method as well.

2739
01:49:53,590 --> 01:49:55,460
Team Gold is too conservative.

2740
01:49:55,460 --> 01:49:57,660
The members of Team Gold
might split up between themselves.

2741
01:49:57,960 --> 01:50:00,500
- Let's wait for that.
- I don't want to go to Team Gold.

2742
01:50:00,500 --> 01:50:02,330
- To be honest...
- Right.

2743
01:50:02,330 --> 01:50:04,970
- Well, this might be a personal opinion,
- Right.

2744
01:50:05,430 --> 01:50:08,470
their attitude earlier upset me.

2745
01:50:08,470 --> 01:50:10,440
- Right.
- I waited for them...

2746
01:50:10,440 --> 01:50:12,740
- to talk to them.
- Right. They could've listened.

2747
01:50:12,740 --> 01:50:14,810
They joined yesterday...

2748
01:50:14,810 --> 01:50:16,410
and missed out on a single trade.

2749
01:50:16,410 --> 01:50:18,810
- And they said, "We don't need to."
- Right.

2750
01:50:18,810 --> 01:50:21,180
- That was just... To be honest,
- That was bad.

2751
01:50:21,180 --> 01:50:23,280
if Maillard will continue to survive,

2752
01:50:23,280 --> 01:50:24,750
it's better for him to stay here.

2753
01:50:24,750 --> 01:50:26,550
That will save Team White and me.

2754
01:50:26,550 --> 01:50:28,960
Right. It's possible.

2755
01:50:29,260 --> 01:50:30,660
You must stay alive today.

2756
01:50:30,790 --> 01:50:32,560
Losing one will be critical.

2757
01:50:32,560 --> 01:50:35,460
They're continuing to play the game
with their headcount.

2758
01:50:35,460 --> 01:50:37,900
It can really end up becoming
a 5-on-5 game.

2759
01:50:38,330 --> 01:50:39,430
Right. Okay.

2760
01:50:40,900 --> 01:50:43,470
I'll go and talk with Team White.

2761
01:50:44,340 --> 01:50:46,570
It upset me, to be honest.

2762
01:50:46,770 --> 01:50:47,980
I was waiting for them,

2763
01:50:48,110 --> 01:50:50,510
but they left even after seeing me.

2764
01:50:50,650 --> 01:50:53,150
"We don't need to."
They left after saying that.

2765
01:50:53,310 --> 01:50:56,020
I thought, "They don't want to do anything
with me."

2766
01:50:56,150 --> 01:50:59,990
I suddenly felt a sense of crisis
against my survival...

2767
01:50:59,990 --> 01:51:02,520
as I had to persuade the others
to favor diamonds.

2768
01:51:02,520 --> 01:51:04,560
My head started spinning like crazy.

2769
01:51:04,690 --> 01:51:07,900
That was why I started persuading them...

2770
01:51:07,900 --> 01:51:11,470
about the reason we must favor diamonds
even without Team Black.

2771
01:51:16,470 --> 01:51:18,370
Gosh.

2772
01:51:32,950 --> 01:51:34,390
Is that Team White?

2773
01:51:34,690 --> 01:51:36,060
It's Team Blue.

2774
01:51:36,190 --> 01:51:38,060
There's something urgent
I need to talk about.

2775
01:51:38,060 --> 01:51:39,160
Go ahead.

2776
01:51:39,860 --> 01:51:43,100
I've thought of a way to handle things
on our own.

2777
01:51:43,400 --> 01:51:45,970
If you wish to leave out Team Black,
I'm fine with that.

2778
01:51:46,100 --> 01:51:48,100
It doesn't matter to me.
He can get abandoned.

2779
01:51:48,270 --> 01:51:50,840
We're considering a move to Team Gold...

2780
01:51:50,840 --> 01:51:52,540
because we want to secure prize money.

2781
01:51:52,570 --> 01:51:54,740
But we can keep things as is.

2782
01:51:54,910 --> 01:51:56,110
We can choose diamonds...

2783
01:51:56,110 --> 01:51:58,880
and prevent Team Black from getting any.

2784
01:51:59,050 --> 01:52:00,920
- Team Red will be moving to Team Gold.
- No.

2785
01:52:00,920 --> 01:52:02,920
- I just talked with them.
- Right.

2786
01:52:02,920 --> 01:52:04,250
- Really?
- So you wish to win...

2787
01:52:04,250 --> 01:52:05,350
without Team Gold, right?

2788
01:52:05,350 --> 01:52:08,090
What's good about that is that
the remaining people won't be a threat.

2789
01:52:08,090 --> 01:52:09,090
- Right.
- Right.

2790
01:52:09,090 --> 01:52:11,060
And to be honest, I don't want to share
the prize money with Team Gold.

2791
01:52:11,430 --> 01:52:12,560
- You get what I'm saying, right?
- Yes.

2792
01:52:12,560 --> 01:52:14,760
That was why I ran over...

2793
01:52:14,760 --> 01:52:16,060
to stop you
from making a relocation request.

2794
01:52:16,930 --> 01:52:18,870
I've been told not to doubt him,

2795
01:52:18,870 --> 01:52:20,400
but I think...

2796
01:52:20,900 --> 01:52:23,100
Team Black might be using Ugong as a spy.

2797
01:52:23,170 --> 01:52:25,040
You should look for him. Patrol the area.

2798
01:52:25,170 --> 01:52:26,370
Do that if you feel convinced.

2799
01:52:27,340 --> 01:52:29,610
You two should come back together.

2800
01:52:29,910 --> 01:52:31,350
It's raining a lot.

2801
01:52:36,120 --> 01:52:37,890
- Mokgye is coming.
- Here?

2802
01:52:38,820 --> 01:52:41,090
It's fine until here.

2803
01:52:42,360 --> 01:52:44,730
Are things okay for you?

2804
01:52:44,730 --> 01:52:47,500
You said you were going to discuss
with your group...

2805
01:52:47,500 --> 01:52:49,460
- about what I mentioned earlier.
- Right.

2806
01:52:49,560 --> 01:52:51,670
I don't think we will be able
to accept the relocation request.

2807
01:52:51,670 --> 01:52:53,470
The members of Team Red...

2808
01:52:53,670 --> 01:52:55,770
- wish to come to our team as well.
- Right.

2809
01:52:55,770 --> 01:52:59,070
They've been actively giving us
a lot of their resources...

2810
01:52:59,270 --> 01:53:00,580
and wooing us.

2811
01:53:00,580 --> 01:53:03,380
Can the members of Team Gold
be moved to different teams?

2812
01:53:03,380 --> 01:53:06,450
We're against doing that.

2813
01:53:06,450 --> 01:53:09,220
- It'll be hard to split the five?
- Right.

2814
01:53:09,220 --> 01:53:10,490
That will be hard to do...

2815
01:53:10,490 --> 01:53:12,790
- even if gold becomes the main currency?
- We're expecting gold...

2816
01:53:12,790 --> 01:53:14,460
- to become the main currency.
- Right.

2817
01:53:14,460 --> 01:53:17,390
- So...
- We'll have to sacrifice a lot...

2818
01:53:17,390 --> 01:53:18,890
including the things we've done
until this point.

2819
01:53:18,890 --> 01:53:20,930
We have to consider the sacrifices made...

2820
01:53:20,930 --> 01:53:22,360
- by the members of Team White.
- Right.

2821
01:53:22,360 --> 01:53:24,030
To be honest,

2822
01:53:24,030 --> 01:53:26,870
I believe that is something
beyond our realm.

2823
01:53:26,870 --> 01:53:28,870
- Why is that?
- It's a decision that should be made...

2824
01:53:28,870 --> 01:53:30,510
by the members of Team White.

2825
01:53:30,510 --> 01:53:32,340
It's beyond our realm
of what decision should be made.

2826
01:53:32,340 --> 01:53:34,010
You have to confirm things
for us to make a move.

2827
01:53:34,010 --> 01:53:36,380
No. We're just responding
to the situation.

2828
01:53:36,380 --> 01:53:38,110
- I don't think it's right for us...
- There's no reason for that?

2829
01:53:38,110 --> 01:53:39,480
to tell you what to do.

2830
01:53:39,480 --> 01:53:40,820
- Okay.
- Okay.

2831
01:53:40,820 --> 01:53:41,880
Thank you.

2832
01:53:46,020 --> 01:53:47,620
- What?
- It turned out better for us.

2833
01:53:47,620 --> 01:53:49,290
- What?
- It turned out better for us.

2834
01:53:49,560 --> 01:53:51,030
- Right.
- It turned out better for us.

2835
01:53:51,030 --> 01:53:52,630
It's better for us to know their stance.

2836
01:53:52,760 --> 01:53:54,800
If we go to them, we'll get tossed out
after being used by them.

2837
01:53:54,800 --> 01:53:56,000
- Right.
- Okay.

2838
01:53:56,000 --> 01:53:57,170
Thank you for sharing your opinion.

2839
01:53:57,170 --> 01:53:59,430
We'll sort out our thoughts
and meet up with Team Red.

2840
01:53:59,430 --> 01:54:01,970
I wish for all of us to meet again.

2841
01:54:01,970 --> 01:54:03,810
- Let's meet before dinner.
- Okay. Let's do that.

2842
01:54:03,810 --> 01:54:04,910
Dinner is coming soon.

2843
01:54:04,910 --> 01:54:06,210
- Right.
- Let's meet after a break.

2844
01:54:06,540 --> 01:54:08,180
Return safely. It's slippery.

2845
01:54:08,180 --> 01:54:09,210
Okay.

2846
01:54:10,550 --> 01:54:13,920
If we move to Team Gold
to prevent going to war,

2847
01:54:13,920 --> 01:54:16,220
we'll be the ones taking the risk.

2848
01:54:16,320 --> 01:54:18,990
I mentioned this
as we needed a guarantee as well.

2849
01:54:18,990 --> 01:54:20,490
"Let our members go to Team Gold."

2850
01:54:20,660 --> 01:54:22,220
"If you won't accept our members,"

2851
01:54:22,420 --> 01:54:24,590
"move your members to different teams."

2852
01:54:24,590 --> 01:54:27,160
But they refused to do that.

2853
01:54:27,460 --> 01:54:28,460
"What?"

2854
01:54:28,460 --> 01:54:31,300
They're not willing to show
any signs of trust...

2855
01:54:31,300 --> 01:54:32,970
and just want us to trust them.

2856
01:54:33,530 --> 01:54:36,000
An idea popped up in the midst of that.

2857
01:54:41,210 --> 01:54:42,940
It's time for dinner.

2858
01:54:43,340 --> 01:54:47,550
Please gather in the Town Hall for a meal.

2859
01:54:48,420 --> 01:54:50,250
Okay. I should take this with me.

2860
01:54:57,430 --> 01:54:59,530
(The supermarket has disappeared.)

2861
01:55:00,090 --> 01:55:02,100
You have to give me back what was kept.

2862
01:55:06,170 --> 01:55:07,970
- Jae Ho!
- Yes?

2863
01:55:08,700 --> 01:55:11,470
Shouldn't you have kept
the things I bought?

2864
01:55:12,210 --> 01:55:13,310
I got rid of everything.

2865
01:55:15,010 --> 01:55:19,410
(Vector closed the supermarket
during the trade activities.)

2866
01:55:20,880 --> 01:55:24,320
I had no way to find out
who was going to team up with Team Gold.

2867
01:55:24,450 --> 01:55:27,120
As I couldn't distinguish my enemies,

2868
01:55:27,390 --> 01:55:29,260
I suddenly got an idea...

2869
01:55:29,390 --> 01:55:32,030
of closing the market.

2870
01:55:32,360 --> 01:55:35,060
I didn't give food to Team Gold
from the start.

2871
01:55:35,230 --> 01:55:39,330
It's some sort of message
thrown at the diamond teams.

2872
01:55:40,230 --> 01:55:41,770
"If you leave me out like this,"

2873
01:55:41,770 --> 01:55:44,940
"I won't open the supermarket
for three days."

2874
01:55:45,570 --> 01:55:48,840
I did everything I could...

2875
01:55:49,680 --> 01:55:51,410
to send out this message.

2876
01:55:51,810 --> 01:55:53,380
I bought it with my money.

2877
01:55:53,380 --> 01:55:55,580
Isn't that too harsh?

2878
01:55:55,650 --> 01:55:56,820
You had it earlier.

2879
01:55:56,950 --> 01:55:58,550
I didn't finish all of it.

2880
01:56:01,290 --> 01:56:02,790
If I knew this was going to happen,

2881
01:56:02,790 --> 01:56:04,230
I should've brought the food with me
like the others.

2882
01:56:04,490 --> 01:56:05,590
That's harsh.

2883
01:56:17,370 --> 01:56:19,640
As long as someone won't get killed
by the code,

2884
01:56:20,310 --> 01:56:22,010
it's better for him to stay alive.

2885
01:56:23,980 --> 01:56:26,610
How much have you talked about it?

2886
01:56:26,610 --> 01:56:28,820
I've thought of the best method possible.

2887
01:56:28,950 --> 01:56:30,650
Must Donkey be killed?

2888
01:56:30,820 --> 01:56:33,650
I believe it's better for us...

2889
01:56:33,850 --> 01:56:36,020
- to have a bigger number.
- Right.

2890
01:56:36,020 --> 01:56:38,860
One or two might die
through any kind of mission.

2891
01:56:38,860 --> 01:56:40,130
If that happens,

2892
01:56:40,130 --> 01:56:41,160
each person can win...

2893
01:56:41,160 --> 01:56:42,230
- around 10,000 dollars.
- Right.

2894
01:56:42,230 --> 01:56:45,970
Today, you must provide aid
as much as possible...

2895
01:56:45,970 --> 01:56:48,470
- with the credits you have.
- We'll provide aid.

2896
01:56:48,540 --> 01:56:49,700
To produce a lot tomorrow,

2897
01:56:49,700 --> 01:56:51,710
- a relocation is essential.
- Right.

2898
01:56:51,710 --> 01:56:54,080
- Two from them must come to us.
- Okay. We'll provide aid today...

2899
01:56:54,080 --> 01:56:55,640
and go through a relocation
before production starts tomorrow.

2900
01:56:55,810 --> 01:56:56,810
- Sounds good, right?
- Right.

2901
01:56:56,810 --> 01:56:59,050
There's no food as the Platform is closed.
Do you have food?

2902
01:56:59,180 --> 01:57:01,250
- The Platform is closed?
- The fridge has disappeared.

2903
01:57:01,250 --> 01:57:02,720
- He said he threw out everything.
- We can't go in?

2904
01:57:02,880 --> 01:57:05,790
I went to have my leftover bagels
and dumplings.

2905
01:57:05,890 --> 01:57:07,290
- He got rid of the fridge.
- He got rid of the fridge.

2906
01:57:07,290 --> 01:57:09,090
- The fridge is missing.
- He won't give us the food we bought.

2907
01:57:10,660 --> 01:57:11,990
- Don't get mad.
- Right.

2908
01:57:11,990 --> 01:57:13,190
It's fine.

2909
01:57:13,190 --> 01:57:14,560
Anyway,

2910
01:57:14,560 --> 01:57:17,870
we will surely win if we move together.

2911
01:57:17,870 --> 01:57:19,570
Right. We had that in mind.

2912
01:57:19,570 --> 01:57:21,570
We should keep Donkey alive.

2913
01:57:22,000 --> 01:57:23,240
If two get killed,

2914
01:57:23,240 --> 01:57:25,010
we lose our advantage in number.

2915
01:57:25,010 --> 01:57:26,640
This is a game that favors the side
with the larger number.

2916
01:57:27,380 --> 01:57:30,140
Even one more person will benefit us.

2917
01:57:30,140 --> 01:57:31,780
This is why I'm suggesting this method.

2918
01:57:31,780 --> 01:57:33,110
Okay. Understood.

2919
01:57:33,780 --> 01:57:35,020
This is where we're at right now.

2920
01:57:36,650 --> 01:57:38,220
He got rid of the fridge.

2921
01:57:38,690 --> 01:57:39,750
Gosh.

2922
01:57:40,250 --> 01:57:41,620
Is he trying to start a fight?

2923
01:57:42,160 --> 01:57:44,760
I don't usually get mad over things,

2924
01:57:44,760 --> 01:57:47,900
but I get mad
when food is treated like that.

2925
01:57:47,900 --> 01:57:49,400
It upset me a lot.

2926
01:57:49,400 --> 01:57:51,070
Beyond the game,

2927
01:57:51,070 --> 01:57:54,500
I thought it was a thoughtless act...

2928
01:57:54,500 --> 01:57:56,440
that went against human nature.

2929
01:57:56,440 --> 01:57:58,110
That was what made me mad.

2930
01:58:04,710 --> 01:58:07,280
The path to Team White is so tough.

2931
01:58:08,980 --> 01:58:10,220
(Pitou went to Team White's dormitory
right away.)

2932
01:58:10,380 --> 01:58:11,550
Yes.

2933
01:58:11,790 --> 01:58:14,290
- What is it?
- Pitou's here.

2934
01:58:14,290 --> 01:58:15,820
- Pitou's here?
- Yes.

2935
01:58:16,120 --> 01:58:17,490
Is something changing?

2936
01:58:18,160 --> 01:58:19,560
First...

2937
01:58:19,560 --> 01:58:20,730
I think we'll win.

2938
01:58:21,030 --> 01:58:23,500
This is what I'm thinking.

2939
01:58:23,500 --> 01:58:27,440
Bring as many credits over as possible
by providing aid.

2940
01:58:27,440 --> 01:58:28,840
- From Team Red.
- Okay.

2941
01:58:28,840 --> 01:58:31,840
As soon as you wake up tomorrow,
go to the Community Center...

2942
01:58:31,840 --> 01:58:34,440
- and request to relocate.
- Okay.

2943
01:58:34,440 --> 01:58:37,780
We need to get rid
of all of the lives here today.

2944
01:58:37,780 --> 01:58:38,880
- Right.
- Get rid of them,

2945
01:58:38,880 --> 01:58:40,850
then starting tomorrow,
we can provide aid twice.

2946
01:58:40,850 --> 01:58:45,690
During those two times, you need
to transfer diamonds to Team Red and Blue.

2947
01:58:45,690 --> 01:58:47,560
- From here. From Team White.
- From Team White. Right.

2948
01:58:47,560 --> 01:58:49,320
- By issuing diamonds. Sounds good.
- Yes.

2949
01:58:49,320 --> 01:58:50,390
You understand what's going on, right?

2950
01:58:50,390 --> 01:58:51,390
We got it.

2951
01:58:51,760 --> 01:58:57,260
There's a chance to become the majority
with the pro-diamond natives.

2952
01:58:57,260 --> 01:58:58,870
I thought so much...

2953
01:58:58,870 --> 01:59:01,740
about how to make that happen.

2954
01:59:01,740 --> 01:59:04,340
I went all over the place
talking to people.

2955
01:59:04,340 --> 01:59:08,540
The White, Blue, Red alliance
was restored,

2956
01:59:08,540 --> 01:59:12,750
and I think the great alliance
with Gold...

2957
01:59:12,750 --> 01:59:14,650
has been broken.

2958
01:59:16,950 --> 01:59:19,890
As long as we have Team Red on our side,

2959
01:59:19,890 --> 01:59:23,660
I think it's enough to maintain this,

2960
01:59:23,660 --> 01:59:24,930
since we already have seven votes.

2961
01:59:24,930 --> 01:59:28,330
And I don't really want
to take in Team White and Blue.

2962
01:59:28,330 --> 01:59:31,130
We need to decide on this.

2963
01:59:31,130 --> 01:59:32,470
On what to do.

2964
01:59:32,470 --> 01:59:33,900
Will we take relocators?

2965
01:59:34,570 --> 01:59:36,570
Since we said we wouldn't take relocators,

2966
01:59:36,570 --> 01:59:38,810
- let's stop talking about that.
- Right. We've decided...

2967
01:59:38,810 --> 01:59:39,970
- not to take any.
- Even if they want to come,

2968
01:59:39,970 --> 01:59:41,180
I can just deny them.

2969
01:59:41,180 --> 01:59:42,740
- Right.
- We're done with that.

2970
01:59:42,740 --> 01:59:45,480
Team White goes to Team New Blue.

2971
01:59:45,480 --> 01:59:46,850
They remake Team Blue.

2972
01:59:46,850 --> 01:59:49,680
Then there's that team and two
on Team Red.

2973
01:59:49,680 --> 01:59:51,320
Let's make them compete.

2974
01:59:51,320 --> 01:59:53,050
- Right.
- Then we make those two powers...

2975
01:59:53,050 --> 01:59:54,360
come on our side as much as possible.

2976
01:59:54,360 --> 01:59:55,420
What's best for us?

2977
01:59:55,420 --> 01:59:57,560
- If we get nine votes, that's great.
- You're right.

2978
01:59:57,560 --> 02:00:00,660
Even if we don't,
we need to get at least seven votes.

2979
02:00:00,660 --> 02:00:02,560
Then we're good there.

2980
02:00:02,560 --> 02:00:05,430
We won't need to stop
Team White relocating to Team Blue...

2981
02:00:05,430 --> 02:00:07,470
- or reject Team Red.
- You're right.

2982
02:00:07,470 --> 02:00:09,570
We can open up those chances...

2983
02:00:09,570 --> 02:00:12,210
and we can divide things
based on contribution.

2984
02:00:12,210 --> 02:00:13,540
Let's go with that.

2985
02:00:13,540 --> 02:00:15,880
- Got it. Let's do that.
- We need to go eat dinner first.

2986
02:00:15,880 --> 02:00:17,180
Let's go.

2987
02:00:18,110 --> 02:00:20,410
(Town Hall)

2988
02:00:21,450 --> 02:00:22,520
It's all closed.

2989
02:00:22,520 --> 02:00:23,580
(Team Gold finds
the supermarket is closed.)

2990
02:00:31,490 --> 02:00:33,890
I've seen it closed once before.

2991
02:00:33,890 --> 02:00:35,000
So I wasn't surprised,

2992
02:00:35,000 --> 02:00:37,700
but the Team Gold members
were very surprised.

2993
02:00:37,700 --> 02:00:39,830
I think they were a bit upset.

2994
02:00:40,400 --> 02:00:41,670
Is it totally closed?

2995
02:00:41,840 --> 02:00:44,000
I just stopped the supermarket trades
in the morning.

2996
02:00:44,000 --> 02:00:45,210
- You stopped it?
- Yes.

2997
02:00:47,370 --> 02:00:49,980
(Learning the supermarket is closed,
the atmosphere turns cold.)

2998
02:00:50,410 --> 02:00:52,480
Today went so smoothly.

2999
02:00:52,480 --> 02:00:54,080
- It feels like a lucky day.
- Today was...

3000
02:00:54,080 --> 02:00:57,020
Today's lunchtime was the most thrilling.

3001
02:00:57,020 --> 02:00:59,520
I feel like we're having a lucky day.

3002
02:00:59,520 --> 02:01:02,120
- Let's clap.
- But in times like this...

3003
02:01:02,120 --> 02:01:04,360
No, don't clap. Don't you know
the ending of "One Lucky Day?"

3004
02:01:04,560 --> 02:01:05,760
Oh, that's what you're talking about.

3005
02:01:08,900 --> 02:01:10,500
- Hello.
- Hello.

3006
02:01:10,500 --> 02:01:13,070
(Residents have gathered
for the Majority Rules Game.)

3007
02:01:13,770 --> 02:01:15,470
- I am so sad.
- Right.

3008
02:01:16,740 --> 02:01:18,910
(Everyone sees
that the supermarket is closed.)

3009
02:01:19,170 --> 02:01:21,240
That could've been very bad.

3010
02:01:23,910 --> 02:01:24,950
I guess we're starting right away.

3011
02:01:25,710 --> 02:01:29,320
Today's Majority Rules Game
will soon begin.

3012
02:01:30,380 --> 02:01:32,550
The topic
of today's Majority Rules Game is...

3013
02:01:34,120 --> 02:01:37,190
"Honestly, most problems
you encounter in life..."

3014
02:01:37,190 --> 02:01:38,930
"can be solved with money."

3015
02:01:38,930 --> 02:01:40,360
Money is a good topic.

3016
02:01:40,360 --> 02:01:41,360
("Most problems you encounter in life
can be solved with money.")

3017
02:01:41,360 --> 02:01:43,160
Oh, it's Meaning and Practicality today.

3018
02:01:44,330 --> 02:01:47,740
(The majority of residents are
on the Meaning side.)

3019
02:01:49,200 --> 02:01:50,670
It's here.

3020
02:01:51,210 --> 02:01:53,340
We'll probably eat this on the spot.

3021
02:01:55,140 --> 02:01:56,240
Banana, come on.

3022
02:01:56,240 --> 02:01:57,280
(Competition will be fierce today
as the supermarket is closed.)

3023
02:01:57,280 --> 02:01:58,880
Banana.

3024
02:01:59,150 --> 02:02:03,220
Today, I tried to buy someone with money.

3025
02:02:03,220 --> 02:02:04,320
It didn't work.

3026
02:02:04,750 --> 02:02:05,850
I disagree.

3027
02:02:06,390 --> 02:02:08,290
I'm facing many of those problems here.

3028
02:02:09,060 --> 02:02:10,790
I wanted to meet lots of good people,

3029
02:02:11,530 --> 02:02:12,860
but I think my personality
is getting worse.

3030
02:02:13,890 --> 02:02:17,670
So I don't think this can be solved
with money. The end.

3031
02:02:17,670 --> 02:02:19,170
I disagree.

3032
02:02:19,170 --> 02:02:22,400
What I consider most important in life...

3033
02:02:22,400 --> 02:02:24,640
is friendship, peace, and such things.

3034
02:02:24,640 --> 02:02:25,940
When it comes to love,

3035
02:02:25,940 --> 02:02:27,940
there were many more things
that couldn't be solved with money.

3036
02:02:27,940 --> 02:02:30,340
That's why I think...

3037
02:02:30,840 --> 02:02:33,350
I don't think I was that convincing.

3038
02:02:33,580 --> 02:02:35,650
From other people's perspectives,

3039
02:02:35,650 --> 02:02:38,150
I killed my two team members for money.

3040
02:02:38,150 --> 02:02:41,560
I'm thinking, "Do you think
what you said makes sense?"

3041
02:02:41,790 --> 02:02:43,760
But here, that's not important.

3042
02:02:43,760 --> 02:02:45,130
It's important to be in the majority.

3043
02:02:45,130 --> 02:02:47,130
You say things can't be solved with money,

3044
02:02:47,130 --> 02:02:49,100
but people who argue so...

3045
02:02:49,100 --> 02:02:51,100
generally don't have money.

3046
02:02:51,100 --> 02:02:53,070
Actually, money does solve most things.

3047
02:02:53,070 --> 02:02:55,640
Honestly, if we had brought
about 10,000 dollars with us here,

3048
02:02:55,640 --> 02:02:56,840
we could've solved everything.

3049
02:02:57,370 --> 02:02:58,840
All of the problems here.

3050
02:02:59,370 --> 02:03:02,680
I think you're thinking
too easily of people.

3051
02:03:02,680 --> 02:03:04,450
This is what I think.
If you can't solve something with money,

3052
02:03:04,450 --> 02:03:05,680
it's because you don't have enough.

3053
02:03:06,650 --> 02:03:09,220
I think people will do anything
for 100 million, or 1 billion dollars.

3054
02:03:09,920 --> 02:03:13,150
I don't think
people understand the problem.

3055
02:03:13,150 --> 02:03:15,290
Did I say money was the most important
in the world?

3056
02:03:15,290 --> 02:03:16,660
That's not the proposition.

3057
02:03:16,660 --> 02:03:18,130
If you read the proposition,

3058
02:03:18,130 --> 02:03:20,890
it says, "most" and "probably."

3059
02:03:20,890 --> 02:03:24,330
I think people keep skipping over
these key words.

3060
02:03:24,500 --> 02:03:29,040
If you list up most of the problems,

3061
02:03:29,040 --> 02:03:32,370
I think there are more problems...

3062
02:03:32,370 --> 02:03:34,940
that you can solve with money.

3063
02:03:34,940 --> 02:03:39,180
I believe the problems we don't think
can be solved with money...

3064
02:03:39,180 --> 02:03:42,350
are due to special circumstances.

3065
02:03:42,350 --> 02:03:44,950
If we go back to our real lives,

3066
02:03:44,950 --> 02:03:46,490
being honest,

3067
02:03:46,490 --> 02:03:50,690
I think there are many problems
we can solve with money.

3068
02:03:50,690 --> 02:03:52,160
So I agree.

3069
02:03:52,160 --> 02:03:54,130
I got married last year.

3070
02:03:54,130 --> 02:03:57,770
I got married
under very difficult circumstances.

3071
02:03:57,770 --> 02:04:00,370
What I think about every day,

3072
02:04:00,370 --> 02:04:02,540
getting married and starting a family,

3073
02:04:02,540 --> 02:04:04,710
is that the issue of money...

3074
02:04:04,710 --> 02:04:06,440
is so very important.

3075
02:04:06,440 --> 02:04:09,480
I'm so desperately feeling that.

3076
02:04:09,480 --> 02:04:12,650
What I think is generally more important
than money...

3077
02:04:12,650 --> 02:04:14,620
is boundaries.

3078
02:04:14,620 --> 02:04:17,050
We also call boundaries lines.

3079
02:04:17,050 --> 02:04:19,620
I'll tell you about my lines.

3080
02:04:19,620 --> 02:04:23,660
When I see someone doing something
that I can't logically comprehend,

3081
02:04:23,660 --> 02:04:26,660
I think they crossed a boundary,
and I get very angry.

3082
02:04:26,660 --> 02:04:30,300
Just to let you know, I only get angry
a few times a year.

3083
02:04:30,300 --> 02:04:33,670
But when someone doesn't let me eat,
it makes me very angry.

3084
02:04:33,670 --> 02:04:35,140
I'm not showing it,

3085
02:04:35,140 --> 02:04:37,100
but I'm very angry right now.

3086
02:04:37,910 --> 02:04:40,570
When we didn't get to eat last time,

3087
02:04:40,570 --> 02:04:43,180
I know it was from some agreement
among the leaders.

3088
02:04:43,180 --> 02:04:45,050
But I can't accept...

3089
02:04:45,050 --> 02:04:46,950
not getting to eat a second time.

3090
02:04:46,950 --> 02:04:50,250
I'm smiling right now,
but I'm actually so angry...

3091
02:04:50,250 --> 02:04:52,120
that I could break everything in here.

3092
02:04:52,120 --> 02:04:55,620
To be honest, I wanted to express...

3093
02:04:55,620 --> 02:04:57,090
my resentment toward Vector.

3094
02:04:57,090 --> 02:05:00,990
One thing you can't buy with money...

3095
02:05:00,990 --> 02:05:02,630
is Maillard's heart.

3096
02:05:02,630 --> 02:05:04,360
After living here for six days,

3097
02:05:04,360 --> 02:05:06,300
the things important to Maillard...

3098
02:05:06,300 --> 02:05:09,100
are his team and his people.

3099
02:05:09,100 --> 02:05:11,810
If you mess with his people, he barks.

3100
02:05:11,810 --> 02:05:14,010
So once you make Maillard angry,

3101
02:05:14,010 --> 02:05:16,340
you can't solve the issue
with the Maillard I see,

3102
02:05:16,340 --> 02:05:19,450
even if you give him 10 million dollars.

3103
02:05:19,450 --> 02:05:21,720
Like so, I see many people...

3104
02:05:21,720 --> 02:05:24,720
you can't solve issues with
by using money.

3105
02:05:24,720 --> 02:05:27,720
So I will press "Disagree."

3106
02:05:43,540 --> 02:05:46,540
I'm up here to talk to you...

3107
02:05:46,540 --> 02:05:47,940
about my day today.

3108
02:05:50,740 --> 02:05:53,850
When I made the name, Vector,

3109
02:05:53,850 --> 02:05:56,520
I didn't know I'd get this role.

3110
02:05:58,150 --> 02:06:01,360
These past days have been very hard,
to be honest.

3111
02:06:01,360 --> 02:06:04,890
While doing things I need to do
as the weapon dealer,

3112
02:06:04,890 --> 02:06:06,690
I felt such a disparity.

3113
02:06:06,690 --> 02:06:08,460
I'm really sad that I brought on...

3114
02:06:08,460 --> 02:06:10,230
such rage and resentment.

3115
02:06:10,230 --> 02:06:14,070
So I'm feeling very conflicted...

3116
02:06:14,070 --> 02:06:16,200
about what I should do
for the remaining three days.

3117
02:06:17,000 --> 02:06:19,510
Also, I know you must be struggling...

3118
02:06:19,510 --> 02:06:20,840
because food wasn't provided.

3119
02:06:20,840 --> 02:06:24,980
But I want you to know
this was Team Gold's request.

3120
02:06:24,980 --> 02:06:28,020
- Team Gold...
- What?

3121
02:06:32,220 --> 02:06:34,220
We never said such a thing.

3122
02:06:34,220 --> 02:06:39,460
"How about not providing food
to those who conspire..."

3123
02:06:39,460 --> 02:06:42,030
"or interact with Team Gold?"

3124
02:06:42,030 --> 02:06:43,130
That doesn't make sense.

3125
02:06:43,130 --> 02:06:45,400
What are you talking about?
Why are you lying?

3126
02:06:46,170 --> 02:06:48,340
In a way, it was a solemn occasion.

3127
02:06:48,340 --> 02:06:50,840
Did he have to do that there?

3128
02:06:50,840 --> 02:06:52,640
Everything is out in the open already.

3129
02:06:52,640 --> 02:06:54,540
Why? For what?

3130
02:06:55,340 --> 02:06:56,980
I heard there was such a rumor.

3131
02:06:56,980 --> 02:06:58,850
It gave me an idea.

3132
02:07:00,250 --> 02:07:01,520
I'm not comfortable with this.

3133
02:07:02,320 --> 02:07:04,850
- I'm not comfortable at all.
- But please...

3134
02:07:04,850 --> 02:07:07,420
don't shift the blame for your decision...

3135
02:07:07,420 --> 02:07:09,290
onto us using our words.

3136
02:07:09,290 --> 02:07:12,130
- We wanted to eat with everyone,
- Right.

3137
02:07:12,130 --> 02:07:14,730
and we feel so bad for the team members...

3138
02:07:14,730 --> 02:07:17,030
who can't eat because of us.

3139
02:07:17,030 --> 02:07:18,700
- Right.
- Don't shift the blame...

3140
02:07:18,700 --> 02:07:21,100
of your decision onto us.

3141
02:07:21,600 --> 02:07:23,240
And stop lying.

3142
02:07:23,470 --> 02:07:24,810
Don't live like that.

3143
02:07:27,570 --> 02:07:30,540
Although it was a game,
my heart really hurt.

3144
02:07:31,140 --> 02:07:33,510
I don't think I can ever be the villain.

3145
02:07:34,850 --> 02:07:36,720
It was so tough.

3146
02:07:37,020 --> 02:07:38,420
I was at peak stress levels.

3147
02:07:39,290 --> 02:07:41,860
But that's the fate of a villain.

3148
02:07:41,860 --> 02:07:44,730
My goal is to starve Team Gold,

3149
02:07:44,730 --> 02:07:47,090
slowly work up their emotions,

3150
02:07:47,090 --> 02:07:49,160
and negatively affect their performance.

3151
02:07:49,160 --> 02:07:53,800
For the diamond team to win
if a war really does break out,

3152
02:07:53,800 --> 02:07:55,440
Team Gold's war power needs to fall.

3153
02:07:56,240 --> 02:07:59,870
In a way,
getting them emotionally worked up,

3154
02:07:59,870 --> 02:08:01,710
creating some internal friction,

3155
02:08:01,940 --> 02:08:04,310
and weakening their motivation
by starving them were...

3156
02:08:04,410 --> 02:08:06,510
the only thing I could do.

3157
02:08:09,520 --> 02:08:11,180
If you're mistaken...

3158
02:08:11,180 --> 02:08:13,450
I mean, if that's what you think,
I have nothing to say.

3159
02:08:14,050 --> 02:08:15,560
I only say this...

3160
02:08:15,560 --> 02:08:17,460
to tell you that I don't feel good
about this.

3161
02:08:17,460 --> 02:08:18,690
I also...

3162
02:08:19,660 --> 02:08:22,260
wouldn't have done this
if it hadn't been for this game.

3163
02:08:22,260 --> 02:08:24,530
I have a role to play as a merchant,

3164
02:08:24,630 --> 02:08:26,930
and this is my only influence.

3165
02:08:27,970 --> 02:08:29,470
His attitude itself...

3166
02:08:29,470 --> 02:08:32,110
was unpleasant.

3167
02:08:32,140 --> 02:08:33,440
To be honest,

3168
02:08:33,440 --> 02:08:34,840
I was irritated.

3169
02:08:34,840 --> 02:08:36,710
Who would want to play...

3170
02:08:36,810 --> 02:08:38,810
the mafia member in the game of Mafia?

3171
02:08:38,810 --> 02:08:40,410
Obviously, it's for fun.

3172
02:08:40,810 --> 02:08:42,120
But some people...

3173
02:08:42,120 --> 02:08:44,320
find it to be a huge pressure...

3174
02:08:44,320 --> 02:08:46,190
to lie to others.

3175
02:08:46,290 --> 02:08:47,390
But...

3176
02:08:47,390 --> 02:08:49,860
now that it's all out in the open,

3177
02:08:49,860 --> 02:08:53,830
you involved us in your lie,

3178
02:08:53,830 --> 02:08:57,330
although you could open up
about your feelings.

3179
02:08:57,630 --> 02:09:01,270
That triggered something in me.

3180
02:09:02,100 --> 02:09:03,800
Getting back to the topic,

3181
02:09:03,800 --> 02:09:06,440
just like how we can't fix
our relationship with money,

3182
02:09:06,440 --> 02:09:08,410
setting aside the prize,

3183
02:09:08,410 --> 02:09:10,110
there are so many...

3184
02:09:10,110 --> 02:09:13,180
miscellaneous problems,
which mean so much to us now.

3185
02:09:13,350 --> 02:09:14,650
So,

3186
02:09:14,650 --> 02:09:16,220
I will disagree.

3187
02:09:16,220 --> 02:09:18,790
(Meaning, Practicality)

3188
02:09:26,090 --> 02:09:32,400
(Majority Rules Game)

3189
02:09:37,340 --> 02:09:38,440
So,

3190
02:09:38,440 --> 02:09:40,770
I'm out here.

3191
02:09:40,770 --> 02:09:43,180
I'm sure you'll play
the Majority Rules Game on your own.

3192
02:09:43,280 --> 02:09:45,280
I'm here to tell you...

3193
02:09:45,280 --> 02:09:48,520
everything about the role I was given...

3194
02:09:48,520 --> 02:09:51,180
because I'm suspicious of Vector.

3195
02:09:51,490 --> 02:09:53,550
As the game goes on,
I can't help but feel...

3196
02:09:53,550 --> 02:09:54,820
that he's lying to me as well,

3197
02:09:54,820 --> 02:09:55,960
even though I'm his ally.

3198
02:09:55,960 --> 02:09:57,620
So, I'd like to tell you...

3199
02:09:57,620 --> 02:09:59,430
about the role I was assigned.

3200
02:09:59,530 --> 02:10:03,330
First, I joined Team Red as Donkey.

3201
02:10:03,330 --> 02:10:04,870
And there was a rule card.

3202
02:10:04,870 --> 02:10:06,900
Although I'm on Team Red,

3203
02:10:07,230 --> 02:10:09,400
I'm supposed to be Black's ally.

3204
02:10:09,400 --> 02:10:11,670
The ally's role is...

3205
02:10:11,670 --> 02:10:13,340
to start wars...

3206
02:10:13,340 --> 02:10:14,570
and win...

3207
02:10:14,570 --> 02:10:16,740
part of the weapons sales revenue
as a prize in the end.

3208
02:10:16,740 --> 02:10:19,750
My survival is guaranteed...

3209
02:10:19,750 --> 02:10:20,910
because Black loses...

3210
02:10:20,910 --> 02:10:22,850
half of his prize when I'm eliminated.

3211
02:10:22,850 --> 02:10:25,390
Then, Black will have to try and save me.

3212
02:10:25,390 --> 02:10:27,750
Hearing that rule,

3213
02:10:27,850 --> 02:10:30,290
my first thought was,

3214
02:10:30,290 --> 02:10:32,930
"My goal from start to finish is..."

3215
02:10:32,930 --> 02:10:35,130
"to have both Team Red and Black win."

3216
02:10:35,130 --> 02:10:36,700
So, I gave it my all in the games,

3217
02:10:36,700 --> 02:10:38,000
and I enjoyed them.

3218
02:10:39,330 --> 02:10:41,470
Plus, when Black sold...

3219
02:10:41,470 --> 02:10:42,800
the weapons at high prices,

3220
02:10:42,800 --> 02:10:44,070
I was elated.

3221
02:10:44,070 --> 02:10:46,840
"What a great move.
He's certainly clever."

3222
02:10:46,840 --> 02:10:48,070
That was my thought.

3223
02:10:48,070 --> 02:10:51,440
And Izaha was sitting next to me,
actually getting angry.

3224
02:10:51,440 --> 02:10:54,110
I've been in a dilemma the whole time.

3225
02:10:54,110 --> 02:10:55,220
I couldn't decide.

3226
02:10:55,580 --> 02:10:58,050
Then, Team Gold joined,

3227
02:10:58,850 --> 02:11:01,960
and the Wall Code
that we didn't think anyone would solve...

3228
02:11:04,220 --> 02:11:06,290
The Wall Code was...

3229
02:11:06,290 --> 02:11:07,790
solved by Maillard,

3230
02:11:07,790 --> 02:11:10,430
even before he introduced himself.

3231
02:11:10,560 --> 02:11:13,630
I had to stay with the people
who were going to lower my prize...

3232
02:11:13,630 --> 02:11:14,670
and had to keep lying to them.

3233
02:11:14,670 --> 02:11:16,340
I had to keep lying to the person...

3234
02:11:16,340 --> 02:11:17,700
who was angry about losing the prize.

3235
02:11:17,700 --> 02:11:20,070
I walked on eggshells
for six straight days.

3236
02:11:20,070 --> 02:11:21,940
But it was so much fun
when I solved the quizzes with them.

3237
02:11:21,940 --> 02:11:23,180
They were really smart,

3238
02:11:23,180 --> 02:11:24,480
and they were good negotiators.

3239
02:11:24,480 --> 02:11:26,380
But even if I survive until the last day,

3240
02:11:26,380 --> 02:11:29,280
I can't share the prize with them.

3241
02:11:29,280 --> 02:11:31,520
This role just sucks.

3242
02:11:31,790 --> 02:11:33,020
So, I...

3243
02:11:39,090 --> 02:11:42,300
While everyone found out
that he was a spy,

3244
02:11:42,300 --> 02:11:45,670
it all felt complicated...

3245
02:11:45,670 --> 02:11:47,700
(Maillard, cooking YouTuber)

3246
02:11:47,700 --> 02:11:49,040
because he was my teammate.

3247
02:11:49,840 --> 02:11:52,040
There was nothing I could do to help him,

3248
02:11:52,770 --> 02:11:53,910
so...

3249
02:11:55,780 --> 02:11:57,510
It broke my heart.

3250
02:12:01,920 --> 02:12:04,150
It feels like all I do here is...

3251
02:12:04,150 --> 02:12:05,990
acting like a donkey.

3252
02:12:20,970 --> 02:12:22,940
You know, in life,

3253
02:12:24,070 --> 02:12:26,810
I had never had that much money.

3254
02:12:28,780 --> 02:12:30,410
But...

3255
02:12:30,740 --> 02:12:32,880
when I heard about the big prize,

3256
02:12:33,910 --> 02:12:35,080
I decided to come here.

3257
02:12:35,150 --> 02:12:37,350
To make money.

3258
02:12:38,420 --> 02:12:40,720
But then, with this role they gave me,

3259
02:12:40,720 --> 02:12:42,890
no matter how hard I play the games...

3260
02:12:44,190 --> 02:12:45,560
and no matter what I do,

3261
02:12:45,560 --> 02:12:47,760
I can't make any money.

3262
02:12:48,430 --> 02:12:49,760
And it sucks.

3263
02:12:59,910 --> 02:13:02,180
Anyway,

3264
02:13:04,340 --> 02:13:06,610
it's been fun playing with you,

3265
02:13:07,110 --> 02:13:08,210
and it was awesome.

3266
02:13:08,580 --> 02:13:12,090
There seem to be many things
more important than money.

3267
02:13:12,920 --> 02:13:14,620
I will disagree.

3268
02:13:14,620 --> 02:13:16,060
And just in case...

3269
02:13:16,660 --> 02:13:20,360
someone saves me out of pity,

3270
02:13:20,830 --> 02:13:22,860
I'll keep solving the quizzes...

3271
02:13:23,130 --> 02:13:25,570
without any espionage...

3272
02:13:25,900 --> 02:13:27,870
during my time here.

3273
02:13:28,970 --> 02:13:30,100
Good luck, everyone.

3274
02:13:50,390 --> 02:13:55,130
I didn't want us
to hate each other before I left,

3275
02:13:55,130 --> 02:13:57,000
feeling all uncomfortable.

3276
02:13:57,460 --> 02:13:59,530
"If only I hadn't been assigned
to this role..."

3277
02:14:00,500 --> 02:14:02,240
I keep repeating that in my head.

3278
02:14:03,040 --> 02:14:04,200
It just...

3279
02:14:05,140 --> 02:14:06,640
That's why I cried.

3280
02:14:07,670 --> 02:14:10,580
Donkey and I are the same age.

3281
02:14:10,580 --> 02:14:12,710
When I saw him shed those tears,

3282
02:14:12,710 --> 02:14:15,620
I realized how genuine he was about this.

3283
02:14:15,620 --> 02:14:17,120
You can't cry on a survival show...

3284
02:14:17,120 --> 02:14:19,190
unless you're sincere about it.

3285
02:14:19,890 --> 02:14:22,990
I've been a spy before,

3286
